"hadiths[1002]{hadithnumber,text}:"
24049,"(24049) Yahya bin Abi Bukair narrated to us, saying: Zuhair bin Muhammad narrated to us, on the authority of Yazid bin Khusaifi, On the authority of Omar bin Abdullah bin Ka’b, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Othman bin Abi Al-Aas Al-Thaqafi, he said: I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. I was suffering from pain that almost made me weak, so the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to me: Use your right hand. Ali, then say: In the name of God, I seek refuge in God’s glory and power from the evil that I befall, seven times, so I did that, and He healed me. God
(Muslim 67 Ahmad 4/217)"
24050,"(24050) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulayman told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Sulayman bin Amr bin al-Ahwas, On the authority of his mother, Umm Jundub, she said: I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, followed by a woman from Khath’am with a boy with her. He has an affliction, so she said: O Messenger of God, this is my son and the rest of his family, and he has an affliction that does not speak, so he said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Bring me some water. He brought it and he washed his hands with it and rinsed his mouth. Then he gave it to her and said: Give him some of it to drink, and pour some of it over him, and ask God to heal him. So I met the woman and said: If only she would grant me some of it, and she said: It is only for this afflicted person, so I met the woman of the year. So I asked her about the boy? She said: He was healed, and he understood with a mind not like people’s minds.
(Ibn Majah 3532. Tabarani 25)"
24051,"(24051) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Hayya, on the authority of Abd al-Aziz bin Rafi’, On the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Al-Hussein, on the authority of Omar bin Al-Khattab; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Two angels descended, and one sat at my head and the other at my feet, so he said The one at my feet to the one at my head: What's wrong with it? He said: A severe fever. He said: I seek refuge in you. He said: He did not blow, nor did he blow, so he said: In the name of God, I will perform incense for you, and God will heal you. Take it and let it congratulate you. (Tabarani 1093)"
24052,"(24052) Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Amer, who said: Kharijiyah bin al-Salt narrated to me; That his uncle came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and when he returned, he passed by a crazy Bedouin bound in iron, and some of them said: Do you have anything to treat yourself with? Your friend has come back with good health, so I recited the Mother of the Qur’an for three days, twice each day, and he recovered. So they gave me a hundred sheep. When I came, I went to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I informed him. He said: Did you say something other than that? So I said: No. He said: Eat it in the name of God. By my life, whoever eats a telegram is invalid. You have eaten a telegram is right. (Abu Dawud 3893. Ahmad 5/210)"
24053,"(24053) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ja’far bin Iyas, on the authority of Abu Nadrah, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent us thirty riders in a convoy. He said: We camped with a people and asked them about the villages, but they did not... They came to us, he said: Then their master was stung, he said: So they came to us and said: Is there anyone among you who performed ruqyah from a scorpion? He said: I said: Yes, but I will not perform ruqyah until you give us sheep. He said: So they said: We will give you thirty sheep. He said: So we accepted. He said: So I read and he opened the letter seven times. He said: Then he was healed. So we said: Do not rush until you come to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: When we came to him, he said: So I mentioned to him what I had done. He said: Did you not know that it was a ruqyah? Divide the sheep, and strike them with arrows.
(Tirmidhi 2063. Ahmad 3/10)"
24054,"(24054) Abdul Rahim narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Qais bin Abi Hazim, who said: The Messenger of God came May God’s prayers and peace be upon a man, and he said: I cast a spell on so-and-so, and he was mad, so I was given a flock of sheep. I performed a ruqyah based on the Qur’an, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever takes your ruqyah falsely, you have taken a true ruqyah."
24055,"(24055) Ibn Numayr told us, he said: Othman bin Hakim told us, he said: Abdul Rahman bin Abdul Aziz told me, On the authority of Ali bin Murra, he said: I went out with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on a journey, and even when we were on some road we passed. By a woman sitting with her and a young boy of hers, and she said: O Messenger of God, this son of yours is afflicted with calamity, and an affliction has befallen us from him. Is it taken several times a day, I don’t know how many times? He said: Give it to me, so I took it to him, so he put it between him and the middlemen on the journey, then he opened his mouth and blew it out. There are three things in it: In the name of God, I am the servant of God. The enemy of God has been humiliated. Then he handed it to him, then he said: Meet us in the return. This place, so tell us what he did? He said: So we went, then we came back and found her in that place with three sheep. He said: What did your boy do? She said: By the One who sent you with the truth, we did not sense anything from him until the Messenger, so go past these sheep. He said: Get down and take a thigh. One of them was returned, and the rest were returned."
24056,"(24056) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, saying: Israel informed us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Amara bin Abd, on the authority of Ali, he said: There is no ruqyah except that from which Solomon took a covenant."
24057,"(24057) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Urwah ibn Aamir, on the authority of Ubaid ibn Rifa’i al-Zarqi, he said: She said: Names of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Indeed, the evil eye rushes towards Banu Ja`far, so should I protect them from the evil eye? He said: Yes, if something had preceded predestination, the evil eye would have preceded it. (Tirmidhi 2059. Ibn Majah 3510)"
24058,"(24058) Abdul Rahim told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Suleiman bin Yasar; Urwa bin Al-Zubayr informed him that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered the house of Umm Salamah, and behold, a boy The house was complaining, so he asked them about it? They said: We think he has an evil eye. He claimed that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Don’t you protect him from the evil eye?
(Bukhari 5739. Malik 4)"
24059,"(24059) Abdul Rahim narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Najih, on the authority of Abdullah bin Babih A servant of Jubayr bin Mutim, who said: Asma’ bint Umays said: I said: O Messenger of God, the eye is hastening towards Banu Ja’far. So should I seek refuge for them? He said: Yes. If I had said that something precedes predestination, I would have said: Indeed, the evil eye precedes it."
24060,"(24060) Muawiyah bin Hisham narrated to us, saying: Ammar bin Ruzaiq narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Issa, on the authority of Umayyah bin Hind, on the authority of Abdullah bin Aamir bin Rabi’a, on the authority of his father, who said: Sahl bin Hanif and I set out to seek wine. Then we found wine or a teapot, and one of us was ashamed to bathe while someone could see him, so he hid himself from me until he saw If he did that, he took off a cloak of clothing over himself, then he entered the water, and I looked at him and I liked his appearance, so I was struck by it. With a spring, then I caught him while he was in the water, so I called him and he did not answer me, so I went to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. So I told him the news, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Get up. So he came to him, and he rose from his feet, then he entered. Water, and when it came to him, he stroked his chest, then said: O God, remove the heat and cool it, and pour it on, then he said: Get up, so he got up and said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: If any of you sees something that pleases him, or his wealth, or his brother, Let him pray for blessings, for the evil eye is real. (Ahmad 4471 Hakim 215)"
24061,"(24061) Shababā narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Umamah bin Sahl bin Hanif, On the authority of his father; Amer passed by him while he was washing, and he said: I have never seen anything like today, and no hidden skin, so he was so upset that he He became unwell due to the severity of his pain, so he told the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, called for him. Then he became angry with him and said: I killed him. Why should one of you kill his brother? Have you not been blessed? So the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, gave orders for that, and said: Wash him. So he washed and went out with the group.
 Al-Zuhri said: This is one of the types of knowledge. He washed the one who suffered from it. He said: He is brought a cup of water, and he puts his hand into the cup. So he rinses his mouth and rinses it in the cup, washes his face in the cup, then pours it with his left hand on his palm. The right hand, then with his right hand on his left palm, and he inserts his left hand and pours on the elbow of his hand. The right-hander, with his right hand on the elbow of his left hand, then he washes his right foot, then he washes his hand The right-handed man, so he washes his left foot, then his right hand, so he washes the knees, and takes the inside of his garment. Then he pours one pour over his head, and does not leave the cup until it is empty.
(Ahmad 3/486. Ibn Hibban 6106)"
24062,"(24062) Muhammad bin Abdullah narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Aisha; She used to order the person to perform ablution, so he would wash the one who was affected by the eye."
24063,"(24063) Ahmad bin Ishaq narrated to us, saying: Wahib narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The eye is a real thing, and if it is washed, then let it be washed. (Muslim 42. Ibn Hibban 6108)"
24064,"(24064) Abdul Rahim bin Suleiman told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Muhammad bin Yahya; Al-Walid bin Al-Walid bin Al-Mughirah Al-Makhzoumi complained to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about the story of a person he found And he said: When you come to your bed, say: I seek refuge in the perfect words of God from His wrath, His punishment, and the evil of His servants, and from The promptings of the devils, and if they come, then by the One in whose hand is my soul, nothing will harm you until morning. (Tirmidhi 3528. Ahmad 4/57)"
24065,"(24065) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Mus’ab ibn Shayba, on the authority of Yahya ibn Ja’diyah, he said: It was Khalid bin Al-Walid was terrified at night until he went out with his sword. He feared that he might harm someone, so they complained. This was brought to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: Gabriel said to me: Indeed, an evil from among the jinn is plotting against you, so say: I seek refuge With the perfect words of God, which neither the righteous nor the immoral can pass over, because of the evil of what descends from the heavens, and of what ascends therein, and of the evil of He spreads in the earth and what comes out of it, and from the evil of the temptations of night and day, and from the evil of every one who knocks except one who knocks with goodness. Rahman, and Khaled said, so that went away."
24066,"(24066) Abu Asama narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid, who said: Makhul narrated to us; When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered Mecca, the jinn met him with evil and threw evil at him, so Gabriel said: O Muhammad, I seek refuge in these words: So they rebuked him, and he said: I seek refuge in the perfect words of God, which no righteous person can pass over, nor can the immoral person from evil. Of what descends from the heavens, and of what ascends therein, and of the evil of what is spread on the earth and of what emerges from it, and of the evil of the temptations of night and day. And from the evil of every Tariq, except the Tariq who knocks with goodness, O Most Merciful."
24067,"(24067) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Al-Jariri, on the authority of Abu Al-Ala, on the authority of Uthman bin Abi Al-Aas; He came to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and said: O Messenger of God, Satan has come between my prayer and the reading of... He said: That is a devil called a pig, so when you feel it, spit on your left hand three times, and seek refuge in God from Evil
(Muslim 1729. Ahmad 4/216)"
24068,"(24068) Affan narrated to us, he said: Ja’far bin Sulaiman narrated to us, he said: Abu Al-Tayyah narrated to us, he said: A man asked Abdullah bin Khanbash: What did the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, do when the devils attacked him? He said: The devils came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, from the valleys, and descended upon him from the mountains, and they Satan has a torch of fire with which he wants to burn the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he is terrified by it? Jafar said: I think he was late, and Gabriel came and said: O Muhammad, speak. He said: What should I say? He said: Say: I seek refuge in the perfect words of God, which neither the righteous nor the immoral can pass over, from the evil of what He created, and which He progeny and purges, and from the evil of what He created. He descends from the heavens, and from the evil of what He ascends therein, and from the evil of what He scatters on the earth, and from the evil of what emerges from it, and from the evil of temptations. Night and day, and from the evil of every one who knocks except one who knocks with goodness, O Most Merciful. He said: Then the fire of the devils was extinguished, and he defeated them. God
(Ahmad 3/419, Abu Ali 6844)"
24069,"(24069) Abu Osama narrated to us, saying: Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Mujahid, he said: I used to experience a vision of an ogre. And the devils are a affliction and I see imagination, so I asked Ibn Abbas? He said: Tell me what you saw, and do not be distracted by him, for he will be separated from you just as you are separated from him, and do not be a coward. The two black ones. Mujahid said: I saw him, so I leaned on him with a stick until I heard him fall."
24070,"(24070) Zaid told us, he said: Ibn Aoun told us, on the authority of Ibrahim al-Nakha’i, he said: Whenever one of them saw In a dream he disliked, he said: I seek refuge with what God’s angels and messengers have sought refuge with from the evil of what I saw in my dream. Something befalls me from it that I hate in this world and the hereafter."
24071,"(24071) Abdī narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Amr ibn Shu’ayb, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, he said: He said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: If one of you is startled in his sleep, let him say: In the name of God, I seek refuge in the perfect words of God. From His wrath, and from the evil of His punishment, and from the evil of His servants, and from the evil of the devils and what they attend."
24072,"(24072) Muawiyah bin Hisham narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of his brother, on the authority of Abd Al-Rahman bin Abi Layla said: If one of you feels the devil, let him look at the earth and seek refuge in it."
24073,"(24073) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, cauterized Sa’d in his anklet twice. (Abu Dawud 3862 and Ibn Majah 3494)"
24074,"(24074) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Qais bin Abi Hazim, who said: We entered upon Khabbab to return him, and he had He was sick with a stomach ache. (Bukhari 5472 and Tirmidhi 970)"
24075,"(24075) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He was sick of the scorpion, and he was afflicted by the scorpion."
24076,"(24076) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Abjar, on the authority of Sayyar, on the authority of Qais, On the authority of Jarir, he said: Omar swore an oath on me for two days."
24077,"(24077) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Anas; He was suffering from strength."
24078,"(24078) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Hammad ibn Salamah, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, who said: Abu Talhahi’s kawaani, and he was satisfied. From the meeting."
24079,"(24079) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman bin Saad bin Zurara, I heard my uncle Yahya, and what I met a man from among us with something similar, who reported that Saad bin Zurarah was seized with pain in his throat, and it was said to him: slaughter, so the Messenger of God said God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: I will be informed, or I will express my father’s excuse in front of him, so he ironed it with his hand, and he died, and he said The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: It is a bad death for the Jews. They say: So he will not pay for his companion, and I have no power over him nor I have something for myself.
(Ibn Majah 3492, Hakim 214)"
24080,"(24080) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Salim bin Abi Hafsiya, on the authority of Shayban al-Lahham, who said: Ibn al-Hanafiyy’s kawaani In my head."
24081,"(24081) Abdul Salam told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Abi Abdul Rahman; He entered upon him and had cauterized a boy."
24082,"(24082) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ishaq ibn Suwayd, on the authority of Mutarrif ibn Shukhair, who said: Imran ibn Husayn was He forbade ironing, then ironing after that."
24083,"(24083) Zaid bin Harun told us, he said: Imran bin Hudayr told us, on the authority of Abu Majliz, he said: Imran was Ibn Husayn forbade ironing, so he was afflicted with ironing, and after that he started to iron, and he said: I ironed myself. By fire, it did not heal any pain, nor cured any illness."
24084,"(24084) Muhammad bin Abdullah narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: A man was brought to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he was described as “cauterizing.” The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to him: Iron him. Or please him. (Ahmad 1/3901 Tabarani 10)"
24085,"(24085) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Sa’id ibn Hayyan, on the authority of Sayyar Abi Hamza, on the authority of Qays, on the authority of Jarir, he said: Omar swore an oath on me for two days."
24086,"(24086) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Umays, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Saad, on the authority of his father, he said: It was owned by Al-Hasan bin Ali Bakhtiyya, her hump had tilted to her side, so he ordered me to cut it and iron it."
24087,"(24087) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid; Ibn Umar ironed his son while he was in a state of ihram."
24088,"(24088) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: The nations were presented to me, and suddenly there was great darkness, so I said: Is this my nation? It was said: This is Moses and his people. He said: Then it was said to me: Look at the horizon. So I looked and behold, darkness had filled the horizon. It was said: So it was said: This is your nation, and seventy thousand others will enter Paradise without reckoning.
 Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered and did not explain to them, so the people dispersed, and they said: We are the ones who believe in God. And we followed His Messenger, so we are them, or our children who were born into Islam. He said: This was conveyed to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He greeted him and said: They are the ones who do not seek enslavement, do not seek volition, and do not remain hidden, and in their Lord they put their trust.
(Bukhari 6541, Muslim 374)"
24089,"(24089) Ibn Numayr told us, he said: Mujalid told us, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, he said: A man complained to us. He complained severely, so the doctors said: He will not be cured except by cauterization. So his family wanted to cauterize him, but some of them said: No. Until we consulted the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. So they consulted him, and he said: No, so the man was healed. When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw him. May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: Is this the companion of the son of so-and-so? They said: Yes, then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Indeed, he was cauterized. The people said: The cauterist only made him well."
24090,"(24090) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Hassan bin Abi Wajaza, he said: He narrated to me. Aqar, on the authority of his father, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace; He said: He who is enslaved and concealed does not trust in him.
(Tirmidhi 2055, Ahmad 4/251)"
24091,"(24091) Al-Hasan bin Musa narrated to us, he said: Shayban narrated to us, on the authority of his followers, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Imran bin Husayn, on the authority of Ibn Masoud: He said: We spoke with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, one night, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: And peace be upon him: Seventy thousand will enter Paradise with no reckoning upon them: those who will not be enslaved, nor will they be enslaved, nor will they seek refuge. And in their Lord they trust. (Bukhari 911. Tabarani 9769)"
24092,"(24092) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Imran bin Hudayr, on the authority of Abu Majliz, who said: Whoever has his body covered in the fire of a quarrel In it is Satan."
24093,"(24093) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Amr, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, who said: A self took hold of me. Junub during the time of Omar. A man from the Arabs was invited to be my ally, but he refused unless Omar gave him permission, so my father went. To Omar, he told him the story, and Omar said: Do not approach the Fire, for it has a deadline that it will not evade, nor will it shorten."
24094,"(24094) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Abdul Hamid bin Jafar, on the authority of Imran bin Abi Anas, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: He, peace and blessings of God be upon him: He forbade bathing, and detested cauterization. (Ahmad 4/1561 Tabarani 17)"
24095,"(24095) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was sent He was sent to Ubayy ibn Ka'b as a doctor, so he cut off a vein from him, then ironed it on him. (Muslim 73 Abu Dawud 3860)"
24096,"(24096) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abu Makin, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Imran bin Husayn; He cut the veins."
24097,"(24097) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abu Makin, who said: I saw Ibn Sirin at my water, and I said to him: What? What are you doing here? He said: I will sever the race of such and such to my nephew."
24098,"(24098) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Sulaiman, who said: I heard Mujahid say: A vein or vein was cut off from me."
24099,"(24099) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, who said: I saw Urwah afflicted with this disease. It means the one who ate it, so he cut off his leg from the kneecap."
24100,"(24100) Abdī narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abjar, on the authority of Amir, who said: He wipes over the sweat."
24101,"(24101) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mubarak, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He hated ducks and cut their veins."
24102,"(24102) Saul bin Yusuf narrated to us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Abu Rafi’, who said: Omar saw me with his hands bound. Or my legs, so he took me to the doctor, and he said: Calf, for if the calf is left between the bone and the flesh, it will eat away at it. He said: Al-Hasan hated ducks."
24103,"(24103) Mu’tamar told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He hated to bandage the wound, and he said: Put medicine on it."
24104,"(24104) Azhar told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, he said: Muhammad hated cutting off God, and I do not see him hating it. For some religion."
24105,"(24105) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Mas’udi, on the authority of Sahl Abi Al-Asad, on the authority of Abdullah bin Utbah, who said: Dhair came. We brought to Abdullah a boy whose jaw had fallen out, so they wanted to cut it off, so Ibn Masoud said: Do not cut it off. But if there was a delay in its term, it will be cured. Otherwise, you would not have cut off its life."
24106,"(24106) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Mukhtar, who said: Al-Hasan was asked about donkey milk? He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade its meat and milk."
24107,"(24107) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: Donkey meat and its milk are forbidden."
24108,"(24108) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’; He did not see any harm in drinking donkey’s milk."
24109,"(24109) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Muhammad; They both hated to be treated with donkey milk, and they said: It is forbidden."
24110,"(24110) Ubayd Allah told us, on the authority of Uthman ibn al-Aswad, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: I asked him about drinking donkey’s milk? He thought that"
24111,"(24111) Ubayd Allah narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Majza’ bin Zahir, on the authority of his father; He complained about his knees, so he was destined to soak in the donkeys’ dung, so he disliked that."
24112,"(24112) Yahya bin Sulaym al-Taifi told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Umayyah, on the authority of Ata’, who said: He did not see. With the milk of donkeys, it is good to be treated with it."
24113,"(24113) Shabab told us, he said: Shabab told us, he said: I asked the arbiter and Hammad about donkey milk? They said: Whoever hates its meat hates its dairy."
24114,"(24114) His youth told us, he said: His people told us, on the authority of Abraham; Like him"
24115,"(24115) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj bin Abi Othman, he said: Abu Raji, the client of Abi Qalab, narrated to me. On the authority of Abu Qalaba, he said: Anas bin Malik told me; A group of eight people from Ukal came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and they pledged their allegiance to him on the basis of Islam, so they took possession of the land. Their bodies became sick, so they complained about this to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: Don’t you go out with our shepherd in Is it camels that you are infected with from their urine and milk? They said: Yes, so they went out and drank from her urine and milk. (Bukhari 6899. Muslim 12)"
24116,"(24116) Abd al-Rahman bin Muhammad al-Muharbi narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ibn Tawus; That his father used to drink camel urine and take medical care with it."
24117,"(24117) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, who said: There is no harm in camel urine. He is treated with it."
24118,"(24118) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He hated it"
24119,"(24119) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, who said: Muhammad was asked about drinking camel urine? He says: I do not know what this is?"
24120,"(24120) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, who said: Jabbar al-Mashriqi used to describe the urine of camels And if he had been strong, he would not have filtered it."
24121,"(24121) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: There is no harm in inhaling urine. Camels"
24122,"(24122) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Habiba bint Yasar, on the authority of her mother, on the authority of Aisha; She was asked about a boy being soaked in urine, or being washed? His thoughts"
24123,"(24123) Al-Fadl narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Qais bin Muslim, on the authority of Tariq bin Shihab, he said: There was a man with Pigs, so she was treated with the urine of camels and horses. She cooked the urine of camels and dogs, so people started asking him, but he refused. He met Ibn Masoud and said: Tell the people about it."
24124,"(24124) Ismail bin Ayash narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Makhoul, and Abda, on the authority of Umm Abdullah ibn Khalid Ibn Maadan, on the authority of Abiyya; He did not see any harm in drinking the antidote."
24125,"(24125) Ismail bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Safwan bin Amr Al-Saskiski; When Omar bin Abdul Aziz took charge of Al-Walid bin Hisham Al-Qurashi, and Amr bin Qais Al-Sakouni sent Al-Sayfi and provided them with The antidote was from the treasure troves, and he ordered them that whoever came seeking the antidote should give it to him."
24126,"(24126) Ismail bin Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Khaled Al-Hadha’, who said: Abu Qulababi described to me a strain of the antidote, and he said: Men will come out wearing wooden sandals, and in their hands is something that he mentioned, and they will catch snakes, and they will wipe out what He touched their heads and their tails, to collect the blood that was there, then they threw them into the pot and cooked them, and that was The best antidote."
24127,"(24127) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, he said: I mentioned it to him, and he said: Didn’t he forbid it? About every fang? It has fangs and fever."
24128,"(24128) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: Ibn Umar ordered the antidote to be given to him, and he was given it to drink, even if he had known. What is in it is what He commanded."
24129,"(24129) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Muhammad; He hated it, meaning the antidote."
24130,"(24130) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Jarir bin Hazim, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: I heard him and he was asked about the antidote. And it was said to him: He places gnats in it? His thoughts"
24131,"(24131) Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri narrated to us, saying: Sa’id bin Abi Ayyub narrated to us, saying: Sharaheel bin Yazid narrated to us. Al-Maafiri said: I heard Abdul-Rahman bin Rafi’ al-Tanukhi saying: I heard Abdullah bin Amr saying: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. He says: I do not care what I did, and I would not commit a sin if I drank an antidote, or wore an amulet, or said: Poetry by myself. (Ahmad 2/223, Abu Dawud 3865)"
24132,"(24132) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Rizam bin Sa’id, on the authority of Abi Al-Ma’arik, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: None of you will prevent us. A sick person craves food, perhaps God will heal him, for God places his recovery wherever He pleases."
24133,"(24133) Yunus bin Muhammad narrated to us, saying: Fulayh bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Ayoub bin Abdul Rahman bin Abdullah bin Abi Sa’sa’a, on the authority of Yaqoub bin Abi Ya’qoub, on the authority of Umm Al-Mundhir Al-Adawiya, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, entered upon me. He greeted him, and with him was Ali, a camel, and we had baskets hanging. She said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, got up and ate, and he stood up. Ali and he ate, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Wait, for you are a she-camel. He said: Then Ali sat, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, ate from her. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. Then I made them chard and barley. The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to Ali: Who is this? I was injured (Abu Dawud 3852. Tirmidhi 2037)"
24134,"(24134) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of his father, who said: A mask made of dates was given to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. And Ali was feverish. He said: So he threw one date to him, then another, until he gave him seven, then he restrained his hand and said: It is sufficient for you."
24135,"(24135) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Fever is from the expanses of Hell, so cool it with water. (Bukhari 3263. Muslim 81)"
24136,"(24136) Abduh told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Fatima, on the authority of Asma’; She used to bring an ailing woman, and she would call for water and pour it into her pocket, and say: Indeed, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed. May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: Cool it with water, for it is from the scent of Hell. (Ibn Majah 3474, Muslim 1732)"
24137,"(24137) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abaya bin Rifa’i, he said: Rafi’ told me Ibn Khadij; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Fever comes from the heat of Hell, so cool it with water.
(Muslim 1733. Bukhari 5726)"
24138,"(24138) Ibn Numayr and Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, saying: Ubayd Allah narrated to us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: If the fever is exacerbated by the steam of Hell, then cool it with water. (Bukhari 3244, Muslim 78)"
24139,"(24139) Affan told us, he said: Hammam told us, on the authority of Abu Jamra, he said: I was defending people on behalf of Ibn Abbas, so I was detained. For days, he said: What kept you imprisoned? I said: Fever. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Fever is from the stench of Hell, so cool it with water. Zamzam (Ahmad 1/291 Hakim 403)"
24140,"(24140) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Muqassam, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; Whenever he had a bath, he would wet his garment, then put it on, then say: It is from the stench of Hell, so cool it with water."
24141,"(24141) Zaid bin Harun told us, saying: Abbad bin Mansour told us, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The best day on which you use cupping are seventeen, nineteen, and one. And twenty. (Tirmidhi 2053. Ahmad 1/354)"
24142,"(24142) Ibn Fudayl and Yazid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: It was astonishing that He is cupped from the seventeenth to the twentieth."
24143,"(24143) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Makhoul, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Who has cupping On Wednesday, and on Saturday, he was struck by wet water, and he had no one to blame but himself. (Hakim 409. Ibn Majah 3487)"
24144,"(24144) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever has cupping, let him use cupping. On Saturday."
24145,"(24145) Abdul-Wahhab narrated to us, on the authority of Hamid, on the authority of Anas, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Indeed, the most You received treatment with it, cupping, and Indian medicine for your children."
24146,"(24146) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Yasir bin Amr, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: He said: There is healing in size."
24147,"(24147) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, they said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace May God bless him and grant him peace. So he sent a man to him and he made a size for him."
24148,"(24148) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Uyayn bin Hisn entered upon the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. May God bless him and grant him peace while he was cupping, so he said: What is this? He said: The best thing the Arabs have sought medicine with."
24149,"(24149) Aswad bin Amir narrated to us, he said: Hammad bin Salama narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Salama, on the authority of Abu Huraira, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: If there is any good in what you treat with, then there is Cupping
(Abu Dawud 2095, Ahmad 2/423)"
24150,"(24150) Abu Nu’aym narrated to us, on the authority of Zuhair, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, he said: Husayn ibn Abi al-Hurr narrated to me. On the authority of Samarra bin Jundub, he said: I was with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he called for a cupper, and he ordered him to perform the cup. So he took out cups from the horns, clamped them on them, and cut them with the tip of a razor, so the blood poured out while I was with him, so he entered upon him. A man from Banu visited him and said: What is this, O Messenger of God? How can this cut your skin? He said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: This size. : What is the size? He said: It is the best thing that people can seek treatment with.
(Hakim 208. Ahmed 5/9)"
24151,"(24151) Zaid bin Harun told us, he said: Abbad bin Mansour told us, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I did not pass by a group of angels on the night when they took me as a captivity except that they said: May you be rewarded. With cupping, O Muhammad. (Tirmidhi 2053. Ibn Majah 3477)"
24152,"(24152) Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Yazid ibn Abi Habib, on the authority of a man from the Ansar from Bani Salamah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: If there is a cure for any of what you are being treated with, then there is a condition. From cupping, or from drinking honey, or from a sting from fire that causes pain, and I do not like to be burned by it."
24153,"(24153) Al-Fadl narrated to us, saying: Ibn Al-Ghaseel narrated to us, on the authority of Asim bin Omar bin Qatada, he said: I heard Jabir bin Abdullah He said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: If there is any good in any of your medicines, then there is a condition. Cupped, or by drinking honey, or by being stung by fire that matches the disease, and I do not like to be sick with it.
(Bukhari 5683. Muslim 71)"
24154,"(24154) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Abu Al-Mutawakkil Al-Naji, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, he said: A man came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, my brother has had stomach problems. He said: Give him honey to drink. So he gave him something to drink, so he came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, I gave him water to drink and he did not “Yazdādī” except in general terms. He said: Give him honey to drink. So he gave him something to drink, so he came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God. I gave him water to drink, but he did not increase it except by divulging it. He said: Give him honey to drink. Either on the third day, or on the fourth day. You have calculated it. He said: Then he was healed, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: God has spoken the truth, and your brother’s stomach has lied. (Bukhari 5684 and Muslim 91)"
24155,"(24155) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of al-Suddi, on the authority of Ya`foor ibn al-Mughirah, on the authority of Ali, who said: If he complains If any of you wants something, let him ask his wife for three dirhams from her dowry, and buy honey with it, and drink it with the water from the heavens. Then God will bring together the blessed one, the esophagus, the blessed water, and the healing."
24156,"(24156) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Nasir, on the authority of Bakr ibn Ma`izz, on the authority of al-Rabi` ibn Khathim, who said: What I have nothing for the sick except dates, and nothing for the sick except honey."
24157,"(24157) Abu Muawiyah and Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Khaythami, on the authority of Al-Aswad, he said: Abdullah said: May healing be upon you: the Qur’an and honey. (Ibn Majah 3452, Hakim 200)"
24158,"(24158) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, who said: A man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and complained to him about his stomach. His brother, so he said: You should have honey, then he returned to him and said: As if he were, so he said: Your brother’s stomach lied, but the Qur’an is true. You have honey."
24159,"(24159) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: They used to prefer fresh dates for fresh women."
24160,"(24160) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Amr ibn Maymun, who said: There is nothing for post-partum women except fresh water, because God Almighty He made it a provision for Maryam."
24161,"(24161) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Umair, on the authority of Amr ibn Harith, on the authority of Sa’id ibn Zaid, who said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Truffles are from manna, and it is a cure for the eye. (Bukhari 4478 and Muslim 157)"
24162,"(24162) Ubayd Allah narrated to us, saying: Shayban narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Al-Manhal, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Layla, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came out against us and there were people in his hand. He said: These are from manna, and they are a cure for the eye. (Ibn Majah 3453. Ahmad 3/48)"
24163,"(24163) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Abbad bin Mansour, on the authority of Al-Qasim, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger said: God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Truffles are from manna, and it is a cure for the eye. (Dharmi 2840)"
24164,"(24164) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Omar bin Hussein, on the authority of a man from the descendants of Hudhayfi, on the authority of Amir, who said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Truffles are part of manna, and its water is a cure for the eyes."
24165,"(24165) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abdul-Malik bin Umayr, on the authority of Amr bin Harith. On the authority of Saeed bin Zaid, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Truffles are from manna, and its water is a cure for the eyes."
24166,"(24166) Abu Dawud narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of a sheikh from the people of Wasit, who said: I asked Abu Iyad about poetry. Is a pig placed on an animal’s wound? His thoughts"
24167,"(24167) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Muhammad; They both hated that the boy’s head be painted with the blood of the aqeeqah, and Al-Hasan said: It is an abomination."
24168,"(24168) Omar bin Saad told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr; He hated the bitterness of the wolf."
24169,"(24169) Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi told us, on the authority of Bashir ibn Uqba al-Naji, who said: I asked Muhammad about cutting hemorrhoids? He thought of it and said: Put vinegar on it."
24170,"(24170) Saul bin Yusuf told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, he said: I said to Muhammad: Does the man steal a camel? He said: I see this as nothing but corruption."
24171,"(24171) Saul bin Yusuf told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He hated it."
24172,"(24172) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Abu Awani, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Al-Harith, he said: If the soldier is intelligent, It's okay"
24173,"(24173) Zaid bin Harun told us, saying: Hisham told us, on the authority of Muhammad; Was he asked about the soldier? He said: If he is intelligent, then there is no harm in him, but he disliked anything other than intelligent."
24174,"(24174) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Dawud, who said: Al-Sha’bi was asked about a man who used dog meat to heal himself? He said: If you seek treatment with it, God will not cure you."
24175,"(24175) Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, saying: Israel narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim; He was afflicted with quarter fever, and he was given the name of a fox's side, but he refused to eat it."
24176,"(24176) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, saying: Sufyan informed us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Dhakwan, on the authority of Aisha, she said: If he has a fever, he should take three quarters of ghee and a quarter of milk, then drink it."
24177,"(24177) Zaid bin Harun told us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Khalid, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Uthman, said: A doctor with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, mentioned a medicine that was administered to him. The frog. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade killing the frog. (Abu Dawud 5227. Ahmad 3/499)"
24178,"24178 On the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, he said: Do not kill frogs, for their croaking that you hear is praise."
24179,"(24179) Zaid bin Harun told us, he said: Hammam told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: The fox is one of the wildebeest."
24180,"(24180) Mukhlid bin Yazid narrated to us, and he was trustworthy, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’; He was asked about a man whose liver ached, and you told him that his liver was smeared and that his blood was drunk? He said: There is no problem, it is necessary. Ibn Juraij said: I said to him: Isn’t blood forbidden? He said: This is a necessity."
24181,"(24181) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu Jafar, who said: If he is forced to do what was forbidden to him, then what was forbidden to him, then It is lawful."
24182,"(24182) Mukhlid ibn Zayd told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: Ata’ was asked about a woman who dies while having a child in her womb. A man robs him and takes him out? He thought that"
24183,"(24183) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He saw no harm in a man robbing a woman if they were unable to treat a woman."
24184,"(24184) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, he said: Umm Sinan said: When I die, they open my stomach open, for there is a master in it. Ghatafan, he said: When she died, they cut open her stomach and extracted teeth."
24185,"(24185) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Umair, who said: Al-Harith ibn Kaladah, who was the doctor of the Arabs, said: The sun is forced for three times: it makes the wind heavy, wears out the garment, and brings out the buried blood."
24186,"(24186) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Thawr, on the authority of Mahfouz bin Alqamiya; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw a man in the sun, and he said: Turn to the shadow, for he is blessed."
24187,"(24187) Issa bin Yunus and Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Qays, who said: My father came and the Prophet prayed. God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was giving a speech, so he stood before him in the sun, so he commanded that it be done, so it was turned into the shadow."
24188,"(24188) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Samarra, who said: Omar said: Face the sun with your foreheads, for it is Arab pigeons."
24189,"(24189) Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid; He said: Zamzam water is a cure for what he drank."
24190,"(24190) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mughiryah ibn Ziyad, on the authority of Ata’; In the hundred days of Zamzam, he was taken out of the Sacred Mosque with it, and he said: Ka’b with twelve narrators moved to the Levant to seek healing with it."
24191,"(24191) Saeed bin Zakaria and Zaid bin Hubab told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Mu’amil, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: One hundred Zamzam for what he drank for him."
24192,"(24192) Zaid bin Harun told us, saying: Asim bin Suleiman told us, on the authority of Abu Uthman Al-Nahdi; The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, attacked with his companions, and a people passed by them hungry, meaning hungry, by a green tree. So they ate from it, and it was as if a wind had passed by them and extinguished them. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Pour the water into it. Al-Shanan, then they poured it over you between the call to prayer in the morning, and bring the water to a boiling water, and mention the name of God over it, so they did it. This is as if they had activated their mind."
24193,"(24193) Yunus bin Muhammad told us, he said: Abd al-Wahid bin Ziyad told us, he said: Asim al-Ahwal told us, he said: Ibn He walked for a day, then leaned on his right. He said: So I said: Physicians hate for a man to eat and lean on... His right, and he said: Ka’b did not hate that. He used to say: Prostrate yourself with your right, then face the Qiblah. For it is his fulfillment."
24194,"(24194) Zaid bin Harun told us, he said: Ismail told us, on the authority of Qais bin Abi Hazim, he said: A man fell ill. In Al-Mada'in, he said: I see him as one of the hypocrites, so Hudhayfy said: Carry him to the water of the Euphrates, for the water of the Euphrates is lighter than the water of the Tigris. He said: Then he became pregnant and died."
24195,"(24195) Ishaq Al-Azraq told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He hated medicine and put urine in it, but he forbade it."
24196,"(24196) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Khathim, on the authority of Ata’; If the woman breaks it, he said: There is no harm in the man fixing it."
24197,"(24197) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Walid Al-Muzani, on the authority of a woman from his family, on the authority of Abdullah bin fool; He said regarding a woman with a wound: He makes a puncture wound, then he closes it, then he treats it."
24198,"(24198) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Hammam, on the authority of his followers, who said: I said to Jabir ibn Zayd: The mirror breaks from it. The thigh, or the arm, should I force it? He said: Yes."
24199,"(24199) Ali bin Ghurab narrated to us, on the authority of Zam’a, on the authority of Salma bin Wharam, who said: I asked Tawus about the mirror. With this wound, how does the doctor treat it? He said: The site of the wound is closed on the garment, then the doctor treats it."
24200,"(24200) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abjar, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi; He was asked about a woman who has a wound? He said: Its place is pierced, then the man treats it."
24201,"(24201) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amer; If the woman breaks it, he said: There is no harm in the man fixing it."
24202,"(24202) Hussein bin Ali told us, he said: I heard Ibn Abjar say: Give up the evening dinner, unless you are fasting."
24203,"(24203) Hussein bin Ali told us, he said: I heard Ibn Abjar say: All meat is hot."
24204,"(24204) Abu Asama told us, he said: Marzuq bin Abdul Rahman Abu Hassan Al-Muazzin told us, he said: Matar Al-Warraq told us; One of the prophets complained to God about weakness, so He commanded him to cook meat with milk, for strength is in them."
24205,"(24205) Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Subih, the client of Banu Marwan, on the authority of Makhul, who said: I heard him say about Al-Risa: In the name of God, O God, you are the protector, you are the lasting, and you are the healer. He said: Then he ties an iron thread in it, Or hair, then the rhinestone is tied to it."
24206,"(24206) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Abu Burda, on the authority of his father, he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent him May God bless him and grant him peace, and he asked him about what drinks to make with: wheat, ale, and corn, and he said: every intoxicant. It is forbidden.
(Bukhari 4244, Muslim 75)"
24207,"(24207) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Salama, on the authority of Aisha; It conveys to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: Every drink that intoxicates is forbidden. (Bukhari 5866 Muslim 69)"
24208,"(24208) Ismail Ibn Aliyya told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. And peace be upon him. He said: Every intoxicant is forbidden. He said: And Ibn Umar said: Every intoxicant is alcohol. (Muslim 73 Abu Dawud 3671)"
24209,"(24209) Ismail Ibn Aliyya told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Abu Uthman, on the authority of Al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, on the authority of Aisha, on the authority of The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Every intoxicant is forbidden. (Abu Dawud 3680; Ahmad 6/72)"
24210,"(24210) Qubaysah narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ali bin Dhamima, on the authority of Qais bin Habatar, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Every intoxicant is forbidden. (Abu Dawud 3672)"
24211,"(24211) Muhammad ibn Ubaid narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Yazid ibn Abi Habib, on the authority of Marthad ibn Abd Allah Al-Yazani, on the authority of Daylam Al-Himyari, said: I asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I said: O Messenger of God, we In a cold land, we deal with hard work, and we take a drink from this wheat to gain strength with it for our deeds and for the cold. In our country? He said: Does he get drunk? I said: Yes. He said: So avoid him. He said: Then I came to him from his presence, so I said to him the same thing. He said: Yes. Does he get drunk? I said: Yes. He said: So avoid it. I said: People will not abandon it. He said: If they do not abandon it, then kill them.
(Abu Dawud 3676. Ahmad 4/231)"
24212,"(24212) Mulazim bin Amr told us, on the authority of Siraj bin Uqba, on the authority of his paternal aunt Khalida bint Talq, she said: My father told me, He said: We were sitting with the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, when Sohar Abdul Qais came and said: O Messenger of God, what do you see? What drink do we make from our fruits? He said: Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, turned away from him until he asked him three times, then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, led us. He said the salaam and prayed. When he finished the prayer, he said: Who is asking about an intoxicant? He who asks about intoxicants, do not drink it, and do not give it to anyone of the Muslims to drink, for by the One in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, he did not drink it. There has never been a man who sought the pleasure of his intoxication, then God would make him drink wine on the Day of Resurrection. (Tabarani 8259)"
24213,"(24213) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, he said: Muhammad bin Amr narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Every intoxicant is forbidden."
24214,"(24214) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Aban bin Abdullah Al-Bajli, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, On the authority of his grandfather, he said: The Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Every intoxicant is forbidden. (Abu Dawud 3678. Ahmad 2/171)"
24215,"(24215) Abdullah bin Numir told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Amr, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Shahr bin Hawshab, on the authority of Umm Salama, She said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade every intoxicant and slanderer. (Ahmad 6/309, Abu Dawud 3679)"
24216,"(24216) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Marouf bin Wasil, on the authority of Muharib bin Dathar, on the authority of Ibn Buraidah, on the authority of his father, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I forbade you from drinking in human conditions, so drink from every vessel. Except that you do not drink intoxicants. (Abu Dawud 3691)"
24217,"(24217) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Abu Sinan, on the authority of Muharib bin Dathar, on the authority of Ibn Buraydah, on the authority of his father, He said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Drink from the watered waters in all of them, and do not drink any intoxicating drink."
24218,"(24218) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Abu Hayyan, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Maryam bint Tariq, on the authority of Aisha; Anna, she said: Every intoxicant is forbidden."
24219,"(24219) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: Every intoxicant is forbidden, and Ibn Umar said: Every An intoxicating drink."
24220,"(24220) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Burda, he said: Omar said: Indeed, this repugnance will be rejected. Of the five things: Of dates, raisins, honey, wheat, and barley. Whatever you fermented from them and then aged, it is wine."
24221,"(24221) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Al-Mukhtar. He said: I asked Anas about wine? He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade false circumstances, and said: Every intoxicant is forbidden. (Muslim 31. Ahmad 112)"
24222,"(24222) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hayyan, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Maryam bint Tariq, she said: I entered upon Aisha was among the women of the Ansar, so they asked her about the circumstances under which she is rejected? She said: O women of the believers, you will often present many circumstances and be asked about them. There were not many of them during the time of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace, so fear God, and whatever drink intoxicates any of you, let him avoid it, but if water intoxicates with love, Every intoxicant is forbidden. (Hakim 147)"
24223,"(24223) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’, Tawoos, and Mujahid; They said: A little of it is intoxicating, a lot of it is forbidden.
(Bukhari 4419 and Muslim 2322)"
24224,"(24224) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Abu Hayyan, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: I heard Umar ibn Al-Khattab giving a sermon. On the pulpit of Medina, he said: O people, the prohibition of alcohol was revealed on the day it was revealed, and it included five things. ; Of grapes, dates, honey, wheat, barley, and wine, whatever the mind is intoxicated with."
24225,"(24225) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Al-Sa’ib ibn Yazid, who said: Omar ibn Al-Khattab said: It was mentioned to me. The servants of God and his companions drank a drink in the Levant, and I am asking about it. If it is intoxicating, I will flog them."
24226,"(24226) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Al-Sa’ib bin Yazid, who said: I saw Omar He defines them."
24227,"(24227) Zaid bin Al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Salih, he said: Hatim bin Harith narrated to us, on the authority of Malik bin Abi Maryam, he said: We discussed the paint, then Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanam came to us and we discussed it, and he said: Abu Malik al-Ash’ari told me. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, says: Some people from my nation drink wine and call it by another name. They will be struck on the heads with instruments and harps, and God will cause the earth to swallow them up, and will turn them into apes and pigs.
(Abu Dawud 3681, Ahmad 5/342)"
24228,"(24228) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa told us, on the authority of Saad ibn Aws, on the authority of Bilal ibn Yahya, on the authority of Abu Bakr ibn Hafs, On the authority of Ibn Muhayriz, on the authority of Ibn al-Samit, on the authority of Ubadah ibn al-Samit, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: To make it permissible The last of my nation to drink wine by the name you call it. (Ahmad 5/318, Bazzar 2689)"
24229,"(24229) Abu Asama narrated to us, saying: Al-Thawri narrated to us, on the authority of Salma bin Kuhail, on the authority of Dhar bin Abdullah, on the authority of Saeed bin Abdul Rahman bin Abza, on the authority of his father, he said: I asked Ubayy bin Ka’b about wine? He said: You have water, you have to eat fresh fruits, you have to eat honey, you have to eat the milk with which you were successful. He said, so I went back to him and he said: Do you want wine?"
24230,"(24230) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Muhammad, on the authority of Ubaidah, he said: The people talked to me about what I drank. I don’t know what. I have had no drink for twenty years except water, milk, and honey."
24231,"(24231) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, he said: Abu Kathir told us, he said: I heard Abu Hurairah, he said: I heard The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The wine is from these two trees; Of grapes and palm trees. 
(Muslim 15. Abu Dawud 3670)"
24232,"(24232) Zayd bin Hubab told us, he said: Al-Dahhak bin Othman told us, he said: Bukayr bin Abdullah bin Al-Ashjaj told me, He said: I see it on the authority of Amer bin Saad bin Abi Waqqas. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: He forbade you from a few things. It makes a lot of people intoxicated. (Nasa’i 5119. Darami 2099)"
24233,"(24233) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, on the authority of al-Rabi`, on the authority of Abu al-Aaliyah, or someone else, on the authority of Ibn Mughaffal, He said: I witnessed with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he forbade the use of strong wine, and I witnessed it. He permitted it and said: Avoid it. Every intoxicant. (Tahawi 229. Ahmad 4/87)"
24234,"(24234) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Hubira, on the authority of Ali, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade May the peace and blessings of God be upon him. (Tirmidhi 3454, Ibn Majah 3454)"
24235,"(24235) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Sami’, on the authority of Muslim Al-Batin, he said: I asked Abu Amr Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Ja’i, said: A drink made from barley in Yemen."
24236,"(24236) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Juwayriyyah, he said: I asked Ibn Abbas about Al-Badhiq? He said: Muhammad Al-Badhiq preceded me. I was the first Arab to ask Ibn Abbas about that. (Bukhari 5988, An-Nasa’i 5116)"
24237,"(24237) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, he said: He informed me on the authority of Omar bin Abdul Aziz, he said: Some people were drinking, and one of them got drunk, so he flogged them all."
24238,"(24238) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Al-Ala’ ibn Al-Minhal, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwa, who said: Omar ibn Abd was brought Al-Aziz met a group of people who had sat drinking, and with them was a fasting man. He hit them and said: Do not sit with them until they engage in a conversation. Others"
24239,"(24239) Zayd ibn Harun told us, on the authority of Hammad ibn Salama, on the authority of Ali ibn Zayd, on the authority of Rabi’a ibn al-Nabighi, on the authority of His father, on the authority of Ali, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I had forbidden you from these vessels, so drink Therein, and avoid what intoxicates."
24240,"(24240) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Ash’ath ibn Abi Al-Sha’ath’i, he said: I told him: Your father was He drinks wine? He said: Yes, until he met Abdullah bin Omar and he forbade him."
24241,"(24241) Ubayd Allah narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Amr bin Shurahbil, on the authority of Omar, he said: It was The caller of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, when he stood up for prayer, calling out: {Do not approach prayer while you are drunk}"
24242,"(24242) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Hafs, on the authority of Ibn Muhayriz, he said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: A group of your nation will drink wine by the name they call it. (Abdul Razzaq 17055)"
24243,"(24243) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Khaled bin Dinar, on the authority of a sheikh, who said: I heard Ibn Abbas say: Drunkenness is one of the major sins."
24244,"(24244) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, saying: Israel narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim ibn Muhajir, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Al-Numan bin Bashir, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: From wheat is wine, from barley is wine, and from raisins is wine. And from honey there is wine. (Abu Dawud 3668. Tirmidhi 1872)"
24245,"(24245) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far bin Burqan, on the authority of Furat bin Salman, on the authority of a man from Al-Qasim’s companions, on the authority of Aisha, she said : The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The first thing in Islam to be rewarded with a drink is called: Al-Tala’.
(Abu Ali 4712)"
24246,"(24246) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Hayyan, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Aisha, she said: Ashrabiya narrated If it had been at the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he would have forbade it."
24247,"(24247) Yazeed bin Harun told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibn Sirin; That a man said to Ibn Umar: Indeed, our people give up a drink in the morning, so they drink it in the evening, and they give it up in the evening. So they drank it in the morning. Ibn Umar said: He forbade you from intoxication, little or much, and I bear witness to God that The people of Khaybar give themselves a drink of such-and-such, and they call it such-and-such, and it is wine, and the people of So they gave up a drink of such-and-such, and they called it such-and-such, and that is wine, so he counted four people who drank it. One of them is honey. Ibn Aoun said: Ibn Sirin used to call them all except honey."
24248,"(24248) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Sami’, on the authority of Malik bin Umair; Sa`sa` bin Suhan came to Ali and greeted him, and said: O Commander of the Faithful, forbid us from doing what the Messenger of God has forbidden. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: He said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade us from the bears, the hantam, and the muqayir. And the hunger
(Abu Dawud 3690, Ahmad 1/138)"
24249,"(24249) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said : The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade the dabba’, the hantam, the imitated, and the naqir. (Bukhari 53. Muslim 48)"
24250,"(24250) Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Mansour bin Hayyan, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: I bear witness to Ibn Abbas and Ibn Umar testified that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade saddlebags, camels, and imitated clothes. And the horn. (Muslim 1580, Abu Dawud 3683)"
24251,"(24251) Muhammad bin Bishr and Muhammad bin Ubaid narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Salama, on the authority of Abu Hariri, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade the use of shams, saddlebags, and camels. And the horn.
(Muslim 1577. Ibn Hibban 5404)"
24252,"(24252) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abi Ismail, on the authority of Amara bin Asim Al-Anazi, he said: I entered upon Anas bin Malik, I asked him about wine, and he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade the use of wine and pure wine? So I returned it to him, and he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade things that are made of stones and tiles, so I returned them to him, and he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade the use of clay and terracotta. (Bukhari 5587, Muslim 1577)"
24253,"(24253) Ali bin Ishaq narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Mubarak, on the authority of Waqi’, on the authority of Ali bin Rabi’i, on the authority of Samarra, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade the use of clay and terracotta. (Ahmad 5/17)"
24254,"(24254) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The Messenger of God forbade May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, on the authority of Al-Dabba’, Al-Naqir, and the imitated ones. (Muslim 1583. Ahmad 3/384)"
24255,"(24255) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Muharib, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade On the authority of Al-Dabai’, Al-Hantam, and the fake ones, he said: And I see him saying: And the Naqir. (Muslim 1582. Ahmad 2/42)"
24256,"(24256) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, delivered a speech. One day, I came and he had finished, and I asked the people: What did the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say? They said: He forbade the use of pure earth and pumpkin. (Muslim 1581. Ahmad 2/54)"
24257,"(24257) Shababi told us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Salamah, he said: Abu Al-Hakam said: My brother told me, on the authority of Abu Sa’id; The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade pure wine, sweet wines, and pure wines. (Ahmad 66. Abu Ali 1302)"
24258,"(24258) Shababi told us, he said: Shu’ba told us, on the authority of Bukair bin Ata, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Omar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade the use of tambourines, imitations, and hantams. (Tirmidhi 713. Ibn Majah 3404)"
24259,"(24259) Muhammad bin Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade May God bless him and grant him peace, on the authority of Al-Dabba’, Al-Hantam, and the asphalt, and she said: Al-Hantam is a jar that is brought from Egypt and is used to work in it. Wine
(Bukhari 5958, Muslim 1578)"
24260,"(24260) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Ash’ath bin Umair Al-Abdi, on the authority of his father, he said: A delegation from Abdul Qais came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and when they wanted to leave, they said: You have learned from the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace, everything you heard from him, so ask him about wine? So they came to him and said: O Messenger of God, we are in land and land in which nothing is good except for drink. He said: So he said: What is your drink? They said: Wine. He said: What do you drink? They said: In the well. He said: So do not drink from the well. He said: So they went out and said: By God, our people will not agree to this, so they returned. So they asked him, and he told them the same thing. Then they returned, and he said to them: Do not drink from the well lest the man strike your cousin. A blow from which he will still be limping until the Day of Resurrection. He said: They laughed. He said: What are you laughing at? They said: O Messenger of God, by the One who sent you with the truth, we drank in a cistern of ours, and one of us stood up to one another and hit this man. He ascended from it until the Day of Resurrection. (Al-Tabarani 122)"
24261,"(24261) Yazid bin Harun told us, saying: Sulayman al-Taymi told us, on the authority of Asma bint Yazid, on the authority of a cousin To him, it is said to him: Anas, that he heard Ibn Abbas say: Did not God Almighty say: {And whatever the Messenger gives you, take it and whatever He forbade you from it, so refrain from it}? They said: Yes, he said: Didn’t God Almighty say: {And it is not for a believer or a believer when God and His Messenger have decided a matter}? He said: I bear witness to the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, that he forbade pure wine, pureed wine, and mixed drinks. And the humpback.
(Nasa’i 5154)"
24262,"(24262) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abu Shimr al-Dab’iy, who said: I heard Aidh ibn Amr forbidding al-hantam. And Al-Dabai’, Al-Muzafat, and Al-Naqir. He said: So I said to him: On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace? He said: Yes.
(Ahmad 5/64, Tabarani 29)"
24263,"(24263) Muhammad bin Musab told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Abu Salama, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade pure wine, mixed drinks, imitated drinks, and all other circumstances.
(Ibn Majah 408. Ahmad 2/540)"
24264,"(24264) Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, on the authority of Asim al-Ahwal, on the authority of Fudayl ibn Zaid, he said: We were with Abdullah bin Mughaffal and we discussed drinking, and he said: Alcohol is forbidden, so I said: Alcohol is forbidden in the Book of God. He said: What do you want? Do you want what you heard from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbidding the use of tambourine, hantam, and asphalt tiles. (Ahmad 4/87 Darami 2112)"
24265,"(24265) Ahmad bin Ishaq narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Wahid bin Ziyad narrated to us, saying: Kulayb bin Wael narrated to us, saying: His stepson, the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, told me. I think it was Zainab. She said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade it. He greeted the beasts of war and the camels, and I saw the horn in it. (Bukhari 3492. Tabarani 716)"
24266,"(24266) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Farwa, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Abi Laila; He disliked the mixture of pure earth and said: Because I drink the urine of a donkey that is more beloved to me than drinking from pure earth."
24267,"(24267) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Harun al-Abdi, on the authority of Abu Sa`id al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade May God bless him and grant him peace. (Abdul Razzaq 16930)"
24268,"(24268) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Saad bin Ubaidah, on the authority of Al-Bara’, he said: Omar commanded me to I am called out on the Day of Qadisiyah: There is no wine in the cups, no hantam, and no clay pots."
24269,"(24269) Ali bin Musir told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Abdul-Malik bin Nafi’, he said: I asked Ibn Umar about paint. Is it cooked? He said: There is no problem. I said: It is in pure water. He said: Do not drink it in pure water."
24270,"(24270) Saul bin Yusuf narrated to us, on the authority of Sulaiman al-Taymi, on the authority of Abu Majliz, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Abu Hurairah ; He forbade imitation ones."
24271,"(24271) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Amr, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said : The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade the use of dried fruits, tamzafat, hantam, and naqir, and to mix dates with With pride
(Muslim 3. An-Nasa’i 5057)"
24272,"(24272) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Al-Mukhtar bin Falfil, he said: I asked Anas bin Malik about wine? He said: Avoid intoxicants in everything, and avoid anything other than that when you travel in close proximity, or close proximity, or by land. Or drag it."
24273,"(24273) Zaid bin Harun told us, he said: Abdul Khaliq bin Salamah told us, he said, I heard Saeed bin Al-Musayyab He says: I heard Ibn Umar saying at this pulpit, and he pointed to the pulpit of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: A delegation came Abdul Qais Ali the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. So they asked him about drinks? So he forbade them from al-Dabai’, al-Naqir, and al-Hanatam, so I said: O Abu Muhammad, the imitated ones? We thought he had forgotten it, so he said: I have not heard it from Ibn Umar since.
(Muslim 1583. Ahmad 2/41)"
24274,"(24274) Yazeed bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Abu Al-Tayyah, on the authority of Hafs Al-Laythi, on the authority of Imran Ibn Al-Husayn; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade the practice of having sex. (Tirmidhi 1738. Ahmad 4/427)"
24275,"(24275) Ubaid bin Saeed narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, she said : The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade the use of carpets and tiles. (Bukhari 5950, Muslim 35)"
24276,"(24276) Ubaidah bin Hamid told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, he said: I said to Aisha: What he forbade. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, who drank? She said: He forbade the use of carpets and tiles. 
 Abraham said: So I said to the black ones: What about the camels and the green pitchers? He said: You want us to say what was not said?"
24277,"(24277) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abu Hamza, a neighbor of theirs, who said: I heard a man from Bani Mazen, Hilal. It is narrated on the authority of Suwayd bin Muqrin, who said: I brought wine to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and asked him: He turned me away, so I took the jar and broke it. (Ahmad 3/447, Tayalisi 9264)"
24278,"(24278) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Al-Taymiy, on the authority of Abu Nadhrah, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, he said: The Messenger forbade May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, on the authority of green grape wine. I said: What about white wine? He said: I don't know. (Muslim 1580, Tirmidhi 1877)"
24279,"(24279) Zaid bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Taymiyyah, on the authority of Aminah, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade May God bless him and grant him peace, on the authority of Nabeez Al-Jar. (Ibn Majah 3407 and Abd al-Razzaq 14964)"
24280,"(24280) Ibn Mushir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Ibn Abi Awfa, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade And peace be upon him, about the genitive of green, I said: What about white? He said: I don't know. (Bukhari 5596. Ahmad 4/353)"
24281,"(24281) Ismail Ibn Ali told us, on the authority of Sa’id Ibn Yazid, on the authority of Abd al-Aziz Ibn Asid, he said: He said: A man told Ibn al-Zubayr: He gave us a fatwa regarding the wine of the genitive. He said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbidding the wine of the genitive.
(Ahmad 4/3 Bazzar 2227)"
24282,(۲۴۲۸۲) حَدَّثَنَا یَحْیَی بْنُ سَعِیدٍ ، عَنْ أَبِی حَیَّانَ ، عَنْ عَبَایَۃَ بْنِ رِفَاعَۃَ ، أَنَّ جَدَّہُ رَافِعَ بْنَ خَدِیجٍ رَأَی جَرَّۃً خَضْرَائَ لأَہْلِہِ فِی الشَّمْسِ ، فَأَخَذَ جُلْمُودًا فَرَمَاہَا فَکَسَرَہَا ، فَإِذَا فِیہَا سَمْنٌ فَقَالَ :
24283,(۲۴۲۸۳) حَدَّثَنَا غُنْدَرٌ ، عَنْ شُعْبَۃَ ، عَنْ حُصَیْنٍ ، عَنِ امْرَأَۃٍ مِنْ بَنِی شَیْبَانَ ، أَنَّ زَوْجَہَا أَتَاہُمْ So he told them; أَنَّ أَمِیرَ الْمُؤْمِنِینَ عَلِیًّا نَہَاہُمْ عَنْ نَبِیذِ الْجَرِّ ، قَالَ : فَکَسَرْنَا جَرَّۃً لَنَا۔
24284,"(24284) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Uyaynah bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of his father; Abu Burda came from a journey, so he started at Abu Bakra’s house, and he saw a jar in the house, and he said: What is this? It was said: There is wine in it for Abu Bakra, and he said: I wish you had turned it into water-drinking."
24285,"(24285) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Dawud bin Faraij, who said: I heard Abu Hurairah forbidding draft wine"
24286,"(24286) Yazeed bin Harun told us, on the authority of Abdul-Malik, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr; They mentioned wine, so he said: I don’t see anything wrong with it when drinking water, and I hate it when drinking green water."
24287,"(24287) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’ba, on the authority of Abu Raja’, on the authority of Malik ibn Dinar; Jabir bin Zayd and Al-Hassan disliked gin wine."
24288,"(24288) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Thabit, who said: I said to Ibn Umar: He forbade the prepositional wine? He said: They claimed that. I said: On the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? He said: They claimed that. I said: Did you hear it? He said: They claimed that. He said: And God turned him away from him. (Muslim 500, Ahmad 35)"
24289,"(24289) Zayd ibn Harun told us, saying: Sha’bah told us, on the authority of Abu Jamrah; A woman came to Ibn Abbas, and I had sworn not to ask about wine, so she said to him: Ask him, but I refused. He asked him, and a man asked him about the wine of the draft? So he stopped, so I said: O Abu Abbas, I seek refuge in a green jar, so I drink it sweet and good and it makes my stomach growl. So he said: Do not drink it, even if it is sweeter than honey. (Muslim 24)"
24290,"(24290) Yazid bin Harun narrated to us, saying: Suleiman Al-Taymi narrated to us, on the authority of Tawus; That a man came to Ibn Umar and said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade the use of strong wine? Ibn Omar said: Yes, and Tawus said: By God, I heard it from him. (Muslim 53. Ahmad 2/35)"
24291,"(۲۴۲۹۱) حَدَّثَنَا عَفَّانُ ، قَالَ : حدَّثَنَا جَرِیرُ بْنُ حَازِمٍ ، قَالَ : حَدَّثَنِی یَعْلَی بْنُ حَکِیمٍ ، عَنْ صُہَیْرَۃَ بِنْتِ جَیْفَرٍ ، سَمِعَہُ مِنْہَا ، قَالَتْ : حَجَجْنَا ثُمَّ انْصَرَفْنَا إِلَی الْمَدِینَۃِ ، فَدَخَلْنَا عَلَی صَفِیَّۃَ بِنْتِ حُیَیٍّ ، فَوَافَقْنَا There were women from the people of Kufa with you, so they said to us: If you wish, you can ask us and we will listen to you, and if you wish, you can ask and we will listen, so they said: سَلْنَ ، فَسَأَلْنَ عَنْ أَشْیَائَ مِنْ أَمْرِ الْمَرْأَۃِ وَزَوْجِہَا ، وَمِنْ أَمْرِ الْمَحِیضِ ، وَسَأَلْنَ عَنْ نَبِیذِ الْجَرِّ ، فَقَالَتْ : أَکْثَرْتُنَّ یَا أَہْلَ الْعِرَاقِ عَلَیْنَا فِی نَبِیذِ الْجَرِّ ، حَرَّمَ رَسُولُ اللہِ صَلَّی اللَّہُ عَلَیْہِ وَسَلَّمَ نَبِیذَ الْجَرِّ ، مَا عَلَی إِحْدَاکُنَّ أَنْ تَطْبُخَ تَمْرَہَا ، ثُمَّ تَدْلُکُہُ ، ثُمَّ تُصَفِّیہِ فَتَجْعَلُہُ فِی سِقَائِہَا ، وَتُوکِئُ عَلَیْہِ ،"
24292,"(24292) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`bah, on the authority of Shamisa, Umm Salamah al-Atkiya, who said: I heard Aisha say: No. You drink from a vat, and do not draw it or draw a cup."
24293,"(24293) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ali bin al-Mubarak, on the authority of Karima bint Hammam, on the authority of Aisha, that I heard her saying: Beware of green grape wine."
24294,"(24294) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Ala bin Kaysan, who said: I heard Ibn Abi al-Dhayl saying: What is in I do not like the preposition at all, except that Omar bin Abdul Aziz forbade it, and he was a just imam."
24295,"(24295) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ja`far bin Burqan, on the authority of Maimun, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: Do not drink draft wine."
24296,"(24296) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Abdullah said: Sugar is wine."
24297,"(24297) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Farwa, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Layla, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr said: Sugar is wine."
24298,"(24298) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, Ibrahim, and Abu Razin. They said: Sugar is wine."
24299,"(24299) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Ibn Shubarmah, on the authority of Abu Zur’a ibn Amr ibn Jarir, who said: It is wine, and it is Pain from wine."
24300,"(24300) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: This is wine."
24301,"(24301) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Harb, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He was asked about drunkenness? He said: Wine has no meaning."
24302,"(24302) Abu Bakr bin Ayash told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Wael, who said: A group of Bedouins came to Abdullah. They ask him about drunkenness? He said: God has not made a cure for you in what He has forbidden to you."
24303,"(24303) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Abdullah; Like him"
24304,"(24304) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Wael, who said: A man from the neighborhood complained about his stomach, and it was said to him: You called him the yellow one, so they called him drunk, so he sent to Abdullah to ask him about that? Abdullah said: God Almighty has not made a cure for you in what He has forbidden to you."
24305,"(24305) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, and Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: Sugar Wine"
24306,"(24306) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Salma bin Tammam, on the authority of Amer, who said: Sugar is wine."
24307,"(24307) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Fudayl bin Ghazwan, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Zur, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, on the authority of Abd God said: Grape wine is wine."
24308,"(24308) Abu Osama narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Walid, who said: Maimunah bint Abd al-Rahman bin Maqil narrated to me; That her father was asked about raisin wine? His thoughts"
24309,"(24309) Abdul Rahman bin Sulayman told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Bukair, a client of Abdullah bin Masoud, on the authority of Sa’id. Ibn Jubayr said: It is more beloved to me to be a donkey being watered than to drink aged raisin wine."
24310,"(24310) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu Ja’far, Amir, and Ata’; They disliked grape wine."
24311,"(24311) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Harb, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He was asked about soaking raisins? He said: Avoid alcohol."
24312,"(24312) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Bukair, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: Because I am a donkey that can be drawn? Ali, is more beloved to me than drinking aged raisin wine."
24313,"(24313) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hanifa, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, who said: Drink wine. Soaked raisins, as long as they are sweet, soothe the tongue."
24314,"(24314) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Umar, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was May the peace and blessings of God be upon him, the raisins are soaked for him, and he drinks them today, and tomorrow, and the day after, until the third evening, then He commands it to be given to drink, or to be spilled. (Muslim 1589. Abu Dawud 3706)"
24315,"(24315) Affan told us, he said: Abd al-Wahid bin Safwan told us, he said: I heard my father telling, on the authority of his mother, she said: I used to give Uthman raisins in the morning and he would drink them in the evening, or I would give him raisins in the evening and he would drink them in the morning, and he said: Laha Othman: Perhaps you will put perfume in it? She said: Maybe I did. He said: Don't do it."
24316,"(24316) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Musa bin Tarif, on the authority of his father, who said: He used to reject Ali. Raisins in white balls, so he drinks them."
24317,"(24317) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Nafi’, who said: I said to Ibn Umar: I reject Raisin wine, then some of our companions come and throw dates in it, spoiling it for me, so what do you think? He said: There is no harm in it."
24318,"(24318) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Ikrimah; Regarding grape wine, he said: The top of it was forbidden, and the bottom of it was forbidden."
24319,"(24319) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ali ibn al-Aqmar, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: There is no harm in juice wine."
24320,"(24320) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Hallam ibn Salih, on the authority of Sulayk ibn Mishal, who said: Omar went out for Hajj, or performing Umrah, and came down. He asked for water, so he called for a cup of coffee, and he ate and the people ate, then he called for a drink, and a cup of wine was brought to him, and he said: Give it to me. Abd al-Rahman bin Awf, when he smelled him, he threw him back, then he gave him to Sa`d bin Abi Waqqas, and when he smelled him, he threw him back, and said: So bring it. So he tasted it and said: O Ajlan, meaning his servant, what is this? He said: O Commander of the Faithful, I put raisins in a watering can, then I hung them on the stomach of the departed woman and poured some water over him. He said: Bring witnesses to what you say. So he brought witnesses, and they bore witness, and he said: My son, wash my waterskins so that they will be soft for us. Drink it, for the one who drinks it takes advantage of it."
24321,"(24321) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Mansour bin Hayyan, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: A man asked him, and he said: We go to the raisins and wash them of their dust, then we place them in a dungeon, or in a tent, and we leave them in the winter for two months. And in the summer, is it less than that? Saeed said: Avoid that alcohol."
24322,"(24322) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Omar bin Amir, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab (h) and on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, they said: There is no harm in drinking juice as long as it does not boil. Sa`id said: If it is expensive, then it is wine, avoid it, and Abraham said: If it is expensive, then leave it."
24323,"(24323) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If it rises to an expensive level, do not drink it."
24324,"(24324) Abdullah bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Yazid bin Abdullah bin Qusayt, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab; He saw nothing wrong with juice unless it foamed, so if it did foam, he forbade it, and said: It only foams wine."
24325,"(24325) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Khaseef, he said: I asked Saeed about juice? He said: Drink it every day and night."
24326,"(24326) Muhammad narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Amr ibn Abi Hakim, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: Drink juice unless It roars."
24327,"(24327) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Abu Ya‘four Abd al-Rahman bin Ubaid al-Amiri, on the authority of Ayman Abu Thabit said: I was sitting with Ibn Abbas, when a man came and asked him about juice? He said: Drink it as long as it is fresh."
24328,"(24328) Ismail Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: There is no harm in drinking juice as long as it has not boiled. Three."
24329,"(24329) Hafs told us, on the authority of Abdul-Malik, on the authority of Ata’, who said: Drink it three times, as long as it does not boil."
24330,"(24330) Ali bin Musir and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Aidh, who said: I asked Ibrahim about juice? He said: Drink it as long as it does not change."
24331,"(24331) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: There is no harm in drinking and selling what He did not boil."
24332,"(24332) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, Abu Ja`far, and Ata’, they said: Drink the juice, son of Day and night."
24333,"(24333) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Dinar, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: Drink the juice as long as it has not changed."
24334,"(24334) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abdullah bin Murra, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He was asked about juice? He said: Drink it as long as Satan takes hold of you. It was said: And for how much has Satan taken hold of you? He said: In three."
24335,"(24335) Affan told us, he said: Bashir bin Uqba told us, he said: I asked Ibn Sirin about grape juice? He said: The juice of his day in his press. He said: Drink it during his day, for I hate it if it is put into a vessel, or He took a bowl and said: You should eat grape juice, for it is the best, so drink it."
24336,"(24336) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Jabir, who said: We were with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He greeted him and asked for something to drink, and a man said: Shall we not give you wine to drink? He said: Yes, he said: Then the man went out and wasted, and he brought a goblet containing wine, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: No. You would leave him alone, even if you offered him a stick.
(Muslim 94. Abu Dawud 3727)"
24337,"(24337) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, He said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: Give me something to drink from this, so Al-Abbas said: Shall we not give you something to drink from what we make? In homes? He said: No, but give me something to drink from what the people drink. He said: Then a cup of wine was brought to him. He tasted it and frowned, then said: Bring some water. So he poured it on him, then he said: Add it, twice, or three times, then he said: If this happens to you, do with it. This is how
(Daraqutni 81)"
24338,"(24338) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Qurayyat al-Ijli, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn al-Qaqa`, on the authority of Ibn Umar, He said: We were with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and a cup of drink was brought to him. He brought it near, then returned it, and he said to him: Those sitting with him: Is it forbidden, O Messenger of God? He said: So he said: Return it, and they returned it, then he called for water and poured it on him, then he drank, and said: Look at this drink. It has attacked you, so cut its flesh with water. (Nasa’i 5205, Bayhaqi 305)"
24339,"(24339) Yahya bin Yaman told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Khalid bin Saad, on the authority of Abu Masoud; The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was thirsty while circumambulating the Ka’bah, so he asked for something to drink and was brought wine from The drinker smelled it, frowned, and said: I am guilty of sins from Zamzam. So he poured it on him and drank, and a man said: Is it forbidden, O Messenger of God? He said: No. 
(Nasa’i 5212, Bayhaqi 304)"
24340,"(24340) Muhammad bin Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he will be given a drink to drink. If there is no drinker, he will be given a drink for him. Ash'ath said: And the tree is made of tree bark.
(Muslim 1584, Abu Dawud 3695)"
24341,"(24341) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Amr ibn Murā, on the authority of Zazan, he said: I asked Ibn Umar about wine? So I said to him: We have a language other than yours, so he explained it to us in our language. Ibn Umar said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade it. May the peace and blessings of God be upon him, on the authority of al-Hantamiyah, which is the jar, and he forbade the saddlebags, which is the qar’, and on the imitated ones, which is al-muqqar, On the authority of al-Naqir, which is the palm tree, and he commanded it to be left in watering places. (Muslim 1583. Tirmidhi 1868)"
24342,"(24342) Yazid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Sulayman al-Taymi, on the authority of Aminah; I heard Aisha say: Is it impossible for one of you to take water from the musk of her sacrifice every year? For the Messenger God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade or forbade the use of pure wine, imitated wines, and things that the Taymiyyah had forgotten."
24343,"(24343) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hassan bin Salih, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of a man; He asked Al-Hasan bin Ali about wine? He said: Drink, and if you fear that you will become drunk, let him."
24344,"(24344) Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, he said: I asked Muhammad about the wine from the water-carrier that is poured and suspended? He said: I don't know of any harm in it."
24345,"(24345) Khaled bin Harmala Al-Abdi told us, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Amr, the son of my brother Abi Nadhri. Did he ask Al-Hasan about dryness? He said: What is dryness? He said: A watering can on three pillars, with a hook from the top and the bottom. He said: There is no harm in it."
24346,"(24346) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Amr ibn Maymun, he said: Omar said: We are drinking this strong drink. We will crush the camel meat in our stomachs with it, lest it harm us. Whoever drinks any of it, let him mix it with water."
24347,"(24347) Waki’ told us, he said: Ismail bin Abi Khaled told us, on the authority of Qays bin Abi Hazim, he said: Tell me Utbah bin Farqad said: I came to Omar, so he called for some wine that had almost turned into vinegar, and he said: Drink, so I took it. So I drank it, and I was almost unable to swallow it. Then he took it and drank it, then said: Oh, `Utba, we are drinking this wine. It is severe that we will cut off the camel meat in our stomachs, lest they harm us."
24348,"(24348) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Hammam, who said: Omar was brought some raisin wine from... The Taif raisin wine. He said: When he tasted it, he frowned and said: The Taif raisin wine has a spike. Then he called for water and poured it over it. So he drank, and said: If it becomes too hard for you, pour water over it and drink."
24349,"(24349) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya ibn Sa’id, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab; A group of people from Thaqif met Omar bin Al-Khattab while he was near Mecca, so he invited them to bring their wine, so they brought him a cup of He brought wine to his mouth, then called for water and poured it over it two or three times, and said: Break it with water."
24350,"(24350) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Omar said: I am a man with a swollen stomach, or a swollen stomach. The stomach. I drink this fruit but it is not suitable for me. I drink this milk but it does not suit me. I drink this wine. It makes my stomach easier."
24351,"(24351) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Imran bin Muslim, on the authority of Suwaid bin Ghafla, who said: I was drinking wine with my father. Al-Darda' and the Companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in the Levant, in the great camps."
24352,"(24352) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Masruq, on the authority of Al-Shammas, who said: Abdullah said: The people will continue, even if Their drink is lawful until it becomes unlawful for them."
24353,"(24353) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Amr ibn Maymun, who said: When Omar was stabbed, the doctor came to him and said: Which drink do you like best? He said: wine."
24354,"(24354) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Abu Husayn, who said: I saw Zurr bin Hubaysh drinking wine. Al-Khawabiyya."
24355,"(24355) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hamid bin Sulaiman, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Aisha, she said: I used to reject the Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and I was taking a handful of raisins and throwing them in it."
24356,"(24356) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Mujalid, who said: Amer said: Drink the wedding wine, and do not become intoxicated by it."
24357,"(24357) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Issa bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, who said: I bear witness to The Badrians used to drink wedding wine."
24358,"(24358) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim Al-Taymi, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Dharr, he said: A drink of water, or a drink of wine, or a drink of milk is sufficient for me every day, and in all, a drink of Wheat"
24359,"(24359) Ali bin Musir told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Abdul-Malik, he said: I asked Ibn Umar about strong wine? He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was sitting in Mecca, then a man came to him and sat next to him, and he smelled a scent. Severe, so he said: What is this that you drank? He said: Wine. He said: Bring me some of it. He said: So he called for water and poured it over him and drank. Then he said: When I feel sorry for you. I gave you water to drink, so break it with water."
24360,"(24360) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, he said: I made food and invited Abdullah’s companions; Amr ibn Shurahbil, Abdullah ibn Dhib, Ammar, Muriya al-Hamdani, and Amr ibn Maymun, so I made them drink wine and decoction. So they drank, and Al-Amash said: I told him: Did they see the Khawabi? He said: Yes, they used to look at it and draw water from it."
24361,"(24361) Hafs told us, on the authority of Jafar, on the authority of his father; He used to drink wine, and he would give up his lunch and drink it in the evening."
24362,"(24362) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Abu Hayyan, on the authority of Yusuf, who said: Al-Hasan was invited to the wedding, and he would drink from Their wine"
24363,"(24363) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, he said: I got married and invited Ali’s companions and Abdul’s companions. God, one of Ali’s companions; Amara bin Abd, Hubayra bin Yarim, Al-Harith Al-Awar, and among the companions of Abdullah; Alqamah bin Qays, Abd al-Rahman bin Zaid, and Abdullah bin Dhib, so I left for them in the tents, and they were They drink from it, so I said: Have they seen it? He said: Yes, they look at it."
24364,"(24364) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan ibn Salih, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu Ja’far, who said: Wine is permissible."
24365,"(24365) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Sufyan Al-Attar, who said: A man asked what constitutes Hanafi, and he said: O Abu Salem, What do you say about wine? He said: I say regarding wine: He who forbids what God has made lawful is like he who has made lawful what God has forbidden."
24366,"(24366) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Jariri, on the authority of Abu Al-Ala, who said: This is the saying of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Peace and blessings of God be upon him regarding drinks until he said: Do not drink that which spoils your dreams, or that which destroys your wealth."
24367,"(24367) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Muhammad; He only used to drink water from water-filled water."
24368,"(24368) Malazem bin Amr told us, on the authority of Ujaiba bin Abdul Hamid, on the authority of his uncle Qais bin Talq, on the authority of his father Talq Ibn Ali, he said: We sat with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, then the delegation of Abdul Qais came and said: What is the matter with you? It has turned yellow. Your colours, your bellies are great, and your veins are visible? He said: They said: Our master came to you and asked you about a drink that was agreeable to us, but you forbade it, and we were in a protected land. He said: So drink what pleases you. (Tabarani 8256)"
24369,"(24369) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: There is no good in wine if it is sweet."
24370,"(24370) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Sa’id bin Masruq, who said: A man invited us to a meal and we ate, then he came to us. With a drink, so the people drank and I did not drink. He said: Then Bakr, meaning the son of a goat, looked at me with a look that I thought was one of its possessions."
24371,"(24371) Zaid narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If you enter upon your brother and ask him about his drink, then There was wine from a drinker, so he drank."
24372,"(24372) Ubaidah bin Hamid narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Miskin, on the authority of Huzayl bin Sharhabeel, who said: Omar bin Al-Khattab came to Thaqif, so he asked them to drink, and they said: Hide your wine. So they gave him water to drink, and he said: Give me some of your wine to drink. A group of Thaqif. He said: They gave it to drink. He ordered the boy to pour it, then he held it in his hand. Then he said: O people of Thaqif, you are You are drinking from this strong drink. Whoever of you has spilled any of his drink, let him break it with water."
24373,"(24373) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Aswad, who said: Abdullah used to reject him in the genitive case. The green one"
24374,"(24374) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Mujalid bin Abi Rashid, who said: Amr bin Harith entered Ali. Abdullah was performing a pilgrimage, he said: Then Abdullah said: O maidservant, give us wine to drink, so she made him drink from a green jar."
24375,"(24375) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Khalid bin Saad, on the authority of the mother of a son of Abu Masoud Al-Ansari, who said: I used to renounce Abu Masoud in the green jar."
24376,"(24376) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Harith Al-Taymi, on the authority of Umm Ma’abad, he said: She said: O my son, indeed Muharram God has made lawful, just as He makes lawful what God has forbidden, for I used to offer wine to Qarza bin Ka’b, and he was a man to whom God had bestowed good. Often, the companions of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, would give him water to drink, and he would be covered by them; Muadh bin Jabal and Zayd bin Arqam, in the false dān and the green genitive case."
24377,"(24377) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Hakim, on the authority of his mother; That Abu Barzah used to see his family abandoning the jirr, but he did not forbid them."
24378,"(24378) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Muslim, who said: Ibn Abi Awfa used to drink green draft wine."
24379,"(24379) Muhammad bin Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Umm Musa, she said: I used to renounce Ali in the green jar."
24380,"(24380) Ismail bin Aliyah told us, on the authority of Abu Harun al-Ghanawi, on the authority of Abu Majliz, who said: Qais bin He gave some people among the Qurā’ slaves food, then he gave them wine to drink, then he said: Do you know what wine I made you drink? They said: Yes, you gave us wine to drink. He said: No, but it is the wine of Jarar, or Jarar. Then he set off for Maqil bin Yasar. He said: So he said: What is recommended to you? So he called the maid, and she brought a green tow, and he said: This will be rejected for me."
24381,"(24381) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Thalabi, he said: I entered upon Anas bin Malik, so we ate with him, then he called for a green pitcher containing wine, and we gave us something to drink."
24382,"(24382) Muhammad bin Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Hammam, who said: He used to renounce Abdullah. The wine was put in green jars and he drank it, and he used to put wine in green jars for Asama bin Zayd and he drank it."
24383,"(24383) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Amr, on the authority of Shaqiq, who said: Ibn Masoud used to be rejected in The green jar, and a brother was drinking wine in the green jar."
24384,"(24384) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abdullah, Abu Masoud, and Asama: They were drinking draft wine."
24385,"(24385) Muhammad bin Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Ziyad, who said: I saw Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Layla. He drinks green draft wine after the boil has subsided."
24386,"(24386) Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Farwa, who said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla gave me drink in a jar. It is green, and there is something earthy in it, and I watered it from it."
24387,"(24387) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Farwa al-Janni, on the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Abd God, he said: He was drinking green ale wine."
24388,"(24388) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, who said: Amr ibn Shurahbil used to renounce religion, and renounce In the green preposition."
24389,"(24389) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, who said: Ibn Al-Hanafi used to drink green grape wine."
24390,"(24390) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Hamran bin Abdul Aziz, he said: Umm Hafs narrated to me, she said: I was I denounce Imran bin Husayn in Jarr. (Ibn Saad 290)"
24391,"(24391) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn al-Muntashir, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Masruq; He was drinking wine."
24392,"(24392) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn, who said: I entered upon Ibrahim, Al-Shu’bi, and Hilal bin Yassaf. Shaqiq and Sa`id bin Jubayr were in their homes, and I saw them drinking green draft wine."
24393,"(24393) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of al-Hasan bin Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of al-Aswad; He invited them to his wedding, and made them drink green wine. He said: And Abraham invited them to his wedding. So He gives them to drink in green jars."
24394,"(24394) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’ba, on the authority of Malik ibn Dinar, on the authority of Abu Rafi’; He was drinking wine."
24395,"(24395) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, who said: I said to Abraham: We reject the green genitive in the genitive case, then add it in the genitive case. The measured flask, or in the measured vessel? He said: There is no harm in it."
24396,"(24396) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hamran bin Abdul Aziz, who said: Umm Hafs Sariyya Imran bin Husayn told me, She said: I used to go to Imran bin Husayn in the green jar and he would drink it."
24397,"(24397) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ali bin Malik, on the authority of Al-Dahhak; He was drinking Al-Suwaiq wine."
24398,"(24398) Yahya bin Adam told us, on the authority of Abu Awani, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of his brother Isa, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla said: I used to drink wine from green jars with the Badriyah, one of the companions of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace."
24399,"(24399) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Ghaylan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Zayd, he said: I saw Abu Ubaidah bin Abdullah bin Masoud drank wine from a green bowl, and said: What is forbidden is what God has made lawful, like what is lawful is what God has made lawful. God forbids"
24400,"(24400) Marwan bin Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Amr, who said: I drank wine with Abraham at the house of Abraham. green"
24401,"(24401) Abd al-Samad bin Abd al-Warith narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Abu al-Mughirah, on the authority of his father; That Abu Barzah used to be abandoned in a green jar."
24402,"(24402) Abdul-Samad told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salma, on the authority of Abdul-Rahman bin Abi Rafi’; That his father used to reject him in the desert, so he used to drink it sweet from the stalk."
24403,"(24403) Khalaf bin Khalifa told us, on the authority of Al-Ala’ bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Hakim bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was presented in a green jar. (Tabarani 7428)"
24404,"(24404) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Dahhak bin Yasar, on the authority of Yazid bin Abdullah bin Al-Shakhir, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Suhar, on the authority of his father, he said: I said: O Messenger of God, I am a sick man, so he gave me permission to take a turban in which I may withdraw from it. So he gave me permission. Why? 
(Ahmed 31. Bazzar 2910)"
24405,"(24405) Abu Asama told us, he said: Mis’ar told us, on the authority of Sahil Abi Al-Asad, on the authority of Mushad, he said: It was Saad’s wine. In green streams, he said: And he said: Do not say: Give me water, broken."
24406,"(24406) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Simak bin Harb, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Abdul Rahman, he said: My father’s mother narrated to me. Ubaydah, or Umm Ubaydah, said that they were throwing themselves into the green jar, but Abdullah saw them and did not forbid them from doing so. That is (Abdul Razzaq 16953)"
24407,"(24407) Saul bin Yusuf narrated to us, on the authority of Hamid al-Tawil, on the authority of Uqba bin Misra, who said: We were at Maqil bin He left and called for food and we ate, then a cup of wine was brought to us and he drank and we drank, until he came to a son of his own, but he refused. To drink, so Maqil took a stick that he had and hit his head with it, making him angry, then said to him: Will you do such-and-such? And so on, and he mentioned some of its disadvantages: And you refuse to drink from a drink that your father and your paternal uncles drank, because it is bitter wine?"
24408,"(24408) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Mishaj ibn Musa, who said: I was staying at Anas’ house, and I saw him drinking wine. In a green genitive."
24409,"(24409) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Zayd, he said: Asim bin Bhadla narrated to me, saying: I met men who were This night they will take a camel, drink the wine of the draft, and wear saffron clothing. Among them is a button-down, and Abu Wael."
24410,"(24410) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, that he used to drink wine for three days."
24411,"(24411) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Abdul-Rahman, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Burda, Meaning Ibn Nayyar, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: Drink under the circumstances, and do not get drunk.
(Nasa’i 5187. Tabarani 22)"
24412,"(24412) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Yahya bin al-Harith al-Taymi, on the authority of Amr bin Amir, on the authority of Anas, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade wine in these circumstances. Then he said: I forbid you from wine. So drink as you wish, whoever wishes may be given to drink for sin."
24413,"(24413) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Sinan, on the authority of Muharib, on the authority of Ibn Buraydah, on the authority of his father, he said: The Messenger said: God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: He forbade you from drinking wine except as something to drink from, so drink all of it from something to drink, and do not Intoxicating"
24414,"(24414) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Amr bin Amir, on the authority of Anas, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade May God bless him and grant him peace from spreading food in vessels, and then he said: I have forbidden you from spreading food in vessels. So drink as you wish, whoever wishes may be given to drink for sin."
24415,"(24415) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Suleiman, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Abu Iyad, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr He said: It was said to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: Not everyone can find a container, so he gave them permission to take some of it, meaning Circumstances (Bukhari 5931, Muslim 66)"
24416,"(24416) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Ali bin Zayd, on the authority of Rabi’a bin Al-Nabighi, On the authority of his father, on the authority of Ali, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: I had forbidden you from these vessels, So drink from it, and avoid everything that intoxicates."
24417,"(24417) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Yahya bin al-Harith al-Taymi, on the authority of Yahya bin Ghassan. Al-Taimiyi, on the authority of Ibn Al-Rasim, and he was a man from the people of Hijr, and he was a jurist who narrated hadith on the authority of his father; He went to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, with a delegation in charity, carrying it to him. He said: So he forbade them from Wine in these circumstances, so they returned to their land, and the land of Tehama is hot, so they took advantage of it, so they returned to it. The second year in their alms, they said: O Messenger of God, you forbade us from these vessels, so we left them, and the That is upon us, so he said: Go and drink whatever you wish. Whoever wishes may be given to drink for sin. (Ahmad 3/481, Tabarani 4634)"
24418,"(24418) A`far ibn Sa`d narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade Peace be upon him about the circumstances, so the Ansar complained to him, and they said: We have no containers for him, so he said: No permission.
(Bukhari 592. Tirmidhi 1870)"
24419,"(24419) Zayd ibn Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad, he said: Farqad al-Sabkhi narrated to us, he said: Jabir ibn Zayd narrated to us, He said: Masruq told us, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I forbade you from this. The vessels, and the vessels do not make anything permissible, nor do they prohibit anything, so drink from them."
24420,"(24420) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Tariq bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: All Everything that is forbidden is forbidden in every circumstance is permissible."
24421,"(24421) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Sa’id al-Bajli, on the authority of Abu al-Sha’atha’ al-Kindi, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: I heard him say: Vessels do not make anything permissible, nor do they make anything forbidden."
24422,"(24422) Abdi narrated to us, on the authority of Salih, on the authority of Al-Shu’abi, he said: Wine made from sickle is more severe than wine made from wine, and no vessel is forbidden, nor It is better"
24423,"(24423) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, saying: Ismail bin Abi Khalid narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zubayr bin Adiy, he said: It was mentioned when Shurayh refers to the water in which one is rejected. Shurayh said: They do not make anything lawful, nor do they make anything unlawful, but look at what You make therein lawful or unlawful."
24424,"(24424) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khalid, on the authority of a man from Bani Bujayla, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: Each Everything that is forbidden is forbidden in every circumstance is permissible."
24425,"(24425) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Sami’, on the authority of Muslim Al-Batin, he said: I asked Abu Amr Al-Shaybani about beer? He said: A drink made from barley in Yemen."
24426,"(24426) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abi Ismail, on the authority of Ammar bin Asim, on the authority of Anas, who said: Al-Hantam is a jarar. Hamar, she used to come to us from Egypt."
24427,"(24427) Ibn Numayr and Waki’ told us on the authority of Al-Salt ibn Bahram. He said: I asked Ibrahim about Al-Hanatam? He said: They were red jars, boiled, brought from the Levant, and they are called: Al-Hantam."
24428,"(24428) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Harith Al-Taymi, on the authority of Umm Ma’bad, he said: I said: What he said about this The vessels? She said: Ali Al-Kabeer, it fell. As for the hantam, it is the hantam of foreigners, into which a man enters and sweeps it thoroughly: Adverbs Wine, and as for the tambourines, they are gourds, and as for the pure wines, they are the skins whose hollows are measured, and whose hairs are colored with pitch: Adverbs Wine, and as for the naqir, it is the palm tree whose roots are firm in the ground, dug up."
24429,"(24429) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Muslim, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Layla, who said: The hanatems were only jars. They are made of clay, brought from Egypt, but not in green jars."
24430,"(24430) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Layla, who said: Al-Hantam is a green jar. He was bringing it from Egypt, and it contained wine."
24431,"(24431) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: Al-Hantam al-Jarar All of them"
24432,"(24432) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq Al-Shaybani, he said: I said to Abu Burda: What are the items? He said: honey wine, and ale is barley wine."
24433,"(24433) Muhammad bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Sufyan bin Hussein, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Ibn Sirin. He said: I asked them about Wine in bullets? His thoughts"
24434,"(24434) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Al-Mukhtar, he said: I asked Anas, and I said: The flask and the bullets? He said: There is nothing wrong with them, so I said: What do people say? He said: Leave what confuses you for what does not confuse you."
24435,"(24435) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abu Salamah, he said: I came while they were mentioning the wine of the draft at Ikrimah, and a person asked him about lead? He said: That is more malicious or more evil."
24436,"(24436) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Aban bin Sam’a, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he hated bullets."
24437,"(24437) Muhammad bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Ashhab Ja’far bin Al-Harith Al-Nakha’i, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, he said : I asked Ibn Abbas about lead wine? So he gave me permission to do that, and my grandfather had a leaden jar that he would throw away."
24438,"(24438) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Ala bin Al-Musayyab, he said: I saw Ibrahim, Khaythami, and Al-Musayyab bin They bring with them wine in lead, which they drink."
24439,"(24439) Ismail Ibn Aliyya told us, on the authority of Khalid Al-Hadha’, who said: Abu Qalababi used to water drinks for him. Then he turns it into a blanket of lead."
24440,"(24440) Al-Fadl narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Khalda, he said: Ghailan bin Umairah narrated to me, he said: I met Ibn Umar, so I asked him About drinks? So he gave me permission to shoot."
24441,"(24441) Abu Khaled told us, not in Al-Ahmar, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Al-Hikam; He was being rejected by bullets."
24442,"(24442) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Bakr; He used to throw it into bottles."
24443,"(24443) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Aban bin Sam’a, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He gave permission for glass, meaning wine."
24444,"(24444) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Marouf bin Wasil, who said: My mother narrated to me, on the authority of a woman, who is called: a girl. Al-Aqsa', and she was a daughter-in-law of Abdullah bin Omar. She brought green grapes to Ibn Omar, and he said: What is this? She said: We reject this, so Ibn Umar inserted his hand into its stomach and said: I have appointed for you to drink from it, for it is only It is like a bottle."
24445,"(24445) Abu Dawud Al-Tayalisi told us, on the authority of Al-Hakam bin Atiyya, who said: I saw Muhammad drinking from bottles."
24446,"(24446) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Hakim, on the authority of his mother, on the authority of Abu Barzah; He hated drinking from glasses."
24447,"(24447) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Al-Mukhtar bin Falfil, he said: I asked Anas and said: The bottle and the bullet? He said: There is nothing wrong with them. I said: What do people say? He said: Leave what confuses you for what does not confuse you."
24448,"(24448) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Amr, who said: I came to Sa’id bin Jubayr with a green jar. So he put his hand into it, and I said: Shall we reject it? He said: Yes, it is in the same place as the bottle."
24449,"(24449) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Hasan ibn Amr, who said: I drank with Abraham three bottles of wine"
24450,"(24450) Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Nadr bin Mutarrif, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of his father, he said: Abdullah used to throw a hole in the ground for him, and make a den for him there."
24451,"(24451) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Khalid bin Al-Mu’adil, on the authority of Ibn Umar; Omar was brought some wine from the Levant, so he drank from it and said: Have you made it less turbid?"
24452,"(24452) Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman told us, on the authority of Abu Farwa, who said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla gave me drink. It is a strong wine that contains bitterness, and I made it drink from it."
24453,"(24453) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Wael, he said: He used to give us wine to drink that offended us. The smell of my heart."
24454,"(24454) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, who said: I asked Abu Ja`far about the rupee. He said: What is the rupee? I said: Al-Dardi. He said: There is no problem with it."
24455,"(24455) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim; He used to reject paint and put dirt on it."
24456,"(24456) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Salih, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Amr, on the authority of Ibrahim, and Al-Shu’abi; They used to add bitter wine to their wine."
24457,"(24457) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Muhammad, that they used to live in Al-Akrah."
24458,"(24458) Yazeed bin Harun told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab; He hated turbidity."
24459,"(24459) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab: He hated Al-Akr and said: He Wine"
24460,"(24460) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Aroub, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Anas; That Abu Ubaidah, Muadh bin Jabal, and Abu Talha used to drink from the paint, two-thirds of it was gone and one-third remained."
24461,"(24461) Abdul Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Dawud bin Abi Hind, who said: I asked Saeed bin Al-Musayyab about drinking. Who did Omar ibn Al-Khattab grant to people? He said: It is the paint that was cooked until two-thirds of it was gone and one-third remained."
24462,"(24462) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Maymun, on the authority of Umm Al-Darda’, she said: I used to cook for Abu Al-Darda’. Two-thirds of it went away, and a third of it remained to drink."
24463,"(24463) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Maimun, on the authority of Umm al-Darda’, on the authority of Abu al-Darda’; He used to drink some of the paint, one-third of it was gone and one-third remained."
24464,"(24464) Waki’ ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, on the authority of Aban ibn Abdullah al-Bajli, on the authority of a man who named him. He said: He was Ali. He provides people with paint: two-thirds of it is gone and one-third remains."
24465,"(24465) Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Amr, on the authority of Fudhail bin Amr, who said: I said to Ibrahim: What What do you think about the paint? He said: Two-thirds of it has not gone and a third of it has remained, and I do not see any harm in the just person."
24466,"(24466) Waki` told us, on the authority of Bashir ibn al-Muhajir, on the authority of al-Hasan, who said: Drink what two-thirds of it has gone and remains. a third"
24467,"(24467) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Saad bin Aws, on the authority of Anas bin Sirin, who said: Anas bin Malik was sick with a sick stomach. So he ordered me to cook food for him until two-thirds of it was gone and a third of it remained, and he used to drink from it as a result. Food"
24468,"(24468) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Hakim ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Drink some of the paint. Two-thirds are gone and one-third remain."
24469,"(24469) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ali bin Ata’, who said: I heard a Bedouin asking Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab about Paint on half? He hated him and said: You should use milk."
24470,"(24470) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Abi Layla, and Abu Juhayfy, They said: Ali used to provide us with paint. He said: I said: How was he? He said: We used to serve it with bread and drink it with water."
24471,"(24471) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Ali bin Sulaym, who said: I heard Anas say: I drink sweet paint. The biting"
24472,"(24472) Hammad bin Khaled told us, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Salih, on the authority of Salem bin Salem, who said: I entered upon my father in front of him while he was drinking. The beauty of the Lord"
24473,"(24473) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail bin Khalid, on the authority of Uthman bin Qays, who said: I went out with Jarir on the day of Friday. To a bathroom for him with aqul, so we were brought with food and we ate, then we were brought with honey and paint, and Jarir said: Drink the honey, you. He drank the paint and said: He will be disapproved of by you, but he will not be disapproved of by me. I said: What kind of paint is it? He said: I used to smell his scent in that place, and he gestured with his hand to the furthest reaches of the people."
24474,"(24474) Abdullah bin Numayr narrated to us, saying: Ismail bin Abi Khalid narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Mughirah bin Al-Muntashir Ibn My brother Masruq said: I told him: Was Masruq drinking paint? He said: Yes, he used to cook it and then drink it."
24475,"(24475) Ibn Numayr told us, he said: Ismail told us, on the authority of Abu Jarir, on the authority of Al-Nadr bin Anas, he said: Abu Ghaza Ubaidah ibn al-Jarrah came to the land of the Levant, and it was said to Abu Ubaidah: Here is a drink that Christians drink during their fast. He said: Then Abu Ubaidah drank from it."
24476,"(24476) Ibn Numayr told us, he said: Ismail told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Shuraih; That Khalid bin Al-Walid used to drink paint in the Levant."
24477,"(24477) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Yahya bin Ubaid Abi Umar, who said: It was mentioned by Ibn Abbas. Al-Talaa’, and they mentioned cooking it, so Ibn Abbas said: Fire does not make anything permissible, nor does it make it unlawful because the beginning of it was lawful."
24478,"(24478) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Shuraih; He used to drink strong paint."
24479,"(24479) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ali bin Badhima, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah; He used to drink paint at Marwan's, which made his cheeks red."
24480,"(24480) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim; He used to buy paint from someone who did not know who made it, and then drink it."
24481,"(24481) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Suddi, on the authority of a sheikh from the Hadramis, who said: Ali distributed some paint for me, so he sent me a measure of We used to eat it with bread just as we used to eat it with kameh."
24482,"(24482) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Musa bin Abdullah bin Yazid Al-Ansari, he said: It was Abd al-Rahman bin Bishr al-Ansari had a village where he would prepare food, so he called some of his companions and they ate, then they were brought with drink. Of the paint, and among them were people from the people of Badr, so they said: What is this? They said: A drink that the son of man made for himself. They said: This is a man who does not refuse to drink, so they drank."
24483,"(24483) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Abu Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Ali, who said: He used to provide us with paint. So I said to him: What is your situation? He said: Black. One of us took it with his finger."
24484,"(24484) Muhammad bin Bishr told us, he said: Abdullah bin Al-Walid Al-Muzani told us, he said: Abdul-Malik bin Umair, on the authority of Abu Al-Hajjaj; Al-Hajjaj called him and said: Show me Omar’s letter to Ammar about the paint. He went out and was sad, and Al-Shu’abi met him and asked him. So he told him what Al-Hajjaj had said to him, and Al-Sha’bi said to him: “Get a book and a medicine. By God, what I heard from your father.” Except for one time, so he dictated to him: In the name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful, from Abdullah Umar, Commander of the Faithful, to Ammar bin Yasser, now: I was brought a drink from the Levant, so I asked about it: How is it made? So they told me that they cook it until two-thirds of it is gone and a third of it remains. If that is done, it will go away. His head and the fragrance of his madness, and the unlawful has gone and the lawful has remained. Abdullah said: And I see him said: And the perfume from it, so if This book of mine has come to you, so it passed by you, so that they may make room for it in your drinking water, and peace be upon you."
24485,"(24485) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of his father; Omar bin Abdul Aziz hated Al-Munsif, and he sent his message to the people of the cities."
24486,"(24486) Mu’tamar bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud bin Ibrahim, who said: I said to Tawoos: Have you seen this juice that Is it cooked by half, a third, and the like? He said: Have you seen this that is like honey? If you wish, you can eat bread with it, and if you wish, you can pour water on it and drink it. And anything other than it, do not drink it, do not sell it, and do not benefit from its price."
24487,"(24487) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Bashir bin Al-Muhajir, on the authority of Ikrimah and Al-Hasan, who said: Drink some of the paint. Two-thirds are gone and one-third remain."
24488,"(24488) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Burayd bin Abi Maryam, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, who said: We were We reject fresh and fresh foods at the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. When the prohibition of alcohol came down, we burned them from the ground. The vessels, then We left them. (Tahawi 213)"
24489,"(24489) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Najrani, he said: I said to Abdullah bin Omar: We are in a land with Dates and raisins, so can dates and raisins be mixed and we should reject them all? He said: No, I said: Why? He said: A man got drunk during the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the Prophet brought him while he was drunk, so he hit him. Then he asked him about his drink. He said: I drank wine. He said: What wine? He said: Date and raisin wine. He said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Do not mix them, for each one of them is It alone is sufficient. (Ahmad 25. Abu Ali 5756)"
24490,"(24490) Muhammad bin Bishr al-Abdi narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj bin Abi Uthman, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Qatada, on the authority of his father, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: Do not reject dates and raisins. All of them, and do not reject the fresh and the fresh, but reject each one of them separately. (Bukhari 5602. Muslim 24)"
24491,"(24491) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, he said: Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Abu Arta, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, he said: No. The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, on the authority of fresh fruits and dates, and on the authority of raisins and dates. (Ahmad 3/58, Abu Ali 1171)"
24492,"(2449) Ali bin Musahir told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade that dates and raisins be mixed together, and that peas and dates be mixed together. He wrote to the people of Jerash forbidding them from mixing dates and raisins. (Muslim 27 Ahmad 1/336)"
24493,"(24493) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade That dates and raisins should be rejected altogether, and all dates and dates should be rejected. (Bukhari 5601, Muslim 1574)"
24494,"(24494) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad, on the authority of Uqba bin Abdul Ghafir, he said: Abu Sa’id was Al-Khudri forbids combining dates and raisins."
24495,"(24495) Saul bin Yusuf told us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; He hated whole dates alone, and he hated combining them with dates, and he saw nothing wrong with dates and raisins. And he says: Both are permissible, combined or separated. He said: Al-Hasan used to hate combining dates and raisins."
24496,"(24496) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid told us, on the authority of Simak bin Musa Al-Dhabi, who said: I saw Anas bin Malik’s servant girl. You separate the guilt from the beauty, so you reject it as a limit, and you reject the sin as a limit."
24497,"(24497) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hatim bin Abi Saghira, on the authority of Abu Musab al-Madani, he said: I heard Abu Huraira says: When wine was forbidden, they used to take the brus and cut off every sinner from it, then the brus would be taken away. He spits it out, then drinks it."
24498,"(24498) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Muharib, on the authority of Jabir, who said: Al-Basr and dates are wine."
24499,"(24499) Ibn Idris and Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: A man asked Omar about Al-Fadikh, He said: What is Al-Fadikh? He said: Busr, which is ground and then mixed with dates. He said: That is sprinkling. He said: Wine is forbidden, and there is no drink other than it."
24500,"(24500) Abdul Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, who said: It is disliked to mix Peas and dates, raisins and dates."
24501,"(24501) Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Kaysan, who said: I asked Abu Al-Sha’atha’i Jabir bin Zaid about Al-Fasikh? He said: What is Al-Fadikh? I said: Al-Basr and dates, and he said: By God, for you to take water and boil it and put it in your stomach, is better than for you to combine them both. All in your belly."
24502,"(24502) Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, on the authority of Ash`ath, on the authority of Thabit bin Ubaid, who said: Abu Masoud al-Ansari used to command He commanded him to cut off the sinner from his sins, and each one of them would be rejected individually."
24503,"(24503) Affan bin Muslim narrated to us, saying: Al-Muthanna bin Awf narrated to us, saying: Abu Abdullah Al-Jasri narrated to us, on the authority of Ma’qil Ibn Yassar; Did he ask him about the drink? He said: We were in Medina and there were a lot of dates, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade us the old ones. He said: A man came to ask him about his mother. She had reached an age where she did not eat food. Should he give her wine to drink? He said: I said to him: O Maqil bin Yassar. He said: What did you order him to do? He said: I ordered him not to give her water to drink. (Tabarani 5050, Tayalisi 934)"
24504,"(24504) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Al-Taymiy, on the authority of Abu Nadhrah, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, he said: The Messenger forbade God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the authority of dates and raisins being mixed, and on the authority of dates and raisins that are mixed. (Muslim 20. Tirmidhi 1877)"
24505,"(24505) Yazeed bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, who said: We were in the house of Abu Talha. And with us were Suhail bin Baydha, Ubayy bin Ka’b, and Abu Ubaidah, and they were drinking something for themselves, when a herald called out Indeed, wine has been forbidden, so by God they did not see whether it was true or false until they said: O Anas, make up what is left in the vessel. So He sufficed him, and on that day, basts and dates. By God, they did not return therein until they met God. (Muslim 1570, Abu Dawud 3665)"
24506,"(24506) Muhammad bin Musab narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Abu Salama, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Do not combine fresh fruits and dates, raisins and dates, reject each one of them. On the one hand (Muslim 1576. Ibn Hibban 5381)"
24507,"(24507) Muawiyah bin Hisham told us, on the authority of Ammar bin Ruzaiq, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Abd Al-Rahman bin Abi Layla said: The man was passing by the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and they were present. So they curse him and say: This man drinks two mixtures: raisins and dates."
24508,"(24508) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Amr, on the authority of Adiy bin Thabit, on the authority of Al-Bara’ bin Azib; He was drinking paint on half of it."
24509,"(24509) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Talha ibn Jabr, who said: I saw Abu Juhayfa drinking paint on half of it."
24510,"(24510) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Jarir bin Ayyub, on the authority of Abi Zur’i bin Amr bin Jarir; Jarir used to drink it in half."
24511,"(24511) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman and Waki` told us, on the authority of Ubaidah, on the authority of Khaythami, on the authority of Anas; He used to drink it by half."
24512,"(24512) Yahya bin Yaman told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ja’far; Ibn Abza used to drink paint on half of his body."
24513,"(24513) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Al-Mundhir, on the authority of Ibn Al-Hanafiyyah; He used to drink the cooked paint, meaning what was half cooked."
24514,"(24514) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Al-Hakam, who said: Sharih used to drink the paint on half of it. He drank the paint Al-Shadeed, meaning the fair one."
24515,"(24515) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Ayoub, he said: I saw Abu Ubaidah drinking it for half."
24516,"(24516) Ibn Abi Ghani told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Qays, that he used to drink it in half."
24517,"(24517) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Dinar al-Araj, on the authority of Sa`id ibn Jubayr, who said: He drank paint on half of my property."
24518,(24518) Abu Muawiyah and Waki’ told us on the authority of Al-A’mash; That Abraham used to drink it in half.
24519,"(24519) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Yahya, he said: I saw him drinking paint on half of his body."
24520,"(24520) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Shuraih; He was drinking with the paint on half of it. He said: So he drank and gave me something to drink."
24521,"(24521) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim; He used to remove the paint from it and put dirt on it."
24522,"(24522) Ishaq bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Abu Sinan, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Al-Dahhak; He used to reject bakhtaj."
24523,"(24523) Ishaq bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Jabir, on the authority of Mujahid;"
24524,"(24524) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: There is no harm in Bakhtaj wine."
24525,"(24525) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abu Hujayr, who said: Al-Dahhak made us drink Bakhtaj wine."
24526,"(24526) Muhammad ibn Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, he said: Muhammad was asked about the fatih of basr alone? He said: I don't know what it is."
24527,"(24527) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hatim bin Abi Saghira, on the authority of Abu Musab al-Madani, he said: I heard Abu Huraira says: We used to take beer and shake it, then drink it."
24528,"(24528) A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Ikrimah; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, drank Al-Fadhikh at Al-Fadhikh Mosque. (Ahmad 2/106, Abu Ali 5707)"
24529,"(24529) Abu Dawud al-Talisi told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa`id bin al-Musayyab and al-Hasan, who said: No. It is unfortunate that the stalk is ruptured with what is in it."
24530,"(24530) Muhammad bin Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Mehsahaj, who said: I heard a man ordering his servant to cut dates from Basra, so each one of them should be rejected individually."
24531,"(24531) Abdul-Wahhab Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Ikrimah; He disliked the vulgar, even if it was pure."
24532,"(24532) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab, he said, There is no harm in sinning."
24533,"(24533) Muhammad bin Yazid told us, on the authority of Al-Nu’man bin Al-Mundhir, on the authority of Makhoul; He hated drinking water in which alcohol was added."
24534,"(24534) Muhammad bin Yazid told us, on the authority of Dawud bin Amr, on the authority of Makhoul, on the authority of Abu Darda’; The Prophet put wine in it. He said: There is no harm in it. It was slaughtered by the sun and salt."
24535,"(24535) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. And peace be upon him, he said: Whoever drinks alcohol in this world will not drink it in the hereafter, unless he repents. (Muslim 78. Ahmad 2/21)"
24536,"(24536) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: Whoever drinks alcohol and puts it in his stomach, his seven prayers will not be accepted, and if he dies in them, he dies as an unbeliever. If his mind departs from any of the obligatory duties, his prayers will not be accepted for forty days, and if he dies in them, he dies. An infidel (Nasa’i 5179. Tabarani 13492)"
24537,"(24537) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Ali ibn Ata’, on the authority of Hassan ibn Ubayy, and Jazia, on the authority of his father, On the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, he said: Because I commit adultery is more beloved to me than drinking alcohol. If I drink alcohol, I abandon prayer. Whoever abandons prayer has no debt."
24538,"(24538) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Al-Awwam ibn Hawshab, on the authority of Al-Musayyab ibn Rafi’, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Amr, he said : The one who drinks alcohol is like the one who worships Al-Lat and Al-Uzza."
24539,"(24539) Muhammad bin Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Wael bin Abi Bakr, on the authority of Abu Bakr, on the authority of Abu Burda, on the authority of Abu Musa, He used to say: I don’t care whether I drink wine or worship this woman instead of God."
24540,"(24540) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Suleiman bin Habib; Ibn Omar said: If I were to dip my finger into wine, I would not like it to come back to me."
24541,"(24541) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Urwah ibn Ruwaym, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: And peace be upon him: The first time my Lord forbade me; About drinking wine, worshiping idols, and having sex with men. (Abu Dawud 506)"
24542,"(24542) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, he said: Mis’ar narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Aoun, on the authority of Ibn Shaddad, he said: Ibn Abbas said: It was forbidden. Alcohol itself, whether small or large, and sugar from any drink."
24543,"(24543) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of his father; He heard Othman delivering a sermon, so he mentioned wine and said: It is the gathering of the evil ones, or it is the mother of the evil things, then he started He spoke about the Children of Israel and said: A man was given a choice between killing a boy, erasing a book, or drinking wine. So he chose wine and continued until he had finished it all.
(Ibn Hibban 5348, Bayhaqi 287)"
24544,"(24544) Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Talha, on the authority of Masruq, who said: The drinker of alcohol is like an idol worshiper."
24545,"(24545) Muhammad bin Sulaiman Al-Asbaani narrated to us, on the authority of Suhail, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: The alcoholic is like an idol worshiper. (Bukhari 386. Ibn Majah 3375)"
24546,"(24546) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Yahya bin Abbad bin Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr. On the authority of his father, he said: We were with Aisha, and a group of people passed by her door, and she heard the sound and said: What is this? They said: A man who was drunk with alcohol. She said: Glory be to God. I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: The adulterer shall not commit adultery. When he commits adultery while he is a believer, and he does not drink alcohol when he drinks while he is a believer, and a thief does not steal when he steals while he is a believer. Beware, beware of you."
24547,"(24547) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: The fornicator does not commit adultery when he commits adultery while he is a believer, and he does not steal when he steals while he is a believer. He is a believer, and he does not drink alcohol when he drinks it while he is a believer, and he does not deviate from it. People will raise their eyes to it. And he is a believer.
(Nasa’i 7126)"
24548,"(24548) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mudrik, on the authority of Ibn Abi Awfa, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: He does not drink alcohol if he drinks it while he is a believer."
24549,"(24549) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He forbade giving the animals wine to drink."
24550,"(24550) Abd Allah bin Sulayman told us, on the authority of Ubad Allah bin Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He heard that women were combing themselves with wine, so he said: May God cast the harvest on their heads."
24551,"(24551) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Abu al-Saffar, on the authority of his wife; That Aisha was asked about a woman combing her hair with honey while she had alcohol in her? She forbade that in the strongest terms."
24552,"(24552) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Hudhayfah, who said: Do you comb your hair with wine? May God bless her"
24553,"(24553) Khalaf bin Khalifa told us, on the authority of Abu Hashim, on the authority of Nafi’, who said: It was owned by Ibn Omar Bakhtiya, and it She fell ill and it was prescribed for me to treat her with wine, so I treated her, then I said to Ibn Umar: They prescribed for me to treat her. With wine, he said: So you did? I said: No, and I had done so. He said: If you had done so, I would have punished you."
24554,"(24554) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, who said: He does not enter The jinn is addicted to alcohol, is not disobedient, or is ungrateful. (Nasa’i 5182. Ahmad 2/164)"
24555,"(24555) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Salem bin Abi al-Ja’d, And Mujahid, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: No disobedient person will enter Paradise, nor Addicted, and there is no remorse. (Bayhaqi 7874)"
24556,"(24556) Yahya bin Ishaq narrated to us, saying: Yahya bin Ayyub informed us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Zuhar, on the authority of Bakr bin Sawada, on the authority of Qais bin Saad bin Ubadah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Indeed, my Lord has forbidden me Wine, cups, and qinān, meaning the oud. Then he said: Beware of dust, for they are the wine of the world. (Ahmad 3/422, Bayhaqi 222)"
24557,"(24557) Muhammad bin Bishr told us, he said: Abdul Aziz told us, he said: Nafi’ told me, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: A prohibition was revealed. Wine: Indeed, in Medina there are five drinks which they call wine, but none of them contain grape wine. (Bukhari 4616. Muslim 32)"
24558,"(24558) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaddad, he said: When he was captured By the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he was brought with an animal until he came to the Holy House, and two vessels were brought; In one was wine, and in another was milk. So he took the milk, and Gabriel said to him: You have been guided, and your nation has been guided. (Ibn Jarir 15)"
24559,"(24559) Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Wael bin Dawud al-Taymi, on the authority of Ibrahim al-Taymi, who said: He said: Al-Ash'ari: It is more beloved to me to pray for a woman than to drink alcohol."
24560,"(24560) Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Ashhab, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: He said: I am not happy that I drank a vessel of wine, and that I gave the same gold in charity."
24561,"(24561) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Qays, on the authority of Makhoul, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, recommended Some of my family advised them not to drink alcohol, as drinking it is the key to all evil."
24562,"(24562) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hayyan, he said: Abu Al-Furat informed me, on the authority of Abu Dawud, he said: I was At the pulpit of Hudhayf while he was in the cities, he thanked God and praised him, then said: As for what follows, the seller of wine and its drinker There is equality in sin."
24563,"(24563) Shababā narrated to us, he said: Shu‘bā narrated to us, on the authority of Zubaid, on the authority of Khathāmī; He heard him say: I was sitting with Abdullah bin Amr, and he mentioned major sins and even mentioned alcohol, so it was as if he was a man. He neglected it, and Abdullah bin Amr said: No man drinks it in the morning except that he remains a polytheist until the evening."
24564,"(24564) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Al-Nu’man bin Abi Ayyash, who said: We were sent to Abdullah bin Amr, we ask him about which of the sins is the greatest? He said: Wine, so we brought the Messenger back to him, and he said: Wine. Whoever drinks it, seven prayers will not be accepted from him. If he gets drunk, his prayers will not be accepted. His prayers will be accepted for forty days, and if he dies in those days, he dies the death of ignorance."
24565,"(24565) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sa’id bin Abdul Aziz narrated to us, on the authority of Rabi’i bin Yazid, on the authority of Ibn Al-Dailami said: I asked Abdullah bin Amr about the drinker of alcohol? He said: His prayer will not be accepted for forty days or forty nights."
24566,"(24566) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan; In love, a drop of wine or blood falls into it. He said: spilling."
24567,"(24567) Ismail Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Al-Taymi, on the authority of Umm Harash; She saw Ali dyeing himself with wine vinegar."
24568,"(24568) Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Salih, on the authority of Abu al-Zahariyy, on the authority of Jubayr bin Nufayr, he said: Two men from Muadh’s companions disagreed about vinegar, so they asked Abu Darda’? He said: There is no harm in it."
24569,"(24569) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Misrbil Al-Abdi, on the authority of his mother, she said: I asked Aisha Regarding wine vinegar, she said: There is nothing wrong with it, it is good."
24570,"(24570) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Nafi’, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He saw no harm in eating what had been wine but then it turned into vinegar."
24571,"(24571) Azhar told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, he said: Muhammad did not say: vinegar is wine, but he used to say: vinegar grapes, and he He gets dyed in it."
24572,"(24572) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Hammad ibn Zayd, on the authority of Yahya ibn Atiq, on the authority of Ibn Sirin; He saw nothing wrong with vinegar."
24573,"(24573) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abdul-Malik, who said: I saw Saeed bin Jubayr dyeing himself with vinegar. Wine"
24574,"(24574) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Mubarak, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: There is no harm in stinginess of wine."
24575,"(24575) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Suddi, on the authority of Yahya bin Abbad, on the authority of Anas; That Abu Talha asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, about orphans who inherited wine, should he make it vinegar? His thoughts (Abu Dawud 3667, Ahmed 119)"
24576,"(24576) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Muthanna bin Sa’id, who said: I witnessed Omar bin Abdul Aziz writing to his agent through an intermediary. Do not carry wine from one village to another, and whatever you find, make it vinegar."
24577,"(24577) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of al-Qasim, on the authority of Aslam, who said: Omar said: There is no problem. You found it miserly with the People of the Book, unless you knew that they deliberately spoiled it after it had turned into wine."
24578,"(24578) Yahya bin Zakariya bin Abi Zaydi told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: There is no harm in transferring Wine is vinegar."
24579,"(24579) Ibn Uyaynah and Hafs told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: I gave food to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. He took medicine from Zamzam, so he drank it while standing. (Muslim 1602. Ahmad 220)"
24580,"(24580) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Muslim, who said: I saw Ibn Umar standing while drinking."
24581,"(24581) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Abu Sinan, on the authority of Abu Al-Ma’arik, he said: I asked Abu Hurairah about a man’s drinking. And he is standing? He said: There is no harm in it."
24582,"(24582) Hatim bin Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Jafar, on the authority of his father; That Ali was drinking while standing."
24583,"(24583) Mu’ammar narrated to us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, that Sa’d and Aisha saw no harm in drinking while standing."
24584,"(24584) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Ibn Omar; He drank from a water bottle while standing."
24585,"(24585) Muhammad bin Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Misra, who said: I saw Ali standing while drinking, so I said: Did you drink anything? He said: If I drink while standing, I have seen the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, drinking standing, and if I drink while sitting, I will I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, drinking while sitting. (Ahmad 1/114)"
24586,"(24586) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amer; He saw Ibn Umar standing while drinking."
24587,"(24587) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abbad bin Mansour, who said: I saw Salim drinking while standing."
24588,"(24588) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Ajlan, who said: I asked Ibrahim about him? He said: There is no problem with him, if you wish, he can stand, or if you wish, he can sit."
24589,"(24589) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Mujalid, who said: I saw Al-Shaabi drinking, standing and sitting."
24590,"(24590) Abdul Rahman bin Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Waqid, on the authority of Zazan, he said: There is no harm in drinking while standing. Sitting is a dream."
24591,"(24591) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Al-Hakam, on the authority of Al-Hurr bin Sayyah, who said: A man asked Ibn Umar and he said: What do you think? When drinking while standing? Ibn Omar said: I drink while standing, and I eat while walking."
24592,"(24592) Muadh bin Muadh told us, on the authority of Imran bin Hudayr, on the authority of Yazid bin Atarid Abi Al-Buzri, he said: Ibn Umar said: We used to drink while standing, and eat while walking, in accordance with the covenant of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. (Ahmed 2/29)"
24593,"(24593) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Misra, who said: I asked Tawoos and Sa`id ibn Jubayr. About drinking while standing? He saw no harm in it."
24594,"(24594) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Tell me who saw Ali With a cup of coffee, he drinks while standing."
24595,"(24595) Khaled ibn Mukhlid narrated to us, on the authority of Malik ibn Anas, on the authority of Aamir ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubair, who said: I saw my father drinking. And He is standing."
24596,"(24596) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: We used to drink while standing, and we would eat. We follow the covenant of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. (Ahmad 1080, Darami 2126)"
24597,"(24597) Yahya bin Yaman told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Abi Sulaiman, he said: Saeed bin Jubayr said to me: Drink while standing."
24598,"(24598) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Sharik, on the authority of Bishr bin Ghalib, who said: I saw Al-Hussein drinking while he was Standing"
24599,"(24599) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham al-Dastawai, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Abu Issa al-Aswari, on the authority of Abu Sa`id. Al-Khudri said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, rebuked a man who drank while standing. (Muslim 114; Abu Ali 984)"
24600,"(24600) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham al-Dastawai, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of God forbade May God bless him and grant him peace from drinking while standing. (Muslim 1601. Abu Dawud 3710)"
24601,"(24601) Mu`tamar narrated to us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Anas; He asked him about drinking while standing? His thoughts"
24602,"(24602) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He used to hate drinking while standing."
24603,"(24603) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: He disliked drinking while standing for a reason. He takes the stomach."
24604,"(24604) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade And he is safe from drinking from the mouths of the watery. (Musnad 544)"
24605,"(24605) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah bin Utba, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, who said: A man drank from a watering can and a demon entered his stomach, so the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade it. He denied the circumcision of the water bodies. (Muslim 110. Abu Dawud 3713)"
24606,"(24606) Yunus bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Qatadah, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade drinking from waterskins."
24607,"(24607) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade May God bless him and grant him peace from drinking from waterskins."
24608,"(24608) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Ibn Bint Anas Ibn Malik, on the authority of Anas; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered upon Umm Sulaim and there were waterskins hanging in the house, so he drank from them while standing. (Ahmad 6/376. Tabarani 25)"
24609,"(24609) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; He did not see any harm in drinking from the water."
24610,"(24610) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr, who said: I saw Ibn Umar drinking from the water. The medicine"
24611,"(24611) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Rawwad, on the authority of Nafi’; That Ibn Omar used to drink from the water-task."
24612,"(24612) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abbad bin Mansour, who said: I saw Salim bin Abdullah drinking from the water container."
24613,"(24613) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Zayd bin Abdullah bin Omar, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Abd al-Rahman Ibn Abi Bakr, on the authority of Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Peace and blessings of God be upon him: He who eats and drinks from vessels of gold and silver is only engulfed in his belly by fire. Hell (Muslim 1434, Ahmad 6/306)"
24614,"(24614) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Zaid bin Abdullah bin Omar, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abdul Rahman bin Abi Bakr, on the authority of Umm Salama, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace; Like him"
24615,"(24615) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulayman told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Layla. He said: Hudhafi asked for something to drink in Al-Mada'in, and a blacksmith brought him a silver vessel containing a drink, and he wanted to use it to drink. His face, and it was said to him: Indeed, the righteous honor princes with this. He said: I was his intention, and I took it upon him. The argument is that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade us from drinking silver and gold. (Muslim 1637)"
24616,"(24616) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Ash’ath bin Abi Al-Sha’tha’i, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Suwayd bin Muqrin, on the authority of Al-Bara' bin Aazib, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade drinking from silver, for whoever drinks In this world, he will not drink in it in the hereafter."
24617,"(24617) Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Ala’, on the authority of Ali bin Al-Numan, who said: Omar said: Whoever drinks from a cup Overflowing, may God cause him to drink hot coals of burning coal on the Day of Resurrection."
24618,"(24618) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Anas ibn Malik; He was brought a silver cup containing fine flour, so he ordered it to be made and it was made onto a loaf of bread, then he ate it."
24619,"(24619) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, who said: Zazan, Misra, and Sa’id bin They do not drink from vessels of gold or silver, nor do they worship in vessels of gold and silver."
24620,"(24620) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Thabit ibn Ubaid, on the authority of Bashir ibn Abi Masoud; He was brought a silver vessel, so he hated it."
24621,"(24621) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, who said: Zazan, Misra, and Sa’id bin They drink from sterilized vessels."
24622,"(24622) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, on the authority of his father; He would not drink from a vessel covered with silver, but rather drink from a cup with a paper ring in it."
24623,"(24623) Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi told us, on the authority of Imran Abu al-Awwam al-Qattan, on the authority of his leaders; Imran bin Husayn and Anas bin Malik used to drink from the overflowing vessel."
24624,"(24624) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Hamid, who said: I entered upon Al-Qasim bin Muhammad while he was feverish. And on his chest was a cup filled with water."
24625,"(24625) Zaid bin Harun and Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Muslim, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Misra, he said: I saw a peacock drinking from a cup covered with paper."
24626,"(24626) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Yazid bin Ziyad al-Dimashqi, on the authority of Sulayman bin Habib and Sulayman bin Dawood, They said: We brought Omar bin Abdul Aziz a drink in an overflowing cup, so he put his mouth between the two straws and drank, and said: Do not repeat it to me."
24627,"(24627) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, who said: I saw Abu Ja`far drinking from a full cup. A lot of silver, and my water."
24628,"(24628) Abu Dawud narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, he said: I asked Muawiyah bin Qurayh, I said: I go to the money changers and I am given a cup of Silver, should I drink from it? He said: No problem."
24629,"(24629) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Omar; He would never drink from a cup containing a silver ring, or a silver lizard."
24630,"(24630) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, on the authority of Ali bin Hussein; He was brought a silver cup, and he decided to drink from it."
24631,"(24631) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Muhammad; They disliked the cup being rimmed with gold or silver."
24632,"(24632) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Abdul-Malik, on the authority of Ata’; He hated to drink from a cup of silver."
24633,"(24633) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud bin Qays, who said: I brought Al-Muttalib bin Abdullah bin Hantab with an empty cup, and he did not He drinks from it."
24634,"(24634) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Ibn Umar used to hate that He drinks from a cup containing a silver ring."
24635,"(24635) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Rawwad, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He did not drink from a silver vessel."
24636,"(24636) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Jarir bin Hazim, on the authority of Salem; He hated it"
24637,"(24637) Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Muhammad, on the authority of Umm Amr, the daughter of Abi Amr, who said: She was Aisha forbade us to adorn ourselves with gold, or to decorate our vessels, or to adorn them with silver, so we continued until she gave us permission. You have not given us permission to adorn themselves with gold, but you have not given us permission, nor have You given us permission to shave vessels or decorate them with silver."
24638,"(24638) Muhammad bin Yazid told us, on the authority of Ayoub Abi Al-Ala, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He hated to drink from an empty cup."
24639,"(24639) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zayd, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Muhajir, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Umar, and Ibn Abbas, they said: He was disliked to drink from the mouth of the goblet, or from the ear of the goblet."
24640,"(24640) Muhammad bin Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: They used to hate that he should drink from The hole is in the vessel, or it is drunk from its ear."
24641,"(24641) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Muhajir, on the authority of Mujahid; He hated to drink from what was behind the handle of the cup, or the notch that was in it."
24642,"(24642) Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of Ata’; He did not see any harm in drinking in one breath."
24643,"(24443) Hatem bin Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Zaid, who said: I have not seen anyone who was quicker to break the fast than Saeed. Ibn Al-Musayyab would not wait for a muezzin, but a cup of water would be brought and he would drink it in one breath, not even interrupting it. He will finish it."
24644,"(24644) Al-Thaqafi narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, he said: I was informed on the authority of Maimun bin Mihran, he said: Omar bin Abdul Aziz saw me and I. I was drinking, so I stopped drinking and took a breath. He said: He only forbade breathing into the vessel, so if you do not breathe into the vessel, So drink it if you wish in one breath."
24645,"(24645) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, who said: My father saw us drinking in one breath and he stopped, or No more"
24646,"(24446) Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Khaled, on the authority of Ikrimah; He disliked drinking with one breath, and he said: It is the drinking of the devil."
24647,"(24647) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade breathing into a vessel and blowing into it. (Abu Dawud 3721. Tirmidhi 1888)"
24648,"(24448) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham Al-Distawai, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abd Allah bin Abi Qatada, on the authority of his father; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: If one of you drinks, he should not breathe into the vessel.
(Bukhari 5430, Muslim 65)"
24649,"(24649) Abdul-Wahhab Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Khaled, on the authority of Ikrimah; He hated to breathe in the vessel."
24650,"(24650) Abu Dawud al-Talisi narrated to us, on the authority of Ezra ibn Thabit, on the authority of Thamamah, who said: Whenever Anas drank, he would gasp for breath. Twice, or three times, and it happened that when the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, drank, he would breathe into the vessel three times. (Bukhari 5431. Ahmad 3/114)"
24651,"(24651) Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi told us, on the authority of al-Hakam ibn Atiyya, who said: I saw Ibn Sirin breathing three times. If he drinks"
24652,"(24652) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: When you drink, breathe into the vessel three times."
24653,"(24653) Ubaid Allah bin Musa told us, on the authority of Uthman bin Al-Aswad, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman bin Abi Bakr, who said: He sat A man came to Ibn Abbas and said to him: Where did you come from? He said: I drank some of the water of Zamzam. He said: Did you drink some of it as you should? He said: When you drink from it, face the Kaaba, mention the name of God, and inhale three times."
24654,"(24654) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ezra bin Thabit, on the authority of Thumama bin Abdullah, on the authority of Anas; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to breathe into the vessel three times. (Muslim 122)"
24655,"(24655) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Abu Issam, on the authority of Anas, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He breathes three times into the vessel, and says: He is more comfortable, more commanded, and more innocent. (Muslim 123, Tirmidhi 1884)"
24656,"(24656) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Simak, he said: I was in one of the Ansar’s gatherings, and some of them were brought a drink. When he wanted to drink, he blew on it, and some of the people said: Wait, for the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, had forbidden it. about him"
24657,"(24657) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Malik ibn Anas, on the authority of Ayyub ibn Habib, a client of Banu Zurayah, on the authority of Abu Al-Muthanna Al-Janni said: I was with Marwan bin Al-Hakam when Abu Saeed entered and said to him: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbidding blowing on a drink? He said: Yes, he said: Then a man said: I cannot quench it with one breath. He said: Remove the vessel from your mouth, then exhale. He said: If you see filth ? He said: So burn it. (Abu Dawud 3715. Dharmi 2121)"
24658,"(24658) Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade He excluded the issue of blowing food and drink. He said: I have not seen anyone more severe in that than Omar bin Abdul Aziz."
24659,"(24659) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade breathing into a vessel and blowing into it."
24660,"(24660) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Thawr, on the authority of Yazid Dhu al-Arsh, on the authority of a servant of Thawban, she said: I came to Thawban. With a drink, I blew on it, but he refused to drink."
24661,"(24661) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hashim ibn al-Barid, on the authority of al-Qasim ibn Muslim, the client of al-Hasan ibn Ali, who said: He asked for water. Ali, so I brought him a drink and I blew on it, but he refused to drink it, and said: Drink it yourself."
24662,"(24662) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of cold, on the authority of alcohol; He hated blowing on food and drink."
24663,"(24663) Hafs told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, he said: He hated it."
24664,"(24664) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Iyas, on the authority of Ibrahim; He disliked blowing on food and drink."
24665,"(24665) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Qatada, on the authority of his father; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade blowing into a vessel."
24666,"(24666) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Wasil, on the authority of Mujahid; He did not see any harm in blowing on food or drink."
24667,"(24667) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawus; He used to blow on food and drink."
24668,"(24668) Hafs told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Ad-Duha, on the authority of Masruq, who said: A drink was brought to Abdullah, and he said: Give me a piece of it. Hand the black one."
24669,"(24669) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamiya, on the authority of Abdullah; In a similar way"
24670,"(24670) Issa bin Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Ad-Duha, on the authority of Masruq, who said: Abdullah was brought a drink, and he said: Hand the black one, hand the black one."
24671,"(24671) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Salama bin Mahrez, who said: A peacock asked for water, so a drink was brought to him, and he offered it to Abdullah. Ibn Al-Hasan, and he said: Drink."
24672,"(24672) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Ghaylan bin Yazid, who said: Abu Ubaidah was invited to... And a feast, and a drink was brought, and he gave it to the one on his right."
24673,"(24673) Abu Asama told us, he said: Shu’bah told me, on the authority of Amara bin Abi Hafsa, on the authority of Ikrimah, he said: Omar was brought a drink while he was standing on the eve of the night, so he drank and then gave it to the master of the people of Yemen while he was on his right. He said: I am fasting, so he said: I ordered you not to break the fast, and I ordered your companions to break the fast."
24674,"(24674) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who heard it from Anas. He said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, came and I He was ten years old, and he, may God bless him and grant him peace, died when I was twenty years old, and my mothers urged me to serve him. Then he entered our house, and we milked for him some of our domesticated sheep, and gray hair for him from a well in the house, and Abu Bakr to his left. And a Bedouin was on his right, and Omar was near him, and Omar said: O Messenger of God, give Abu Bakr, so he gave him to the Bedouin. And he said: The right hand, then the right hand.
(Muslim 1251 Malik 17)"
24675,"(24675) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace May God bless him and grant him peace. He loves honey and He loves sweet things. (Bukhari 5991 Muslim 1101)"
24676,"(24676) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: He was the most beloved drink to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And the sweet, cold greeting. (Tirmidhi 1896)"
24677,"(24677) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Ali bin Sulaym, who said: I heard Anas say: I drink sweet paint. The biting"
24678,"(24678) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked: Which drink is most beloved to you? He said: Sweet and cold."
24679,"(24679) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He used to soak raisins in a water bottle for him in the evening, and he would drink it in the morning, and it would be soaked for him in the morning. So he drinks it in the evening."
24680,"(24680) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Umm Ghurab, on the authority of Bananiya, she said: I used to soak raisins for Uthman in his dinner, and he would drink from them. And he eats from it."
24681,"(24681) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ali, Amer, and Ata’; They said: There is no harm in soaking raisins in the morning and drinking them in the evening."
24682,"(24682) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: There is no harm in soaking raisins. Sufyan said: What He did not boil."
24683,"(24683) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Salam bin Miskin, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: There is no harm in raisin wine."
24684,"(24684) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ali bin Malik, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, who said: On the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: It is only wine; When it matures, it spoils, but as for what increases in quality over a period of abandonment, there is no good in it."
24685,"(24685) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of a man called: Issa, on the authority of Omar bin Abdul Aziz; Like him"
24686,"(24686) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Abu Al-Sha’athai, on the authority of Muadh, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade May the peace and blessings of God be upon him, on the authority of the drunkards."
24687,"(24687) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Kharijiya, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yassar, who said: The Messenger of God forbade May God bless him and grant him peace on the authority of drunkards. (Malik 10)"
24688,"(24688) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Hammam ibn Al-Harith, who said: Omar was brought some raisin wine. So he drank from it, frowned, called for water and poured it on him, then drank."
24689,"(24689) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Abu Awn, who said: Omar came to a group of people from Thaqif, and he prepared their food, and he said: Eat the porridge before the meat, as it fills the defect, and if your wine becomes strong, break it with water, and do not The Bedouins gave him water."
24690,"(24690) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sumayya, she said: I heard Aisha say: If you are afraid of your wine, break it with water."
24691,"(24691) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khalid, on the authority of Qara al-Ijli, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin al-Qaqa’. On the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: We were with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and a cup of drink was brought to him, and he brought it to him. Then he returned it, and some of those sitting with him said to him: Is it forbidden, O Messenger of God? He said: So he said: Return it, so they returned it, then he called for water and poured it on him, then he drank it, and said: Look at this drink. Then when it overpowers you, wash its water with water."
24692,"(24692) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ali bin al-Mubarak, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Salem al-Dawsi; He heard Abu Hurairah say: Whoever drinks some of his wine, let him sprinkle water on him, and the unlawful things will go away. And it remains permissible."
24693,"(24693) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ikrimah bin Ammar, on the authority of Abu Kathir al-Hanafi, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: Whoever drinks any of it, let him break it with water."
24694,"(24694) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abd al-Wahid ibn Ayman, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Nafi’ ibn Abd al-Harith, who said: Omar said: Drink this wine in this water, for it strengthens the heart and digests what is in the stomach, but it does not You will be overcome as long as you find water."
24695,"(24695) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Mundhir ibn Abi al-Mundhir, who said: I saw Ibn Abbas bowing In the Basin of Zamzam while standing."
24696,"(24696) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Amara, on the authority of Ikrimah; He hated walking in the morning."
24697,"(24697) Yunus bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Fulayh bin Sulaiman, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered upon a man from the Ansar who was bringing water to a wall, and with him was a companion of his. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Do you have any water that spent the night during this night? Otherwise, we will fail.
(Bukhari 5613 and Abu Dawud 3717)"
24698,"(24698) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Sa’id bin Amir, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: We passed with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace be upon him, greeted a pool of water, so we started bowing in it, and he said: Do not bow, but wash your hands and drink. In it, there is no vessel more beautiful than the hand. (Ibn Majah 3433 and Abu Ali 5675)"
24699,"(24699) Bishr bin Al-Mufaddal narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Othman, who said: I spent the night with Sa’id bin Jubayr on the eve of the sacrifice. So he came to a basin containing water of Zamzam, so he scooped it with his hand and drank from it."
24700,"(24700) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir; Abu Hamid came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, with a drink while he was in Al-Baqi’, and he said: Have you not covered it, even if you leave it? May Allah return to him. (Nasa’i 6633. Ahmad 3/294)"
24701,"(24701) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Fitr, on the authority of Abu al-Zubair, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: : Close your doors, cover your utensils, and set up your watering cans. (Ahmad 3/301, Malik 928)"
24702,"(24702) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu al-Wadak, Jabr ibn Nawf, on the authority of Abu Sa`id. Al-Khudri said: We were commanded to give water to the water."
24703,"(24703) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Habib ibn Jarī, on the authority of Abu Ja’far, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was He likes the perfect vessel."
24704,"(24704) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman bin Yazid, on the authority of Zazan, he said: If the vessel remains unfermented, Satan spits in it. I mentioned that to Abraham, and he said: Or he drank from it."
24705,"(24705) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Salam bin al-Qasim, on the authority of his mother, on the authority of Umm Sa`id, she said: I brought Ali a pre-dawn meal, so I put it on him. between his hands while he was praying, and when he prayed, he said: Oh, you covered me, did you see Satan when he was raving about him? He vomited it, but he refused to drink it."
24706,"(24706) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Aaron, a client of Quraysh, who said: I saw Al-Muttalib bin Hantab drinking a stalk of water. Holding almonds."
24707,"(24707) Abu Usama and Waki` told us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Abu al-Mukhtar, on the authority of Ibn Abi Awfa, who said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: The last of the people’s shepherds is the last of them. (Abu Dawud 3718 and Ahmad 4/354)"
24708,"(24708) Shababah bin Siwar told us, on the authority of Suleiman bin Al-Mughirah, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Abdullah bin Rabah, on the authority of Abu Qatada said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The last of the people’s legs is their last. (Muslim 311, Tirmidhi 1894)"
24709,"(24709) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mubarak, on the authority of Bakr bin Abdullah Al-Muzani, on the authority of Abdullah bin Rabah, on the authority of Abu He led him, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: The people’s last legs are their last."
24710,"(24710) Azhar narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: There is no harm in drinking water that is given for charity."
24711,"(24711) Khalid bin Mukhlid narrated to us, saying: Abdullah bin Ja’far narrated to us, on the authority of Umm Bakr Ibn Al-Miswar, she said: It was The one who is praying does not drink from the water that is placed in the mosque, and he hates it, and thinks that it is charity."
24712,"(24712) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: Saad bin Ubadah said: O Messenger of God, please grant me With your truthfulness, he said: Give the water to drink. He said: So he set up two water-carriers, and they did not remain set up. Perhaps I ran between them while I was a boy.
(Abu Dawud 1676. Ahmad 6/7)"
24713,"(24713) Zayd ibn al-Hubab al-Ukli narrated to us, on the authority of Hussein ibn Waqid, on the authority of Ibn Buraydah, on the authority of his father, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, pardoned Al-Hasan and Al-Hussein. (Nasa’i 4539. Ahmad 5/355)"
24714,(۲۴۷۱۴) حَدَّثَنَا شَبَابَۃُ ، قَالَ : حدَّثَنَا مُغِیرَۃُ بْنُ مُسْلِمٍ ، عَنْ أَبِی الزُّبَیْرِ ، عَنْ جَابِرٍ ، قَالَ : عَقَّ رَسُولُ اللہِ May God bless him and grant him peace on the authority of Al-Hasan and Al-Hussein. (ابویعلی ۱۹۲۹۔ طبرانی ۲۵۷۳)
24715,"(24715) Abu Khaled and Ya’la bin Ubaid told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, on the authority of Ikrimah, he said: He performed aqeeqah on the authority of Al-Hasan. And Al-Hussein."
24716,"(24716) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Bakr, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ali bin Hussein, on the authority of Ali, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, performed a shaqah on the authority of Al-Hasan, and he said: O Fatima, shave you. His head and you gave in charity the weight of his hair. They weighed it and its weight was a dirham, or some dirham. (Tirmidhi 1519, Malik 2)"
24717,"(24717) Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Asadi narrated to us, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Ibn Aqeel, on the authority of Ali bin Al-Hussein, on the authority of Abu Rafi’, he said: Fatima said: O Messenger of God, should I not make a blood aqeeqah on behalf of my son? He said: No, shave his head and give his weight in charity. The poor are a few cups of paper or silver. (Ahmad 6/390, Tabarani 917)"
24718,"(24718) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: If I had known that he had not performed the aqeeqah on my behalf, I would have performed the aqeeqah on my own behalf."
24719,"(24719) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ibrahim, he said: He was commanded With the aqeeqah, even with a bird. (Bayhaqi 71)"
24720,"(24720) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Samurah, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: The boy is pledged for his aqeeqah, and he will slaughter it for him. (Abu Dawud 2831. Tirmidhi 1522)"
24721,"(24721) Ibn Numir told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Hafsa Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Salman bin Amer; He heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Indeed, with the boy is his aqeeqah, so shed the blood from him and wipe him away.” Harm
(Ibn Majah 3164. Ahmad 4/17)"
24722,"(24722) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Zayd ibn Aslam, on the authority of a man from Banu Damra, on the authority of his father, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked about the aqeeqah? He said: God does not like disobedience. Whoever among you has a child born to him and would like to keep you away from him, let him do so. (Owner 500)"
24723,"(24723) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Yazid, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Siba’ ibn Thabit, on the authority of Umm Kurz, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: On behalf of the boy, two good sheep, and on the behalf of the slave girl, one sheep. It will not harm you. Whether female or male.
(Abu Dawud 2829. Tirmidhi 1516)"
24724,"(24724) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Habiba bint Misra, on the authority of Umm Kurz; I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: On behalf of the boy, two well-bred sheep, and on behalf of the slave girl, one sheep. (Ahmad 6/422 Darami 1966)"
24725,"(24725) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Aslam, on the authority of Ata’; Umm al-Sibbaa’ asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Should I perform the aqiqah on behalf of my children? He said: Yes, two sheep on behalf of the boy, and two sheep on the behalf of the slave girl."
24726,"(24726) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: On the authority of the boy there were two sheep, and on the authority of The slave girl is a sheep."
24727,"(24727) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud bin Qays, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, he said: He was asked The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the authority of the Aqeeqah? He said: I do not like disobedience. If a child is born to him and would like to forget about it, let him do so. On behalf of the boy, two sheep, and on behalf of the girl, two sheep. (Abu Dawud 2835. Ahmad 2/185)"
24728,"(24728) Shihab bin Muhammad Al-Ghadiri narrated to us, on the authority of Uthman bin Al-Aswad, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: There are two sheep in the aqeeqah. Two rewards, and a sheep on behalf of the slave girl."
24729,"(24729) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Uthman, on the authority of Yusuf bin Mahik, on the authority of Hafsah bint Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Aisha; She said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered us to slaughter two sheep for the boy, and one sheep for the female slave. (Tirmidhi 1513. Ahmad 6/158)"
24730,"(24730) Abd bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Aisha, that she said: The Sunnah on the authority of The boy has two beautiful sheep, and a sheep for the girl."
24731,"(24731) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He used to say: On the authority of the slave girl and on the authority of the boy, a sheep, a sheep."
24732,"(24732) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Saeed, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin al-Qasim, on the authority of his father; He used to perform aqāt on behalf of a boy and a female slave, a sheep, a sheep, a sheep."
24733,"(24733) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwah, on the authority of his father; He used to perform the aqeeqah on behalf of the male and female slaves, a sheep, a sheep."
24734,"(24734) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Abu Jafar, he said: A sheep, a sheep."
24735,"(24735) Yahya bin Sa’id told us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of his father, who said: They are the same."
24736,"(24736) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri; He used to say about the aqeeqah: He is aqeeqah on behalf of the male and female, one sheep, one sheep."
24737,"(24737) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Samurah, on the authority of the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: He will be slaughtered on his behalf on the seventh day, his head will be shaved and his name will be named."
24738,"(24738) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib; The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, ordered the aqeeqah to be performed on the seventh day of the birth, the removal of the male child, and the naming of it."
24739,"(24739) Mu’tamar bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: He did not see any harm in being sterilized. Before or after the seventh, and he used to say: Make the flesh of the aqeeqah whatever you wish."
24740,"(24740) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He said: In the aqeeqah there is an old sheep, it must be slaughtered for him on the seventh day, his head should be shaved, and he should give his name."
24741,"(24741) Abd al-Malik ibn Ayn told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Suleiman, on the authority of Abu Ja`far said: Fatima used to perform the aqeeqah on behalf of her children on the seventh day, name him, circumcise him, shave his head, and give him alms. Its weight is paper."
24742,"(24742) Affan told us, he said: Abdul-Warith told us, he said: Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib told us, on the authority of Muharib bin Dathar, on the authority of Ibn Umar. He said regarding the aqeeqah: It should be slaughtered on his behalf on the seventh day, his head should be shaved, he should be given in charity the weight of his hair in silver, and he should be smeared with His head is covered in blood."
24743,"(24743) Abdullah bin Mubarak told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Ibn Sirin; They disliked the aqeeqah as much as they disliked the sacrifice. He said: And he was with them at his place. The sacrificial animal, he eats and feeds him."
24744,"(24744) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Abdul Malik, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Aisha, she said: She makes a table, So he cooks, then he eats and feeds you."
24745,"(24745) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Jafar, on the authority of his father; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered that the aqeeqah that she had performed should be performed by Fatima on the behalf of Al-Hasan and Al-Husayn. They will be sent to The one who faced it with a man said: Not a bone of it will be broken.
(Abu Dawud 379)"
24746,"(24746) Abdă told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Aisha, she said: She cooks a table, and it does not break. Some of them are bones."
24747,"(24747) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: I asked him about the aqeeqah? He said: Do not break her bones or her head, and do not let the boy touch any of her blood."
24748,"(24748) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Nāḥas ibn Qaym, who said: I heard Ata’ saying: They liked it not to be broken. The aqeeqah has a bone."
24749,"(24749) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Muhammad; They disliked that the boy’s head be smeared with any of the blood of the aqeeqah, and Al-Hasan said: Blood is an abomination."
24750,"(24750) Uthman bin Matar narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If they sacrifice on behalf of the boy, then it is sufficient for the aqeeqah."
24751,"(24751) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Ibn Sirin, who said: A portion of the aqeeqah is sufficient for him. The sacrifice"
24752,"(24752) Othman bin Matar narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, who said: It is not sufficient for him until a sanitation is done for him."
24753,"(24753) Zayd bin Harun told us, he said: Hisham al-Dastawwi told us, on the authority of his leaders, he said: He will be named Ali. The aqeeqah as the sacrifice is given: In the name of God, so-and-so’s aqeeqah."
24754,"(24754) Othman bin Matar narrated to us, on the authority of Saeed, who said: His leaders were asked: How is the aqeeqah slaughtered? He said: He faces her towards the Qiblah, then places the blade on her throat, then says: Oh God, from You and to You, the aqeeqat of so-and-so. In the name of God and God is great, then he slaughters it."
24755,"(24755) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Harith bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Anas ibn Malik used to perform aqiyyah on behalf of his sons on the islands."
24756,"(24756) Saul bin Yusuf told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Muhammad; Indeed, they did not see the maidservant as Aqeeqah."
24757,"(24757) Harith narrated to us, on the authority of Jarir, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, who said: A slave woman shall not be disobedient, nor shall she be honored."
24758,"(24758) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Harun bin Abi Ibrahim, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ubaid bin Umair; That a man asked him about the rabbit? He said: There is nothing wrong with her. He said: She is menstruating. He said: He who knows her menstruation knows how she is pure, but she is pregnant. Of pregnant women."
24759,"(24759) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Hisham ibn Zayd ibn Anas, on the authority of Anas, who said: I heard him say: We caused a rabbit to burst forth, and the young men ran after it until they were lost, then I overtook it and brought it to Abu Talha. So he slaughtered her, then he sent with her to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, with her blessings, and they accepted her."
24760,"(24760) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Talha bin Yahya, on the authority of Musa bin Talha. That a man asked Omar about the rabbit? Then Omar said: If it were not that I would not like to add more to the hadith, or subtract from it, and I will send you to a man, so he sent to Ammar came and said: We were with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and we camped in such-and-such a place. He said: So he gave me a gift. A Bedouin man brought a rabbit and we ate it. The Bedouin said: I saw blood. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: No. Unfortunately
(Ahmad 1/31, Abu Ali 1612)"
24761,"(24761) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hammam, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab, on the authority of Sa’d; He ate it. He said: So I said to Sa`id: What do you say about it? He said: I used to eat it."
24762,"(24762) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Muslim, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Misra, on the authority of Ubaid bin Saad ; Bilal shot a rabbit with a stick and broke its legs, so he slaughtered it and ate it."
24763,"(24763) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: He saw no harm in eating a rabbit."
24764,"(24764) Abu Dawud narrated to us, on the authority of Zam’a, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, who said: Rabbit is permissible."
24765,"(24765) Zaid bin Al-Hubab told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Wasim, he said: I asked Hassan bin Hassan bin Ali about the rabbit? He said: I will pardon her, but I will not forbid her to the Muslims."
24766,"(24766) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Muhammad bin Sayfi, who said: I came to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He greeted me with two rabbits that I had slaughtered in Marwa, so he ordered me to eat them."
24767,"(24767) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, saying: Dawud bin Abi Hind informed us, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Muhammad bin Safwan, On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace; Such as the hadith of Abu Al-Ahwas."
24768,"(24768) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hikam, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Layla; He hated to eat it."
24769,"(24769) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abu Makin, on the authority of Ikrimah; He hated it"
24770,"(24770) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Hammam, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab, on the authority of Ibn Amr, or Ibn Umar; He hated it"
24771,"(24771) Yahya bin Wadh narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Abd al-Karim bin Abi al-Mukhariq, on the authority of Hibban Ibn Jazi’, on the authority of his brother, Khuzaymah Ibn Jazi’, who said: I said: O Messenger of God, I have come to you to ask you about the creatures of the earth. What do you say? In the rabbit? He said: I will not eat it, nor will I make it unlawful. I said: I will eat what you have not made unlawful, and why, O Messenger of God? He said: I was informed that it would bleed. (Bukhari 7051, Ibn Majah 3245)"
24772,"(24772) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Nafi’ told me, he said: It was said to Ibn Omar: Indeed, Saad He eats hyenas, but he did not deny that."
24773,"(24773) Yahya bin Sa’id told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: There is no harm in eating it, and he said: Hunter"
24774,"(24774) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Abu al-Minhal Nasr ibn Aws, on the authority of his uncle Abdullah ibn Zayd, who said: I asked Abu What about the hyena? He said: A ewe from the sheep."
24775,"(24775) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ma’qil, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Jabir, who said: A hyena is more beloved to me than a ram."
24776,"(24776) Ismail Ibn Aliya narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Ubaid Allah Ibn Ibrahim Al-Makki, on the authority of Mawla To them, on the authority of Jabir, he said: The hyena is a hunter, so eat them, and do not hunt them in the Sacred Mosque."
24777,"(24777) Yahya bin Wadh narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Abd al-Karim bin Abi al-Mukhariq, on the authority of Hibban bin Juz’, on the authority of his brother, Khuzaymah bin Juz’, who said: I said, O Messenger of God, what do you say about the hyena? He said: Who eats the hyena?"
24778,"(24778) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, who said: The Arabs used to eat the hyena."
24779,"(24779) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Harun, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, who said: He was one of us to guide The colorful hyena is more beloved to him than the fat chicken."
24780,"(24780) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: Neither Far’a, nor Ataira. (Bukhari 5474, Muslim 1562)"
24781,"(24781) Abdul-A’la told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah; The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Neither Far’a, nor Ataira.
 Al-Zuhri said: As for the branch; For it is the first produce that they produce from their livestock that they slaughter for their gods, and for the livestock in Rajab.
(Bukhari 5473, Muslim 38)"
24782,"(24782) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Abu Ishaq; That Ali and Ibn Masoud did not see the Prophet."
24783,"(24783) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Asama bin Zayd, on the authority of Al-Qasim, who said: I asked him about Al-Atira? He said: These are the rugby animals sacrificed by the people of the pre-Islamic era."
24784,"(24784) Abu Osama told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, he said: I asked Al-Sha’abi about Al-Atira? He said: Your neighbors are the most worthy of people. I said: What is it? He said: In the remaining ten days of Rajab."
24785,"(24785) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mubarak, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The sacrifices of the pre-Islamic people."
24786,"(24786) Muadh bin Muadh told us, he said: Ibn Aoun told us, he said: Abu Ramla informed me, on the authority of Mikhnaf bin Sulaym; He mentioned standing with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, with his knowledge, and he said: O people, I am in charge of every house in every year. Sacrifice and itirah, do you know what the itirah is? He said: This is what people call Rajabiya. (Abu Dawud 2781, Tirmidhi 1518)"
24787,"(24787) Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad, he said: He used to slaughter in every Rajab. Muadh said: And I saw The family of Ibn Aoun."
24788,"(24788) Abdullah bin Numayr narrated to us, saying: Dawud bin Qays narrated to us, saying: Amr bin Shuaib narrated to me, on the authority of his father. On the authority of his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked about the branch? He said: Al-Fur’ is true, and if you abandon it until it is Shaghzba, Ibn Makhad, or Ibn Labun, then you will burden him for the sake of By God, or that you give him to a widow is better than that you slaughter him, make his flesh stick to his dung, fill your vessel, and let your she-camel take care of him. 
 And he asked him about the Prophet? Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, remained silent, so some of the people asked Omar about the family? He said: We used to call it Al-Rajbiyah, and the Ahl al-Bayt slaughtered a sheep in Rajab and they ate it. (Abu Dawud 2835. Hakim 236)"
24789,"(24789) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Abdullah bin Uthman bin Khathham told us, on the authority of Yusuf Bin Mahik, on the authority of Hafsa bint Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Aisha; She said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, commanded us to cut a sheep for every five sheep. (Abu Dawud 2826; Abd al-Razzaq 7997)"
24790,"(24790) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ibrahim ibn Misra, and Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, he said: The Prophet was asked May God bless him and grant him peace, about the branch? So he said: Spend food if you wish, and feed him until he reaches puberty, then bear for him in the way of God, or connect with him as a sacrifice. Better than being slaughtered, his meat mixed with his hair."
24791,"(24791) Affan told us, he said: Abu Awani told us, he said: Ali bin Ata told us, on the authority of Waki’ al-Uqailiy, On the authority of his uncle Abu Razin, who is Laqit bin Amir; He said: O Messenger of God, we used to slaughter sacrifices in Rajab and eat from them and feed those who came to us? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: There is no harm in that. He said: Waki` said: I will never leave her.
(Ahmad 13. Darmi 1965)"
24792,"(24792) Abu Khaled and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwah, on the authority of Fatima bint al-Mundhir, on the authority of Asma’ bint Abu Bakr, she said: We slaughtered a horse at the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and we ate some of its meat, or we ate some of its meat. His flesh
(Bukhari 5510, Muslim 345)"
24793,"(24793) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, who said: We ate horse meat. On the Day of Khaybar, and the meat of wild asses. (Muslim 1541. Ibn Majah 3191)"
24794,"(24794) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, fed us He forbade horse meat, and forbade us from donkey meat. (Tirmidhi 1793, An-Nasa’i 4840)"
24795,"(24795) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace They eat horse meat in their camps."
24796,"(24796) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Abdullah’s companions slaughtered a horse. So they divided it among themselves."
24797,"(24797) Salam narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Our companions used to eat horse meat."
24798,"(24798) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`bah, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim; The lion ate the meat of a horse."
24799,"(24799) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hikam; That Shuraih ate the meat of a horse."
24800,"(24800) Abu Osama told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, he said: I asked Muhammad about horse meat? He did not see any harm in it."
24801,"(24801) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: There is no harm in it."
24802,"(24802) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, who said: I caught them dividing horse meat."
24803,"(24803) Waki’ and Ali bin Hashim told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Al-Manhal, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, On the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: A man asked him about eating horses? Waki` said: About eating horses, so he recited these verses: {And the livestock He created for you in them is warmth} the verses, he said: He thought about it."
24804,"(24804) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: There is no harm in horse meat."
24805,"(24805) Ibn Aliya told us, on the authority of Hisham Al-Dastawwi, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Mawla Nafi’ Ibn Alqamah; Ibn Abbas hated the meat of horses, mules, and donkeys, and he used to say: God Almighty said: {And the livestock He created for you; in them there is warmth and benefits, and from them you eat} so these are for food {and horses and mules and donkeys. That you may ride it} This is for riding."
24806,"(24806) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abd al-Karim al-Jazari, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Jabir, who said: We were We eat horse meat, but not mules. (Bayhaqi 327. Ibn Jarir 83)"
24807,"(24807) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Zubayr bin Adiy, on the authority of Ibrahim; He hated mule meat."
24808,"(24808) Ghandar told us, on the authority of his people, on the authority of Al-Hikam, on the authority of Mujahid; He was asked about horse meat? He said: {And horses and mules and donkeys for you to ride}, as if he hated their flesh."
24809,"(24809) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Humaid, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata, who said: No. There is nothing wrong with eating mule meat."
24810,"(24810) Abdullah bin Numayr narrated to us, saying: Muhammad bin Ishaq narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr bin Damra Al-Fazariy. On the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Salit, on the authority of his father, Abi Salit, who was Badriya, he said: The Messenger of God’s prohibition has come to us. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him about eating donkeys while we were at Khaybar, and the pots would overflow with them, so He sufficed for them on their faces.
(Tabarani 580, Ahmad 3/419)"
24811,"(24811) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade About donkey meat."
24812,"(24812) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade May God bless him and grant him peace regarding the meat of domestic donkeys."
24813,"(24813) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abdullah, and Al-Hasan, the sons of Muhammad, on the authority of their father; Ali said to Ibn Abbas: Did you not know that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade the meat of donkeys? The family"
24814,"(24814) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Bara’, he said: People were struck with severe hunger on the Day of Khaybar. So they attacked the red of the family and cooked some of it, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered the pots to be brought in, and they were rewarded. 
(Bukhari 4222. Muslim 29)"
24815,"(24815) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, saying: Ubayd Allah narrated to us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. And he greeted; He forbade the meat of domestic donkeys on the Day of Khaybar. (Bukhari 4218, Muslim 24)"
24816,"(24816) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Mu’awiyah ibn Salih, he said: Al-Hasan ibn Jabir narrated to me, on the authority of Al-Miqdam ibn The Canadian's anguish is contagious; The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade certain things, and he even mentioned human red blood.
(Abu Dawud 4594. Tirmidhi 2464)"
24817,"(24817) Zayd ibn Harun told us, he said: Hisham ibn Hassan informed us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Sirin, on the authority of Anas ibn Malik, he said: On the Day of Khaybar, the people slaughtered the Reds and boiled pots with them, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered He greeted Abu Talha and called, “Indeed, Allah and His Messenger have forbidden you from eating the meat of domestic donkeys, for it is an abomination. So the fates were filled.
(Muslim 34. Ahmad 3/111)"
24818,"(24818) Abu Asama narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid bin Jabir, who said: Al-Qasim and Makhul narrated to us, on the authority of Abu In front of him; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the Day of Khabar forbade eating domestic donkeys."
24819,"(24819) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, he said: I asked Abdullah bin Abi Awfa about donkey meat. The family? He said: A famine struck us on the Day of Khaybar, and we were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and we struck the people with red blood. Coming out of Medina, we burned it, and indeed our pots were boiling, when the herald of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, called out; That they fill the pots, and do not eat any of the meat of donkeys. So I said: He made it forbidden, forbidden as to what? He said: We talked among ourselves, and we said: He absolutely forbidden it, and he forbade it because it was not given the fifth. (Bukhari 4220, Muslim 1538)"
24820,"(24820) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaidah, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Salama, on the authority of Abu Hurairah; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade the human donkey on the day of Khaybar. (Tirmidhi 1795. Ahmad 2/366)"
24821,"(24821) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus bin Abi Ishaq, he said: Abu Al-Wadak narrated to us, he said: Abu Al-Wadak narrated to us. Saeed Al-Khudri, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace; He passed by the pots as they were boiling and said to us: What are these donkeys? Are they domestic or wild? So we said: No, but my family. He said: So suffice her. He said: So suffice her, and we are hungry and thirsty for her. (Abu Yali 1178)"
24822,"(24822) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: Its meat and milk are forbidden."
24823,"(24823) Yahya bin Wadh narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Asim bin Omar bin Qatada al-Dhafri, on the authority of Salma bint Nasr, on the authority of a man from the Banu Murā, who said: I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, the greatness of his wealth is Reds, will I be more affected by them? He said: Don't you graze the desert and eat the trees? I said: Yes, he said: Then pour from it. (Musnad 656)"
24824,"(24824) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ubaid bin Al-Hasan, on the authority of Ghalib bin Dhikh, who said: I said: O Messenger of God, We have been afflicted with old age, and the fat content of donkeys. He said: “Everyone has a fat owner. I have only acquired filth from the camel of the village.”
(Abu Dawud 3803. Tabarani 670)"
24825,"(24825) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Layla, who said: It was only disliked. Keeping on the back, meaning the meat of donkeys."
24826,"(24826) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`bah, on the authority of Ubaid bin al-Hasan, on the authority of Ibn Maqil, on the authority of people from Muzain Al-Dhahirah, he said: Ghalib bin Abjar said: I asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, I said: Nothing of my wealth remains except Is it red? He said: Feed your family with your own fat. He said: I hate for you the wandering of the city."
24827,"(24827) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Al-Amash narrated to us, on the authority of Zayd bin Wahhab, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Hasna, he said: I was We were traveling with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and a fog struck us, and pots were boiling, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Peace be upon him: What is this? So we said: We have been struck by fog. He said: One of the children of Israel has become a mutant, and I fear that she may be demented. He said: So he sufficed for her, and we were hungry. (Ahmad 4/1961 Abu Ali 931)"
24828,"(24828) Abu Asama told us, he said: Ubad Allah ibn Umar told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked. May God bless him and grant him peace while he was on the pulpit in the presence of a lizard? He said: I will not eat it, nor will I deprive it of it. (Muslim 1542. Ahmad 2/13)"
24829,"(24829) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, saying: Dawud bin Abi Hind narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Nadrah, on the authority of Abu Sa’id. Al-Khudri, he said: A man came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: We are in the land of Madhab, so what do you command me to do? Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: One of the children of Israel transformed an animal, and I do not know which animal it is. He neither commanded nor forbade it. (Muslim 50. Ibn Majah 3240)"
24830,"(24830) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hikam, on the authority of Zayd ibn Wahhab, on the authority of Al-Bara’ ibn Aazib, on the authority of Thabit ibn He bade him farewell and said: A lizard was brought to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: My mother has become mutated, and God knows best.
(Ahmad 4/220, Tayalisi 1220)"
24831,"(24831) Ubaid bin Saeed narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, She said: A lizard was given as a gift to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, but he did not eat from it. She said: So I said: O Messenger of God, no? Do I feed him the question? He said: Do not feed the beggar except what you eat. (Ahmad 6/105)"
24832,"(24832) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Yazid bin al-Asam, on the authority of Maimunah, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Give us a lizard, so I made it, and two men from... Then she brought it to them, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered while they were eating, so he laid down his hand, then He picked them up, and they threw out what was in their hands, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to them: No, for you are the people of Najd. You eat it, but we, the people of Medina, enjoy it.
(Abu Ali 7048)"
24833,"(24833) Affan narrated to us, he said: Abu Awani narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Malik bin Umayr narrated to us, on the authority of Husain, a man from Bani Fazara, on the authority of Samurah bin Jundub, who said: A Bedouin came to the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he was giving a sermon. So he broke off his engagement and said: O Messenger of God, what do you say about lizards? He said: One of the children of Israel became mutated, so I do not know which animal was transformed. (Tabarani 2224)"
24834,"(24834) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Yazid bin Al-Asam, who said: A bride invited us to Medina. Then thirteen lizards approached us, some eating and some leaving, so I met Ibn Abbas the next day and informed him, so the people gathered around him more. Some of them even said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I do not eat it, nor forbid it, nor make it permissible, nor I deprive him of it, and Ibn Abbas said: How miserable is what you said. Indeed, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was sent as a place and as a place of prohibition, while he was With Maimunah, and with him are Al-Fadl ibn Abbas, Khalid ibn Al-Walid, and another woman, when Khawan Ali was brought near to him. Meat. When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, wanted to eat it, Maimunah said to him: It is lizard meat, so he stopped. He held out his hand and said: I have never eaten this meat before, and he said to them: Eat, so Al-Fadl bin Abbas and Khaled bin Al-Walid ate from it. And the woman, and Maimunah said: I do not eat except from something from which the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, has eaten (Muslim 1545. Ahmed 1/294)"
24835,"(24835) Abdul Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Al-Zabarqan, he said: A grilled lizard was given as a gift to Shaqiq bin Salama. So I ate from it."
24836,"(24836) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, left. Then a famine struck them, and a man came to him carrying fog, so he gave it to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he looked. To her, he said: A tribe of the Children of Israel transformed animals on the earth, but they did not eat them, nor did they forbid them."
24837,"(24837) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, saying: Mis’ar narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Aoun, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Layla; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, smelled the scent of a lizard, so he gave them permission to eat it."
24838,"(24838) Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, saying: Mis’ar narrated to us, on the authority of Ziyad ibn Alaqah; Omar saw a man with a good body, and he asked him or told him, and he said: Who ate the lizard? So Omar said: I wish there was a lizard in every hole. Dhabine."
24839,"(24839) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, who said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked about the lizard? He said: I will not eat it, nor will I deprive it of it. (Abdul Razzaq 8673)"
24840,"(24840) Zayd ibn Harun told us, he said: Dawud informed us, on the authority of Abu Nadhrah, he said: Omar said: Indeed, God is of benefit. With the lizard, it is the food of common shepherds, and if I had it, I would eat from it."
24841,"(24841) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ziyad bin Alaqi, on the authority of Saad bin Ma’abad; Omar saw a fat man from among the warriors one year, and he said: What do you eat? He said: Fog. He said: I wish there were two fogs in every hole."
24842,"(24842) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab, who said: Umar said: A lizard is more beloved to me than Chicken"
24843,"(24843) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Toubah al-Anbari, on the authority of Shu`bi, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked May God bless him and grant him peace from the lizard? He said: It is permissible and there is no problem with it, but I spare it."
24844,"(24844) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Minhal, on the authority of his uncle, who said: I asked Abu Hurairah about the lizard? He said: I neither eat it nor refrain from it."
24845,"(24845) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Abi Aoun, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Laila; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, smelled the smell of a lizard, and said: “I am, or we are from a people who do not eat it,” and he made a concession to them. Eat it"
24846,"(24846) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abdul-Jabbar bin Abbas, on the authority of Oraib Al-Hamdani, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali; He hated the lizard."
24847,"(24847) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abd al-A’la, who said: I asked Ibn al-Hanafiyyah about the lizard? He said: If you like it, eat it."
24848,"(24848) Abdī narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Rukān, on the authority of Ismā ibn Rabi’ī, who said: We came to Omar and we are fat, good-looking people. Here we are, he said: So he said: What is your food? We said: Fog. He said: Then Omar said: Will it reward you? We said: Yes, and he said: I wish there was something like it for every lizard."
24849,"(24849) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: A man came to Ibn Abbas and said: Do you eat spleen? He said: Yes, but spilled blood is forbidden."
24850,"(24850) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Misra, he said: I I eat spleen and whatever I like, but I hate to deprive it of it."
24851,"(24851) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He did not see any harm in the spleen."
24852,"(24852) Abd al-Rahim and Waki` told us, on the authority of Fitr, on the authority of Mundhir, on the authority of Muhammad ibn al-Hanafiyyah; When he was asked about running and spleen, Waki’ would say: And other things that he dislikes? He recited these verses: {Say: I do not find in what has been revealed to me forbidden}."
24853,"(24853) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, or someone else, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: There is no harm in the spleen."
24854,"(24854) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, on the authority of Ali bin Abi Talib, He said: He did not eat chickpeas or spleen."
24855,"(24855) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali, who said: The spleen is the mouth of Satan."
24856,"(24856) Jarir told us, on the authority of Qaboos, on the authority of his father; A woman asked Aisha and she said: We have some of the Magians, and they have the Eid and they make gifts for us? She said: As for what has been slaughtered on that day, do not eat, but eat from their trees."
24857,"(24857) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Hakim, on the authority of his mother, on the authority of Abu Barzah; He had Magi residents, and they used to offer him guidance on Nowruz and the festival, so he used to say to his family: “What was it?” Whoever eats it, eat it, and whatever is other than that, return it."
24858,"(24858) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Abu Wael, and Ibrahim, who said: When the Muslims came, they were struck by He fed the Magi; Of their cheese and of their bread, and they ate and were not asked about any of that."
24859,"(24859) Abu Osama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: He hated to eat what the Magians cooked in Their pots, and he did not see any harm in eating from their food other than that; Bread, or ghee, or kamakh, or shiraz, or milk."
24860,"(24860) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata, who said: There is no harm in the Magi’s bread."
24861,"(24861) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Do not eat the food of the Magians except Fruits"
24862,"(24862) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Abu Barza, who said: We were on a campaign, and we met people. Of the polytheists, so We caused them to abstain from a group of theirs, so we fell into it and began to eat from it, and we were listening to it. The Jahiliyya says that whoever eats bread becomes fat, so when we ate that bread, he made one of us look at his kindness. Was he fat? ?"
24863,"(24863) Yazeed told us, he said: Hisham told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Muhammad, they said: The polytheists used to bring ghee. In their circumstances, the Companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the Muslims bought it and ate it, and we We eat it"
24864,"(24864) Jarir told us, on the authority of Mansour, he said: I asked Ibrahim about mountain ghee? He said: The Arab is more beloved to me than the Arab, and we will eat from the Jabaliya."
24865,"(24865) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad; He saw nothing wrong with mountain ghee."
24866,"(24866) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Uthman, who said: We used to eat ghee, but we did not eat dung. We do not ask about circumstances."
24867,"(24867) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Muhammad; Amer bin Abdullah used to hate ghee that came from this, meaning the mountain, and he did not see any harm in it. He comes from here, meaning the desert."
24868,"(24868) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: He did not see any harm in eating watery ghee."
24869,"(24869) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Abu Razin, who said: They used to stir mountain ghee with water from cheese."
24870,"(24870) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Makhul, on the authority of Abu Idris, on the authority of Abu Tha’labah al-Khushani. He said: I said: O Messenger of God, we are invading the enemy’s land and we need your equipment. He said: Dispense with them as much as you can, and if not If you find something else, wash it, and eat and drink from it. (Tabarani 568)"
24871,"(24871) Ismail bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Burd, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, who said: We used to fight with The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, is the land of the polytheists, so we do not refrain from eating from their utensils and drinking from them. I gave them something to drink. (Abu Dawud 3834. Ahmad 3/327)"
24872,"(24872) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Urwa bin Abdullah Al-Qushayri Abi Al-Minhal, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, he said: The companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to prevail over the polytheists, and they would eat in their vessels, and they drink from their water vessels."
24873,"(24873) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abdullah bin Naji; Hudhayf was given a drink of water, so Deqan brought him a bowl containing wine, so he washed it and drank from it."
24874,"(24874) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: They used to hate the vessels of the infidels, so if They did not find any of it, so they washed it and cooked in it."
24875,"(24875) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If you need the pots and vessels of the Magians, So wash it and cook it."
24876,"(24876) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Omar bin Al-Walid Al-Shinni, who said: I asked Saeed bin Jubayr about the powers of the Magi? He said: Wash it and cook in it."
24877,"(24877) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Maymunah; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked about an elephant that fell into ghee and died? He said: Throw it and everything around it, and eat it. (Bukhari 5538, Abu Dawud 3837)"
24878,"(24878) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Hurairah; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked about a woman who died of fat? He said: So he ordered her to be taken and around her to be thrown away. (Abu Dawud 3838)"
24879,"(24879) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Misra, on the authority of Ali; Concerning the mouse falling into the ghee, he said: If it is melted, throw it out, and if it is solid, throw it and what is around it, and eat The rest of it"
24880,"(24880) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Ibn Sirin; Al-Ash'ari was asked about ghee in which a gecko died? He said: Sell it at all costs, and do not sell it to a Muslim."
24881,"(24881) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Nafi’; That a rat fell into a pot belonging to the family of Ibn Omar, and he was asked? He said: Benefit from it, and treat people with it."
24882,"(24882) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Safiyya bint Abi Ubaid; A jar belonging to the family of Ibn Omar contained twenty pieces of ghee or more, and a woman fell into it and saw it and died. So Ibn Omar ordered them to They will wake up with it."
24883,"(24883) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hamran ibn Ayn, on the authority of Abu Harb ibn Abi al-Aswad, he said: Ibn Masoud reported that he saw a mouse that fell into ghee and died? He said: God only forbade the flesh and blood of the dead."
24884,"(24884) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya ibn Ayyub, who said: Abu Qubayl informed me, on the authority of Tabi’a ibn A woman like Ka`b, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, who said: If a mouse falls into oil and dies, it is not permissible to eat it. For a Muslim, nor for a Jew, nor for a Christian."
24885,"(24885) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Jamil ibn Ubaid al-Tai, who said: Thumama ibn Abdullah ibn Anas narrated to me, On the authority of his grandfather Anas; He was asked about a mouse falling into ghee or oil? He said: If it is solid, they are taken and everything around it is taken and thrown away, and what is left is eaten, and if it is melted, they are taken in the morning with it."
24886,"(24886) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Ja’far bin Burqan, on the authority of Thabit bin Al-Hajjaj, who said: Aisha said: If it was If it is solid, throw it away, and whatever is next to it, and everything that remains. If it is liquid, do not eat it."
24887,"(24887) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If the bleeding occurred in melted ghee and she died in it, she did not It can be eaten, and if it is solid, the inventory and what is around it should be thrown away, and anything else can be eaten."
24888,"(24888) Hushaym told us, saying: Yunus told me that Al-Hasan and Muhammad said: He has that."
24889,"(24889) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, similar to that."
24890,"(24890) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Abdul-Malik, on the authority of Ata’, who said: If he was immobile, then he threw it and did not Layla and everything that is left, but if it is melted, then eat it in the morning and do not eat it."
24891,"(24891) Abdul-Wahhab Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of cold, on the authority of alcohol; I saw that it fell into oil, so they asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace? He said: Eat it in the morning and do not eat it. And Makhoul used to say: If it falls into ghee, and it is frozen, then it is thrown and what is around it, and anything else is eaten, even if it is It melted and nothing was eaten from it."
24892,"(24892) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; He was asked about a vision that fell into solid fat? So he ordered that whatever was around it be thrown and the rest of it be eaten."
24893,"(24893) Hushaym told us, he said: Abu Hamza told us, he said: I heard Ibn Abbas and he was asked about cowardice? He said: Put the knife in it, mention the name of God, and eat."
24894,"(24894) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Abu Hayyan Al-Azdi, he said, I asked Ibn Omar about cowardice? He said: Nothing has come to us from Iraq that is more amazing to us than this."
24895,"(24895) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Qardha, who said: Omar said: Eat cheese, for it is colostrum and milk."
24896,"(24896) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Tamlik. She said: Did I ask Umm Salama? She said: Put your knife in it, and mention the name of God Almighty, and eat."
24897,"(24897) Salam narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Masruq, on the authority of Mundhir, on the authority of Ibn al-Hanafiyyah, they said: Eat cheese casually."
24898,"(24898) Yahya bin Sa’id told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Rabi’a, on the authority of his maternal aunt, she said: We brought cheese from Iraq, so she sent to Aisha and said: Eat and feed me."
24899,"(24899) Hushaym narrated to us, saying: Mughirah narrated to us, on the authority of Abraham, he said: Omar wrote: Mention the name of God over cowardice. And eat. Ibrahim said: When we traveled to these mountains, we saw the work of foreigners, what we saw, we disliked it, except that... We ask about him."
24900,"(24900) Ubaidah bin Humaid told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ubaid bin Abi Al-Jaad, on the authority of Qays bin Al-Sakan, he said Abdullah said: Do not eat cheese except what the Muslims and the People of the Book have made."
24901,"(24901) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ja`far al-Razi, on the authority of al-Rabi’, on the authority of Abu al-Aaliyah, on the authority of Suwayd, a boy who was To Salman and praised him well, he said: When we conquered Al-Mada'in, people went out in search of the enemy. He said: Salman said: We were struck. He asked him, and he said: Open it. If it is food, we will eat it, and if it is money, we will give it to those people. He said: So we opened it. So, behold, loaves of bread and a knife. He said: This was the first time the Arabs saw the hawari. So Salman began describing Tell them how to do it, then he took the knife and started cutting it, and said: In the name of God, eat."
24902,"(24902) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Ibn Sirin, who said: There is no harm in what the People of the Book did. Cowardice"
24903,"(24903) Abbad told us, on the authority of Abdul-Malik, he said: I asked Saeed bin Jubayr about cowardice? He said: What did the Muslims and the People of the Book do?"
24904,"(24904) Abu Osama told us, on the authority of Abdul-Malik, he said: I heard Saeed bin Jubayr saying: Do not eat cheese except What the Muslims, Jews, and Christians did, as for the Magians, their sacrifices are not permissible for us, so how can their cowardice be permissible for us? ?"
24905,"(24905) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Abu Wael, and Ibrahim, who said: When the Muslims came, they were struck by The Magi fed him with their bread and cheese, and they ate and were not asked about that. He described the cheese to Omar, and he said: Mention the name of God upon him, and eat of him."
24906,"(24906) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: When we came to the mountain and saw what they did, We hated it."
24907,"(24907) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Umm Musa, on the authority of Ali, who said: If you do not know who made it, then mention the name of God. On him, and eat him."
24908,"(24908) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Shaqiq, on the authority of Amr ibn Shurahbil, he said: We mentioned cowardice when... Omar, so we said to him: Indeed, the most harmonious of the dead is made of him, and he said: Summon him and eat him."
24909,"(24909) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jahsh, on the authority of Mu’awiyah ibn Qurayh, on the authority of Al-Hasan ibn Ali; He was asked about cowardice? He said: There is no harm in it, put down the knives, mention the name of God upon it and eat."
24910,"(24910) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Amr bin Othman, on the authority of Musa bin Talha, who said: I heard him mention: Talha used to put down the knife, mention the name of God, and cut and eat."
24911,"(24911) Hafs told us, on the authority of Al-Zabarqan, on the authority of Abu Razin, who said: There is no harm in cowardice."
24912,"(24912) Hafs told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Amara, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Abdul-Rahman bin Al-Harith, he said: They were They feed themselves with cowardice on their journeys."
24913,"(24913) Issa bin Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Amr bin Mansour, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, came. During his invasion of Tabuk, he greeted him with cowardice, and it was said: This is food made by the Magians, so he said: Mention the name of God upon him. And eat it
(Abu Dawud 3815)"
24914,"(24914) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Salem; He used to eat Kufi cheese."
24915,"(24915) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Uthman al-Shahham, he said: Al-Nushjan Abu Al-Mughirah told us, he said: I asked Ibn Abbas about Cowardice? He said: No fruit comes to us from Iraq more wonderful to us than cowardice."
24916,"(24916) Ubaidah bin Humaid told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Sa’id bin Ubaidah, who said: A man asked Ibn Umar. About cowardice? Ibn Omar said to him: What is cowardice? He said: From milk, so Ibn Omar said to him: Eat cheese and drink it, so he said: Is there death in it? Then Ibn Omar said to him: Do not eat the dead."
24917,"(24917) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ali Al-Azdi, who said: I said to Ibn Umar: We will travel and pass. With the shepherds, the child, and the woman, and they give us meat of which we do not know what kind it is? He said: Whatever the Muslims feed you, eat."
24918,"(24918) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ajlan, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said : If you come to your Muslim brother and he feeds you food, then eat and do not ask. If he gives you a drink, then drink and do not ask. If he asks you, If there is any of it, wash it with water."
24919,"(24919) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Omar Al-Ansari, who said: I heard Anas bin Malik say: If you enter upon a man Do not displease him in his stomach, so eat from his food and drink from his drink."
24920,"(24920) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Ismail, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, who said: What I found in... The Muslim house, so eat."
24921,"(24921) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Ziyad, who said: We entered upon a shepherd who invited us for food. He brought us some wine, which I disliked, so Ali took it. Abu Bakr said: It should be the son of Al-Hussein bin Ali. So he drank it and said: When you visit your Muslim brother, eat his food and drink his drink."
24922,"(24922) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Musa bin Umair, who said: I heard Al-Sha’bi say: If you enter a Muslim’s house, eat from His food, and his drink."
24923,"(24923) Abdul Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, she said: They said: O Messenger of God, the Bedouins bring us meat, but we do not know what it is. Has the name of God been mentioned upon it, or not? He said: Give him the blessings and eat him. (Bukhari 2057, Darmi 1976)"
24924,"(24924) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he heard Abu Bakr bin Ubaid Allah bin Abdullah tell about his grandfather. On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: Satan eats with his left hand and drinks with his left hand, so when one of you eats Let him eat with his right hand, and let him drink with his right hand. (Muslim 1050, Abu Dawud 3770)"
24925,"(24925) Zayd ibn Harun told us, he said: Hisham ibn Hassan informed us, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Diqan, on the authority of Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: When one of you eats, let him eat with his right hand, and let him drink. With his right hand, for Satan eats with his left hand and drinks with his left hand. (Ahmad 3/202, Abu Ali 4256)"
24926,"(24926) Marwan bin Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Abdul Malik, on the authority of Ubaid bin Salman, on the authority of Al-Dahhak bin Muzahim, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: Do not eat with your left hand, and do not drink with your left hand, for Adam ate with his left hand and forgot, so he inherited that from him. Forgetting"
24927,"(24927) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Walid Ibn Kathir, on the authority of Wahb Ibn Kaysan, he heard it from Omar Ibn Abi He greeted him. He said: I was a boy in the lap of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and my hand used to wander around the newspaper, so he said to me: Boy, in the name of God, and eat with your right hand, and eat from what follows you. (Bukhari 5376. Muslim 108)"
24928,"(24928) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of my father, and Jazā al-Sa’di, on the authority of a man From Muzainah, on the authority of Omar bin Abi Salamah, who said: I entered upon the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was eating, and he said: Sit. My son, and say: In the name of God, and eat with your right hand, and eat from what suits you. (Abu Dawud 3771, An-Nasa’i 6756)"
24929,"(24929) Yahya bin Saeed Al-Qattan told us, on the authority of Amara bin Mutarrif, on the authority of Burayd bin Abi Maryam, on the authority of his father, He said: Omar bin Al-Khattab saw a man who was striking with his left hand to eat with it. He said: No, unless it is your hand. Ailing, or sick."
24930,"(24930) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Jabir bin Subh, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Abi Jarwa, on the authority of his paternal aunt; Aisha saw a woman eating with her left hand, so she stopped her."
24931,"(24931) Azhar narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, who said: I drank with Muhammad with my left hand, but he did not forbid me."
24932,"(24932) Zaid bin Al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Ikrimah bin Ammar, on the authority of Iyas bin Salama; That his father told him: A man ate with the left hand of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: Eat with your right hand. He said: “I cannot,” he said: “No, you cannot.” Nothing prevented him except pride. He said: “No one raised it except in it.” (Muslim 1071, Ahmad 4/45)"
24933,"(24933) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Sulaiman, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, who said: He forbade The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, told him to eat one of us with his left hand. (Muslim 104, Abu Dawud 4134)"
24934,"(24934) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: And peace be upon him: When one of you tastes food, he should not wipe his hand until he has sucked it, for he does not know in which food he will be blessed. Therein
(Muslim 1607. Ibn Majah 3270)"
24935,"(24935) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: If one of you eats food, he should not wipe it until he licks it, or he licks it. (Bukhari 5456. Muslim 129)"
24936,"(24936) Suwayd bin Amr told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace When God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ate, he licked his three fingers and said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded us to remove the pages. He said: None of you knows what kind of food he will be blessed with. (Muslim 1607. Abu Dawud 3841)"
24937,"(24937) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Kaab bin Malik, On the authority of his father, he said: I saw the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, licking his three fingers from food. (Muslim 131. An-Nasa’i 6752)"
24938,"(24938) Jarir told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of Ata, who said: Omar said: It is not appropriate for a Muslim, if he eats food, to He wipes his hand until he licks it, or licks it."
24939,"(24939) Hushaym told us, saying: Husayn told us, on the authority of Mujahid, he said: I never saw Ibn Umar perform ablution with food. He never licked his three fingers, then wiped his hand with dirt."
24940,"(24940) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abdul-Malik, on the authority of Ata’, who said: The companions of the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, when food is brought near, they do not wipe their hands until they purify them by licking them."
24941,"(24941) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, saying: I said to Ubaid Allah ibn Abi Yazeed: Were you watching Ibn Abbas’ food? He said: Yes, I said: What did you see him doing? He said: I saw him licking his three fingers."
24942,"(24942) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir; The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, ordered the licking of fingers and newspapers, and said: You do not know what the blessing is in. (Muslim 133)"
24943,"(24943) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Salih, and Abu Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: When one of you has finished his food, let him lick his fingers, for he does not know what his food is in. Blessed be He.
(Muslim 136)"
24944,"(24944) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He used to lick his three fingers when he ate, and he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: He does not know what What is blessed food? (Ahmed 2/7)"
24945,"(24945) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: And he said: If a morsel falls from the hand of one of you, let him wipe off any dirt on it and eat it.
(Muslim 1607. Ibn Majah 3279)"
24946,"(24946) Abdul-Wahhab Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Anas; A morsel fell from his hand, so they searched for it until they found it, and said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: If it fell If one of you licks a morsel, let him sprinkle what is on it, then eat it, and do not leave it to Satan. (Ahmed 100)"
24947,"(24947) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ata’ ibn al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Sa’id ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger said: God, may God bless him and grant him peace: When food is served, eat from its edge and leave its middle, for the blessing descends in its middle. (Abu Dawud 3766. Tirmidhi 1805)"
24948,"(24948) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Miqsam, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: When the bowl is placed, eat from it. Around it, and leave its peaks, for at its peaks is blessing."
24949,"(24949) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Sa’id bin Huwayrith, I heard Ibn Abbas say: We were with The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came after defecation and was brought food, and it was said to him: Will you not perform ablution? He said: I did not pray and perform ablution.
(Muslim 1198, Ahmad 1/221)"
24950,"(24950) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, he said: Omar ibn Al-Khattab came out of the toilet and brought food, and they said: We called for ablution, and he said: I only eat with my right hand, and I feel good with my left. So he ate and did not touch water."
24951,"(24951) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Salim bin Abi Al-Ja’d, on the authority of his father; Ibn Masoud invited a man to his meal, and he said: You have urinated. He said: You have not urinated on your hand."
24952,"(24952) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Mansur, on the authority of Salim bin Abi Al-Ja’d, on the authority of his father, He said: Abdullah invited a man to eat, and he said: I have urinated. He said: Your urine is not on your hand."
24953,"(24953) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Akhi Al-Zuhri, who said: My sister told me; She saw Al-Zuhri eating for five, so she asked him about that? He said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to eat for five."
24954,"(24954) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Khaled bin Abi Bakr, who said: I saw Al-Qasim and Salim eating for three Fingers"
24955,"(24955) Abdī narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwah, on the authority of Ibn Ka’b, on the authority of his father; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to eat with his three fingers, and he would lick them. (Muslim 1605. Abu Dawud 3844)"
24956,"(24956) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Issa bin Hattan, on the authority of Musab bin Saad, on the authority of his father; If his chest complained, he would make soup for him with garlic in it and he would make it soup."
24957,"(24957) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Nafi’; If Ibn Umar had a chest complaint, he would make soup for him with garlic in it, and they would eat it."
24958,"(24958) Issa bin Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Abu Ubaid Hajib Sulayman, on the authority of Nu’aym bin Salamah, He said: I entered upon Omar bin Abdul Aziz, and found him eating boiled garlic with salt and oil."
24959,"(24959) Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Imran bin Hudayr, who said: Ikrimah was asked about him? He said: We will eat it for a week or two, but we will leave the city."
24960,"(24960) Khalaf bin Khalifa told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibn Sirin; He did not see any harm in eating garlic and onions raw."
24961,"(24961) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, who said: We eat garlic and onions. And leeks."
24962,"(24962) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: There is no harm in garlic in cooking."
24963,"(24963) Abu Osama told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad, he said: Omar said: Whoever eats anything from these two trees, Let their fragrance ripen, meaning onions and leeks."
24964,"(24964) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: I do not know of any harm in eating garlic, unless a man hates it. His scent"
24965,"(24965) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He used to cook it in pots and eat it."
24966,"(24966) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Yazeed, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Umm Ayyub, she said: It was revealed The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, is upon us, so we prepared food for him from some legumes. He disapproved of it and said: I am not Like you, I fear that I will harm my companion."
24967,"(24967) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, saying: Ubaid Allah bin Omar narrated to us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Omar; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever eats from these herbs should not approach the mosque until It removes its fragrance, meaning garlic."
24968,"(24968) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Salim bin Abdullah bin Yazid, on the authority of Hudhayfy’s cook, he said: He was Hudhayf ordered me not to put leeks in his food."
24969,"(24969) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Adiy, on the authority of Zirr bin Hubaysh, on the authority of Hudhayfy, who said: Who He ate garlic, so let him not bring it to us three times."
24970,"(24970) Ismail Ibn Aliyya told us, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Hamid Ibn Hilal, on the authority of Abu Burda; The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, found the smell of garlic from the smell of garlic, and said: Did I not forbid you from this tree? He said: O Messenger of God, I have sworn to you that you will enter into your hand. He said: And he is wearing a robe or a shirt. So he entered into your hand, and lo! With a bandage on his chest, he said: I see an excuse for you."
24971,"(24971) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hakam bin Atiyya, on the authority of Abul-Rubab, on the authority of Maqil bin Yasar, he said: I heard him say: We were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on a journey, and he said: Whoever eats from this tree, let him not. They bring our prayer nearer."
24972,"(24972) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Mu’tamar narrated to us, on the authority of his father, saying: Al-Hasan saw leeks with his mother, and he said: My nation, throw down this evil tree."
24973,"(24973) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: And he greeted: Whoever eats of this herb should not approach our mosque, or he said: the mosque."
24974,"(24974) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Suleiman bin Al-Mughirah, on the authority of Hamid bin Hilal, on the authority of Abu Burda, on the authority of Al-Mugheerah bin Shu’ba said: I ate garlic, then I came to the prayer area of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I found that he had preceded me. He prayed, and when he prayed, I stood up and finished, and he smelled the smell and said: Whoever eats of these vegetables should not approach our mosque. Until its scent goes away, Al-Mughirah said: When I finished the prayer, I went to him and said: O Messenger of God, I have an excuse. He gave me your hand. He said: I found him at ease, by God. So he gave me his hand, and I brought it to my chest. He found him tied up. He said: You have an excuse."
24975,"(24975) Al-Fadl ibn Dukayn narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq, on the authority of Umair ibn Qumaym, on the authority of Sharik ibn Hanbal, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever eats of these vile vegetables should not offer them. Our mosque, meaning garlic."
24976,"(24976) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Salim bin Abi al-Ja’d, on the authority of Ma’dan bin Abi Talha Omar bin Al-Khattab said: You are eating two trees that I do not see as anything but evil: this garlic and this onion. I used to see a man at the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, having a scent coming from him, and he would be taken by the hand until He will be taken out with it to Al-Baqi', and whoever eats it must surely die while cooking it. (Muslim 3971, Ahmad 1/27)"
24977,"(24977) Yunus bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Abu Al-Khair, on the authority of Abu Rahim Al-Sama'i; That Abu Ayyub narrated to him on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: It contains onions, so eat them, and I hate to eat them from For his sake, meaning the kingdom, but as for you, eat it. (Muslim 1700, Ahmad 5/413)"
24978,"(24978) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He hated eating garlic, onions, and leeks."
24979,"(24979) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Abdul Karim Abi Umayyah, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: I am not pleased that I ate it, meaning garlic, but I did not have a zina of gold."
24980,"(24980) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Jabalah ibn Suhaim, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of God forbade May God bless him and grant him peace from the Qur’an, unless you ask your companions for permission. (Bukhari 5446. Tirmidhi 1814)"
24981,"(24981) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Musa bin Diqan, who said: I saw Salim bin Abdullah eating dates, one by one."
24982,"(24982) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Abu Jahsh, on the authority of Abu Hurairah; He ate dates with his friends, so he said: I have compared, so they compared."
24983,"(24983) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Habiba bint Abbad, on the authority of her mother, who said: I asked Aisha about the Qur’an between Two dates? She said: If it were lawful, it would be lowly."
24984,"(24984) Zaid bin Al-Hubab narrated to us, saying: Ya’qub bin Muhammad bin Tahla’ narrated to us, saying: Abu Al-Rijal narrated to us, on the authority of his mother. Omar, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to me: O Aisha, a house in which there are no dates. His family is hungry. (Muslim 1531, Abu Dawud 3827)"
24985,"(24985) Abd bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Abu Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: They used to prefer not He dispersed the dates from their homes. Abraham said: And I will explain it: It was when a foreigner entered upon them and they wanted his dignity, so they imprisoned him. And they brought him close to him, and if he ate from it, they honored him, but if he did not eat, then it was sufficient for them. Ibrahim said: And another; The beggar comes, but the Ahl al-Bayt has no bread, nor does he allow themselves to gather flour and wheat for him. So they will give him one date, two dates, and the like, so he will do without the need of the Ahl al-Bayt, and the beggar will be kept straight with it."
24986,"(24986) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Mus’ab bin Sulaym, on the authority of Anas, who said: I saw the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, eating Filled with dates. (Muslim 1616. Abu Dawud 3765)"
24987,"(24987) Abu Asama and Muhammad bin Bishr told us, on the authority of Zakaria bin Abi Zaydah, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Burda. On the authority of Anas bin Malik, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: God is pleased with a servant if he eats He eats something and praises Him for it, or drinks something and praises Him for it. (Muslim 89. Tirmidhi 1816)"
24988,"(24988) Abu Asama told us, he said: Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid bin Jabir told us, he said: Bishr bin Ziyad told us, on the authority of Suleiman bin Abdullah, on the authority of Atris bin Arqub, said: Abdullah said: Whoever says when his food is put out: In the name of God is good. The names. To God belongs everything that is on earth and in the heavens. No disease is harmed by His name. O God, place in it a blessing, a well-being, and a cure. That food is harmful to him no matter what it is."
24989,"(24989) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali, who said: If you eat food and forget to say the name, So say: In the name of God, at the beginning and at the end."
24990,"(24990) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Tamim bin Salamah, who said: It was narrated that if a man mentions the name of God over his food And He praised Him for His last reward. He was not asked about the blessings of that food."
24991,"(24991) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim Al-Taymi, on the authority of Al-Harith bin Suwayd, he said: Salman was When he tastes it, he says: Praise be to God, who has sufficed us with our provisions and made sustenance abundant for us."
24992,"(24992) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Riyah ibn Ubaidah, on the authority of a servant of Abu Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Saeed, he said: Whenever the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ate food, he would say: Praise be to God, who fed us and gave us drink, and made us Muslims (Tirmidhi 3457, Abu Dawud 3846)"
24993,"(24993) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, saying: Mis’ar narrated to us, on the authority of Hilal, on the authority of Urwa; When the food was served, he would say: Glory be to You, what you have bestowed upon us, Glory be to You, what you have bestowed upon us, our Lord and our Lord. Our children, and the Lord of our forefathers. He said: Then God, glory be to Him, will name him and lay down his hand."
24994,"(24994) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Asim bin Abi Al-Najjoud, on the authority of Dhakwan Abi Salih, on the authority of Aisha; He offered her food, and she said: Eat it. They said: What is an edamame? She said: Thank God for it when you finish."
24995,"(24995) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Saeed, he said: Abu Saeed was Al-Khudri, when the food was served, said: Praise be to God who has fed us and given us drink, and made us Muslims."
24996,"(24996) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Saeed, on the authority of his father; In the same way"
24997,"(24997) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of al-Jariri, on the authority of Abu al-Ward, on the authority of Ibn Abad, or Ibn Ma`abad, He said: Ali said: Do you know what is the right of food? I said: What is his right? He said: You say in the name of God, O God, bless us with what You have provided for us. He said: Do you know what he thanked him for? I said: What is his gratitude? He said: You say: Praise be to God who has fed us and given us drink."
24998,"(24998) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Ibrahim al-Taymi. He used to say: Praise be to God who fed us and gave us drink."
24999,"(24999) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Ibrahim al-Taymi. He used to say: Praise be to God who has sufficed us with our provisions and made provision good for us."
25000,"(25000) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, he said: My father would not be given food or drink, even medicines. So he gives him food or drinks until he says: Praise be to God who guided us, fed us, gave us drink, and bestowed blessings upon us. God is Greatest. O God, protect us with your grace from all evil, and protect us morning and evening from it with all good, we ask you for its completeness and thanks, not There is no god but God, there is no god but God. There is no god but Allah. There is no god but Allah. Whatever God wills, there is no strength except in God, O God, bless for us what You have provided for us, and protect us from the torment of the Fire."
25001,"(25001) Al-Hasan bin Musa told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr; When he finished eating, he would say: O God, you have satisfied and quenched your thirst, so congratulate us, and you have provided for us, so you have been abundant and well-pleased. So we increased."
25002,"(25002) Muawiyah bin Hisham told us, he said: Ammar bin Ruzaq told us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Abi Hafsiya, On the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr; He said: When food is served and you say the name, then eat whatever was brought with it, then the first namism is sufficient for you."
25003,"(25003) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Ziyad, who said: Tell me who saw Ibn Abbas He eats while reclining."
25004,"(25004) Fudayl bin Iyad narrated to us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Rafi’, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not eat. May God bless him and grant him peace. He never reclined except once, when he said: Oh God, I am your servant and your messenger."
25005,"(25005) Hisham told us, on the authority of Husayn, who said: When Khalid ibn al-Walid came here, behold, he was armed with the Persians. There came over them a man called: Hazarmurrud. He said: They mentioned the greatness of his character and his courage. He said: Then Khalid bin al-Walid killed him. Then He called for his lunch and he had lunch while leaning on his body, meaning his body."
25006,"(25006) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: If we eat while reclining."
25007,"(25007) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: They hated to eat. Hiding, for fear that their bellies will grow large."
25008,"(25008) Abu Osama told us, on the authority of Abu Hilal, who said: I saw Ibn Sirin eating while reclining."
25009,"(25009) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Ali bin Al-Aqmar, on the authority of Abu Juhayf, who narrates it, he said: As for me, I do not eat. Reclining (Bukhari 5398 and Tirmidhi 1830)"
25010,"(25010) Zayd bin Harun told us, he said: Hussam bin Misk told us, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, he said: I entered upon Ubaidah So I asked him about a man who eats while reclining? So he ate while reclining."
25011,"(25011) Waki’ and Abu Bakr bin Ayyash narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Amr Al-Shaybani, who said: Abdullah bin Masoud was with a man of dirhams, and he said: What do you do with these dirhams? He said: This, Abu Abdul Rahman, is thirty dirhams. I want to buy ghee with it for Ramadan. He said: You put it in it. What do you eat and drink? He said: Yes, he said: Go and give it to your wife, and he ordered her to buy meat every day for a dirham, so it is. Good for you"
25012,"(25012) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of the one who narrated to him, he said: Jabir passed by Omar with meat that he had bought for a dirham, and he said: Laha Omar: What is this? He said: I bought it for a dirham. He said: Whenever you crave something, you buy it? Do not be among the people of these verses: {You have withheld your good things in your worldly lives}"
25013,"(25013) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Hamza bin Abdullah; Al-Hasan had half a dirham of meat every day."
25014,"(25014) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Raja’ bin Abi Salamah, who said: Omar bin Abdul Aziz used to prepare food. He brought it, but he did not eat from it, and they did not eat it. He said: What is the matter with them that they do not eat it? They said: If you do not eat, then they will not eat. So he ordered a dirham each day from his wealth, which he spent on cooking, so he ate. And they ate"
25015,"(25015) Humayd and Al-Fadl narrated to us, on the authority of Zuhayr, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, who said: Al-Sha’bi used to buy every collection. A dirham of meat."
25016,"(25016) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Zuhair, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, he said: Omar said: His family is sufficient. A house during the month is worth three dirhams of meat."
25017,"(25017) Yahya bin Yaman told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Ubaid, on the authority of Ali bin Rabi’i, he said: It was for Ali Two women. He used to buy meat every day for this woman for half a dirham, and for this woman for half a dirham."
25018,"(25018) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hazzam bin Hisham, on the authority of his father, who said: Omar said to his sons: Do not continue to eat meat. Do not immerse yourself in fresh water, and do not continue to wear your shirt."
25019,"(25019) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Rafi’, on the authority of Al-Qaqa’ bin Hakim, who said: Aisha said: O my son Tamim, do not continue to eat meat, for it is as harmful as wine."
25020,"(25020) Ali ibn Mushir narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwah, on the authority of his father, who said: If the man was to blame for not He is patient with meat."
25021,"(25021) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Habib bin Shahid, on the authority of Ibn Buraidah; Salman used to make food from his earnings, and he would invite the lepers and eat with them."
25022,"(25022) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of a man; He saw Ibn Umar eating with a leper, so he put his hand where the leper’s hand was."
25023,"(25023) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin al-Qasim, on the authority of his father, he said: He came before Abu Bakr A delegation from Thaqif brought food. The people approached and a man left with this disease, meaning leprosy. Abu said to him: Bakr: He came closer, so he approached, and he said: Eat, so he ate and made Abu Bakr put his hand where his hand was."
25024,"(25024) Yunus bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Mufaddal bin Fadalah, on the authority of Habib bin Shahid, on the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Mundakir, On the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, took the hand of a leper and placed it with him in a bowl, and said: Eat, in the name of God. Trust in God, and put your trust in God. (Abu Dawud 3921, Ibn Majah 3542)"
25025,"(25025) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Yahya bin Ja’di, who said: A black man came who had smallpox. He frowned and did not sit next to anyone unless he made him stay, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, took him and made him sit next to him. beside him"
25026,"(25026) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Bukair, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: A leper attached to Ibn Abbas. So I said to him: Are you attached to a leper? He said: Go ahead, for perhaps he is better than you and me."
25027,"(25027) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Qays, on the authority of Miqsam, who said: They used to fear lest they eat with the blind man. And the lame and the sick, until these verses were revealed: {There is no burden upon the blind, nor upon the lame, nor upon the sick}."
25028,"(25028) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Mundhir, on the authority of Al-Rabi’ bin Khuthaym; He said to his family: Make something for me. He said: So they did. He said: So he called a man who was suffering from dementia. He said: So he made the spring feed him. His saliva was dripping, and when he ate and left, his family said to him: We treated him and treated him badly. Did you feed him? This man does not know what he ate. Al-Rabi’ said: But God knows."
25029,"(25029) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Nafi’ ibn al-Qasim, on the authority of his grandmother Umm al-Qasim, on the authority of Aisha, she said: He was a servant of mine. A leper, he used to sleep in my bed and eat in newspapers, and if he had lived, he would have remained that way."
25030,"(25030) Hushaym and Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Ali bin Ata, on the authority of Amr bin Al-Sharid, on the authority of his father, he said: There was a leper in the Thaqif delegation, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent to him: We have pledged allegiance to you, so return. (Muslim 1264. Ahmad 4/389)"
25031,"(25031) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Nāṣ ibn Qaym, on the authority of a sheikh, who said: I heard Abu Hurairah say: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Flee from a leper, as you flee from a lion. (Bukhari 417. Ahmad 2/443)"
25032,"(25032) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Saeed, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Amr bin Othman, on the authority of his mother Fatima bint Hussein, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Do not keep looking at the lepers.
(Bukhari 417. Ahmad 1/233)"
25033,"(25033) Muhammad bin Sawai told us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Abu Qalab; It was astonishing for him to avoid the leper.
(Abdul Razzaq 20331)"
25034,"(25034) Abu Asama told us, he said: Ubad Allah ibn Umar told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: A believer eats with one intestine, and a disbeliever eats with seven intestines. (Bukhari 5394, Muslim 1631)"
25035,"(25035) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: He said: A believer eats with one intestine, and a disbeliever eats with seven intestines. (Muslim 1431. Ahmad 3/333)"
25036,"(25036) Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Amr, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: He said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: A believer eats with one intestine, and a disbeliever eats with seven intestines.
(Tirmidhi 1819. Ahmad 2/435)"
25037,"(25037) Waki’ told us, he said: Al-Amash told us, he said: I think Abu Khalid Al-Walbiy mentioned it on the authority of Maymunah, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The unbeliever eats with seven intestines, and the believer eats with one intestine.
(Ahmad 6/335. Tabarani 13)"
25038,"(25038) Zayd bin Al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Musa bin Ubaidah, he said: Ubaid Al-Aghar narrated to me, on the authority of Ata bin Yasar, On the authority of Jajaja Al-Ghafari, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The infidel eats from seven intestines. The believer eats with one person. (Tabarani 2152)"
25039,"(25039) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: He said: The food of one is sufficient for two, and the food of two is sufficient for four. (Muslim 181, Tirmidhi 1820)"
25040,"(25040) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khalid, on the authority of his father, who said: I entered upon a man while he was eating dates. And he frothed up milk, so he said: Come on and call it, for the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to call them the best ones. (Ahmad 3/474)"
25041,"(25041) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of his father, who said: I entered upon Ali on the day of Chat, and... He had a drink in his hand, so he gave it to me and said: Drink. I said: What is it? He said: A third of honey, a third of ghee, and a third of milk. I said: I do not want it. He said: If you drank it, you would still be warm and full. All your day."
25042,"(25042) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Ala’ bin Al-Musayyab, who said: I saw Ibrahim and Khaythamiah. They eat it with honey."
25043,"(25043) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, saying: Ibrahim bin Saad narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Jafar, He said: I saw the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, eating dates with cucumbers."
25044,"(25044) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to eat watermelon with fresh dates.
(Tirmidhi 2000, Ahmad 3/142)"
25045,"(25045) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Khalda, he said: We came to Ibn Sirin, and he said: I do not know what to feed you. There is a man among you who stayed in his house, then brought out a food for us and began to feed us."
25046,"(25046) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: The monkey is not one of the livestock."
25047,"(25047) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Hassan, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid; He hated the hedgehog."
25048,"(25048) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father; He did not see any harm in eating hair."
25049,"(25049) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Abu Yafour, on the authority of Ibn Abi Awfa, who said: I fought with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May the peace and blessings of God be upon him: Seven battles: We eat locusts. (Muslim 1546. Tirmidhi 1821)"
25050,"(25050) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Shabib, on the authority of Jundub, a man from among them, who asked Ibn Abbas about eating locusts? He said: There is no harm in it."
